PVD("nepal_ndp_2025-2029",{"docs":["","Nepal NDP 2024 28"],"s":{"2":[[1,"158","2","Multi-level Government Coordination and Joint Planning Framework","Delineate the roles, responsibilities and scope of federal, provincial and local levels of government, and through their coordination, collaboration and partnership, formulate targeted plans and programs and increase capacity for implementation.",""],[1,"170","1","Revision of Work Jurisdiction under Federalism","the responsibilities of three levels of government require to be further clarified through comprehensive revision of work jurisdiction.",""],[1,"170","1","Legal Provisions for Common Rights Use","Similarly, legal provisions are needed for use of common rights, including other laws.",""],[1,"170","1","Coordination and Collaboration for Provincial and Local Economic Development","Balanced development and consolidation of the provincial and local economy through coordination and collaboration of the federal government leads to development and prosperity of the whole nation.",""],[1,"170","1","Intergovernmental Coordination for Balanced Development","Making provincial and local economies dynamic and consolidated for balanced development requires stronger coordination, mutual understanding and collaboration among the three levels of government.",""],[1,"172","2","Clarification of Fiscal Federalism and Economic Responsibilities","Effectively implement the economic responsibilities assigned to the provinces and local levels by the Constitution of Nepal.",""],[1,"173","5","Coordination for SDG Implementation Across Government Levels","Achieve the sustainable development goals through efforts of all three levels.",""],[1,"173","5","Balanced Regional Development and Resource Distribution Framework","Ensure balanced development of all sectors of the country through just distribution of resources and planned development.",""],[1,"173","5","Federal-Provincial-Local Coordination Culture Initiative","Develop a culture of coordination, cooperation and cooperative work at the federal, provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"174","3","Implementation of the Unbundling Report","Review and implement the unbundling report to maintain clarity of constitutional rights and responsibilities.",""],[1,"174","3","Intergovernmental Coordination Agency Activation","Activate inter-governmental coordination agencies and implement relevant decisions through institutionlized collaboration.",""],[1,"205","2","Federal Governance Coordination and Good Governance Strengthening","It is indispensable to strengthen the rights, obligations and duties, work responsibilities and effective coordination among the governments at different levels in a federal governance system.",""],[1,"205","2","Equal and Easy Access to Public Services","It is the responsibility of the state to guarantee good governance by ensuring equal and easy access of the people to services and facilities provided by the state.",""],[1,"206","3","Inter-Provincial Council for Federal Coordination","an inter- provincial council has been established under chairmanship of the Prime Minister, consisting of the Minister of Home Affairs, the Minister of Finance and the Chief Minister of the respective provinces.",""],[1,"206","3","Federation, Province and Local Level Coordination and Interrelation Act","For functional coordination between the three levels of government, the Federation, Province and Local Level (Coordination and Interrelation) Act, 2020 has been enacted and implemented.",""],[1,"206","3","National Coordination Council Meetings","The meeting of the National Coordination Council chaired by the Prime Minister has been held regularly and coordination and facilitation has been done between the three levels of government.",""],[1,"207","2","Intergovernmental Coordination and Legal Governance Reform","In accordance with singular and concurrent rights conferred by the constitution to the three levels of government, carry out work description, and through formulation and enforcement of necessary laws, maintain levelwise coordination among the three governments.",""],[1,"207","2","Equitable State Resource Allocation for Inclusion","Distribute the resources of the state on an objective and fair basis in accordance with values and recognized principles of inclusion to make sure that the target groups get access to political, economic, administrative, social, educational, and private sector domains.",""],[1,"208","3","Administrative Federalism Institutional Development","Make necessary legal arrangements for operation and management of federal, provincial and local government services.",""],[1,"208","4","Multi-Actor Governance Strengthening Initiative","Enhance the role of public, private, cooperative, community and non-governmental organizations to achieve the goals of sustainable development.",""],[1,"208","4","Governance Body Capacity-Building Initiative","Take adequate initiatives towards capacity-building of governance bodies.",""],[1,"208","4","Institutional Good Governance Maintenance in Financial and Community Sectors","Maintain institutional good governance in the financial (banking, microfinance, cooperative sector), private, non-governmental and community sectors.",""],[1,"208","6","Subnational Security Policy and Programme Formulation","The federation, provinces and local levels should formulate policies and programs related to social",""],[1,"211","2","Human Rights Coordination and Collaboration Mechanism","Enhance coordination and collaboration between the concerned constitutional commissions and government agencies, parliament and judiciary for the promotion and protection of human rights.",""],[1,"211","3","Regulatory Capacity Strengthening and Coordination Reform","Improve the regulatory capacity of the state by ensuring coordination between all three levels of government in order to structurally improve the existing regulatory framework.",""]],"3":[[1,"39","4","Public Investment Project Selection and Management Reform","Make the highest rate of return as a base for selection after cost-benefit analysis while developing and selecting projects.",""],[1,"42","6","Integrated Project Bank and Project Management Reform","Establish and operate an integrated project bank.",""],[1,"53","5","Public Expenditure Reform Program","Through reform programs to be launched in public expenditure, efficiency of federal, provincial and local levels in public spending will be substantially enhanced.",""],[1,"60","1","Public Expenditure Efficiency and Domestic Resource Mobilization","In the plan period, allocational eficiency and productivity of public expenditure will be maintained in all three tires of the government for creating employment opportunities and raising equitable production and productivity through mobilization of domestic resources,",""]],"4":[[1,"103","7","Population Education Mainstreaming Initiative","Internalize and mainstream population education in all subject sectors and levels to manage demographic transition and migration in the development process.",""],[1,"103","7","Population Management Concept Adoption","Adopt the latest concept of population management in order to derive benefits from demographic dividend.",""],[1,"111","4","Population Policy Revision and Birth Rate Incentive Reform","Revise the existing population policy and encourage an increase in the birth rate.",""]],"5":[[1,"234","5","SDG Implementation Capacity and Results-Based Monitoring Strengthening","Improve investment and build capacity for implementation of SDGs and results-based monitoring.",""],[1,"235","1","SDG Partnership and Collaboration Strengthening","enhance cooperation, coordination and collaboration among the government, private sector, cooperatives, development partners, civil society and the people at large, as well as strengthen global partnership programs.",""],[1,"235","1","Private Sector Mobilization for SDG Delivery","Effectively mobilize the private sector through improvement of investment climate and financial incentives for achievement of SDGs.",""],[1,"235","2","SDG Disaggregated Data and Progress Monitoring System","Generate necessary disaggregated data related to the Sustainable Development Goals, develop an overall data system and monitor progress.",""],[1,"237","6","Regular SDG Monitoring and Evaluation System","Conduct regular monitoring of progress based on action plan on the Sustainable Development Goals indicators.",""],[1,"237","6","National SDG Data Portal Implementation","Ensure effective implementation of the national data portal for regular monitoring of the progress made by the federation, provinces and local levels towards achievement of SDGs.",""],[1,"237","6","SDG Achievement Evaluation and Feedback Mechanism","Conduct achievement evaluation on the basis of integrated report, provide feedback for effective implementation in case of indicators with low progress.",""],[1,"237","6","Voluntary SDG Review by Subnational Governments","Encourage a voluntary review of the progress made by the provinces and local levels in SDGs achievement.",""],[1,"240","4","Coordination and Partnership Program for SDG Implementation","11) Coordination and partnership program: Promote cooperation of the federation, provinces and local levels in the formulation and implementation of sustainability- friendly local periodic plans.",""],[1,"240","4","Multi-Stakeholder Mobilization for SDG Achievement","Mobilize the public, private sector, cooperatives, community organizations and non-governmental organizations towards achievement of SDGs.",""],[1,"240","4","Capacity Strengthening for Nepali Missions Abroad","Enhance the institutional capacity of Nepali missions abroad and other related bodies to obtain support in accordance with the commitments made by development partners and to increase access to the financial and technical funds to achieve SDGs.",""],[1,"240","4","Diplomatic Initiatives for Sustainable Development","Take diplomatic initiatives focused on sustainable development.",""]],"6":[[1,"4","4","Effective Implementation of Periodic Plans","effective implementation of periodic plans remains critical.",""],[1,"4","4","Three-Level Government Participation Mechanism","active and meaningful participation of all three levels of government is necessary.",""],[1,"5","2","Sixteenth Plan Implementation","call upon all stakeholders to join hands in successfully implementing the plan.",""],[1,"6","6","Transformative Measures and Key Programs","Transformative measures and key programs that can address the structural impediments seen in various sectors and dimensions of development have been included.",""],[1,"24","8","Multi-Level and Multi-Stakeholder Coordination for Sustainable Development Implementation","Strengthen inter-relations and work capacity among federal, provincial and local levels as well as government, private, cooperative, non-governmental sectors and development partners to implement sustainable development plans and programs.",""],[1,"24","10","Evidence-Based Policy and Development Programming","Implement policies and development programs based on study, research and scientific evidence.",""],[1,"208","5","Result-Oriented Monitoring and Evaluation System","Establish result-oriented monitoring and evaluation system through adequate financial resource mobilization, human resource mobilization and policy facilitation.",""],[1,"208","5","Project Management System Improvement","Improve project management system based on monitoring results.",""],[1,"208","5","Project Head Performance Linkage","Link progress of the project to the performance of the project head.",""],[1,"208","5","Timely Project Completion Requirement","Complete the project within specified time for securing results.",""],[1,"210","6","Effective Monitoring and Evaluation System Development","Establish legal system to determine clear accountability of public officials.",""],[1,"211","1","Integrated Project Management Information System","Develop an integrated project management information system at the federal, provincial and local levels to improve the methods and processes of all stages of planning (identification of problems, selection of options for solutions, implementation, monitoring and evaluation and feedback).",""],[1,"211","1","Project Human Resource Stability Measures","Maintain stability of skilled human resources in the project.",""],[1,"211","1","Prior Project Preparation for Budget Allocation","Undertake prior project preparation tasks while selecting projects and allocating budget.",""],[1,"214","4","Effective Monitoring and Evaluation System Development Program","Effective monitoring and evaluation system development program: Conduct joint monitoring and evaluation of projects and programs through levelwise and agencywise coordination as provisioned by the constitution.",""],[1,"214","5","Project Management Reform Program","11) Project management reform program: Establish smart coordination among stakeholders related to implementation.",""]],"9":[[1,"211","3","Legal and Institutional Reform of the Regulatory Regime","Reform the legal, organizational and appointment systems for structural strengthening of the existing regulatory regime.",""],[1,"211","3","Public Accountability Review for Regulatory Officials","Make arrangements for public accountability examination of officials working for regulatory bodies.",""],[1,"215","2","Effective Regulation Program","Effective regulation program: Strengthen the structural system of inspection and supervision for quality of public service delivery and management reforms.",""],[1,"215","5","Cooperative Sector Transparency and Regulation Program","Program for strengthening the cooperative sector: Adopt a system for the cooperative organizations to operate transparently according to the purpose, principle and concept of the cooperatives and to focus on production and employment.",""],[1,"215","5","Second-Tier Cooperative Regulation and Monitoring Mechanism","Establish a separate second tier mechanism for effective regulation and monitoring of the cooperative sector.",""]],"10":[[1,"174","2","Disaggregated Data Production and Use System","For consolidation of policy and planning system, produce, process, analyze and use necessary disagregated data.",""],[1,"174","2","Integrated Reporting System for Data Exchange","Develop integrated reporting system for exchange and use of data and information.",""],[1,"174","2","Local-Level Monitoring and Evaluation System","Develop and implement effective monitoring and evaluation system to make local level project management effective.",""],[1,"178","2","Integrated Data and Monitoring and Evaluation System","Develop integrated data and monitoring and evaluation system: Develop and make use of integrated data system in coordination and cooperation of provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"180","3","Data System and Monitoring and Evaluation Promotion Program","Data system and monitoring and evaluation promotion program: Establish and operationalize statistical units at provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"207","2","Integrated Government Data System","Establish and operate an inter-linked and integrated data system among all agencies working at the three levels for better public service and development management as well as maintenance of peace, order and security.",""],[1,"209","4","Integrated Government Data System Development and Expansion","Develop and expand integrated data system for formulating policy and plans based on facts and connect it to the electronic system.",""],[1,"212","4","Integrated National Data System Development and Strengthening Program","Develop an integrated national data system to make policy and planning effectively based on facts and evidence.",""],[1,"212","5","Invisible Economy Data Collection and Integration Initiative","Collect fact-based information related to the invisible economy and other topical issues and enhance effectiveness in policy, planning and implementation of related sectors.",""],[1,"212","5","Federated Data Integration System","Establish and include data scattered in various agencies of the federation, provinces and",""],[1,"213","1","Integrated Local-Level Management Information System","local level by setting up an integrated management information system.",""]],"11":[[1,"101","4","Athlete Training and Competition Skills Development","Adopt new skills and techniques in training and tournaments to produce competitive athletes for national and international levels.",""],[1,"107","2","Sports Infrastructure Development and Athlete Training Programme","Provide training along with construction and upgrading of sports infrastructure.",""],[1,"107","2","Sports Talent Identification and Competition Development Initiative","Identify and develop talented athletes by conducting sports competitions from local and basic levels.",""],[1,"107","2","Physical Education Curriculum and Staffing Reform","Include physical education in compulsory curriculum and ensure minimum human resources for it.",""],[1,"115","3","School Sports Integration Programme","Develop education system by connecting early learning with sports.",""],[1,"115","4","Balanced Sports Infrastructure Development and Training Programme","To develop sports infrastructure in a balanced manner, develop one sports village each in every local level and make arrangements for sports training.",""],[1,"115","4","Provincial Sports Complex and Tournament Programme","Develop at least one well-equipped sports complex in all provincial levels and hold district, provincial and national level tournaments in them.",""],[1,"115","4","Elite Athlete Training and Support Measures","Provide training opportunities on a par with international standard for capable sportspersons.",""],[1,"115","4","Athlete Self-Reliance Support Package","For promotion of self-reliance among sportspersons, make arrangements for concessional loans, insurance, employment in organized sector and operation of business.",""],[1,"115","4","Sports Museum Construction","Construct sports museum.",""],[1,"115","4","Sports University Establishment and Operation","Establish and run sports university.",""],[1,"115","5","Sports Training Centers in the Himalayan Region","Establish at least two sports training centers in the Himalayan region to impart relevant training for participation in international tournaments.",""],[1,"115","6","Completion of National Pride Sports Stadium Projects","Complete construction of Biratnagar, Moolpani and Bharatpur stadiums, which have been declared projects of national pride.",""],[1,"117","12","Province-Level Stadium Construction Programme","Construction of province level stadiums with international standard facilities",""],[1,"117","13","International-Standard Cricket Stadium Construction","Construction of cricket stadium with international standard facilities",""],[1,"117","14","Local Level Playground and Semi-Covered Hall Construction","Construction of local level playgrounds with semi-covered halls",""]],"12":[[1,"34","2","Domestic Savings Mobilization and Capital Formation Initiative","Increasing savings by discouraging unnecessary consumption expenditure to accomulate resources needed for capital formation.",""],[1,"34","2","Productive Investment of Domestic Savings","Investing domestic and national savings in productive sectorto boost cpital formation.",""],[1,"34","2","Private Sector and Household Savings Mobilization","Mobilizing the savings of the private sector and households and facilitating capital formation by creating enable environment for foreign investment.",""],[1,"38","3","Financial Sector Regulation and Productive Credit Mobilization","Review and implement existing policies to ensure that financial resources flow to the productive sector.",""],[1,"38","3","Financial Services Expansion for Entrepreneurship and Innovation","Develop financial services to encourage entrepreneurship and innovation.",""],[1,"38","3","Nationwide Expansion of Bank and Financial Institution Branches","Encourage the expansion of branches of banks and financial institutions to ensure financial access to citizens living in all areas of the country.",""],[1,"38","3","Monetary and Fiscal Policy Coordination for Macroeconomic Stability","Align monetary policy with fiscal and other economic policies to achieve macroeconomic stability and use policy tools to support economic growth and distributive justice.",""],[1,"38","3","Mobilization of Social Security Funds for Production and Infrastructure","Mobilize resources of the financial institutions related to social security for production and infrastructure development as an additional measure.",""],[1,"43","1","Productive Use of Financial Instruments Programme","Programmes based on productive use of financial instruments: Encourage the flow of financial resources to the productive sector.",""],[1,"43","1","Financial Sector Stability and Transparency Measures","Increase stability and transparency in the financial sector.",""],[1,"43","1","Expansion of Financial Services and Access","Expand financial services and enhance financial access at all local levels.",""],[1,"93","1","Access to Finance and Financial Literacy Expansion","Increase access to finance and financial literacy.",""]],"13":[[1,"197","5","Single-Window Foreign Grants and Assistance System","Establish a single-window system for receiving foreign grants and assistance;",""],[1,"197","5","Aid Alignment and Treasury Integration Reform","Align international development assistance within the national budget system and government treasury and enhance the disbursement capacity;",""],[1,"197","5","Priority-Sector Development Assistance Mobilization","mobilize development assistance in productive and national priority sectors through needs identification and balanced development;",""],[1,"197","5","International Finance Tools for Climate and Green Economy","deploy new tools for international finance on areas such as climate change and building a green economy;",""],[1,"197","5","Alternative International Finance Capacity Development","Develop institutional capacity to mobilize competitive alternative international finance to build transformative large-scale infrastructure when Nepal graduates into a developing country.",""],[1,"199","2","Development Assistance Mobilization for Ready-to-Go High-Return Projects","Mobilize development assistance for ready to go and high-return projects and programs; mobilizing new international financial instruments such as green bonds; issue local currency-denominated bonds; enhance the capacity of responsible bodies and human resources to mobilize climate-related finance; enhance the utilization and absorption capacity of development aid prioritizing project-specific development assistance.",""],[1,"199","2","Green Bond and Local Currency Bond Issuance","mobilizing new international financial instruments such as green bonds; issue local currency-denominated bonds; enhance the capacity of responsible bodies and human resources to mobilize climate-related finance; enhance the utilization and absorption capacity of development aid prioritizing project-specific development assistance.",""],[1,"199","2","Climate Finance Mobilization Capacity Strengthening","enhance the capacity of responsible bodies and human resources to mobilize climate-related finance; enhance the utilization and absorption capacity of development aid prioritizing project-specific development assistance.",""],[1,"201","7","Project-Specific Development Bond Issuance Program","Project-Specific Development Bond Issuance Program: Raise investment through project-specific development bonds for special projects.",""],[1,"202","3","International Finance Mobilization Enhancement Program","(13) Effectiveness of International Finance Mobilization Enhancement Program: Prioritize the mobilization of development assistance based on policies and programs; introduce new international finance instruments such as green bonds, climate-resilient bonds, blended finance, and bonds issued in local currencies; enhance the effectiveness of hedging systems to reduce exchange rate and interest rate risks when mobilizing international finance; improve processes and increase expenditure capacity to enhance the effectiveness of foreign aid; base the selection of projects to be operated through foreign aid on development needs, potential outcomes, and balanced development.",""]],"14":[[1,"33","4","Fertile Land Utilization Measures","Preventing the tendency to leave fertile land barren.",""],[1,"33","4","Middlemen Elimination in Agricultural Markets","Abolish the existing system of middlemen between production and the market, which creates obstacles for real producers to benefit.",""],[1,"37","1","Agricultural Land Consolidation and Cooperative Farming Support","Consolidate and control fragmentation of fertile arable land to strengthen the primary sector under the real sector.",""],[1,"37","1","Youth and Returnee Cooperative Farming Promotion","Create an environment that increases the morale of youth and manpower returning from foreign employment to promote collective and cooperative farming on barren land and public land.",""],[1,"37","1","Timely Supply of Hybrid Seeds and Fertilizers","Ensure a system of timely supply of hybrid seeds and fertilizers.",""],[1,"37","1","Agricultural Credit and Insurance Services","Provide agricultural credit and insurance services to real farmers.",""],[1,"37","1","Production-Based Agricultural Subsidies","Provision of production-based subsidies.",""],[1,"37","1","Forest Product Utilization Regulatory Simplification","Scientific management of forests by simplifying legal and procedural rules for the utilization of forest-based products.",""],[1,"37","1","Storage and Market Infrastructure Development","Proper arrangement of storage facilities and markets.",""],[1,"37","1","Local Raw Material Based Industrial Development","Establishment and operation of industries based on local raw materials for development and expansion of the secondary sector.",""],[1,"37","1","Micro, Small, and Cottage Industry Promotion","Promotion of micro, small, and cottage industries.",""],[1,"37","1","Hydropower Generation and Transmission Expansion","Increase hydropower generation and expand transmission lines.",""],[1,"37","1","Local Industry Construction Materials Production","Produce building materials for public and private construction in collaboration with local industries.",""],[1,"37","1","Local Labor Mobilization Initiative","Emphasize the mobilization of local labor.",""],[1,"37","1","Tourism and Knowledge Sector Promotion","Promote tourism, information technology, professional, scientific, and technical activities, and other areas with comparative advantages in the tertiary sector with priority.",""],[1,"37","1","Labor and Enterprise-Friendly Entrepreneurship Promotion","Promote labor and enterprise-friendly culture to enhance entrepreneurship by maintaining interlinkages between rural and urban economies.",""],[1,"37","1","Sectoral Interlinkage Promotion","Maintain sectoral interlinkages by creating an environment where goods and services produced by one economic sector are used as raw materials or supporting inputs by other sectors.",""],[1,"37","1","Green Economy Mainstreaming Across Economic Sectors","Apply the concept of green economy in all economic sectors to strike a balance in the environment and adapt to climate change.",""],[1,"39","2","Market and Supply Information System","Develop a market and supply information system and intensify market monitoring in collaboration with the provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"42","2","One Local Level, One Specific Production Campaign","Commercialize and diversify agriculture through a 'one local level, one specific production' campaign.",""],[1,"69","1","Agricultural Productivity and Competitiveness Enhancement Programme","Increase production and productivity of agriculture by ensuring easier availability of means of production and agricultural infrastructure (including roads, energy and irrigation), technology and inputs, and effective mobilization.",""],[1,"69","1","Agricultural Market and Post-Harvest Infrastructure Expansion","Expand transportation services, collection centers, chilling centers, warehouses and processing centers which are necessary for transportation, storage, processing and marketing of agricultural produce.",""],[1,"69","1","Agricultural Research and Innovation Support","Ensure that necessary resources, technology, human resources, etc. are available for study, research and innovation in the agricultural sector.",""],[1,"69","1","Minimum Support Price Implementation Reform","Make implementation of minimum support price fixed for agricultural produce effective.",""],[1,"69","1","Youth Engagement in Agriculture Initiative","Increase the attraction of skilled and educated youths in agriculture.",""],[1,"69","1","Agricultural Credit, Insurance, and Subsidy Support","Ensure easy credit and insurance facilities in agriculture by making subsidies and concessions based on production.",""],[1,"70","5","Agricultural Infrastructure, Mechanization, and Commercialization Support","Identify special production areas and increase agricultural infrastructure, mechanization, diversification and commercialization of agriculture.",""],[1,"70","5","Agricultural Transport, Storage, and Processing Services","Add value to agricultural produce through provision of systematic and modern transportation, storage and processing services.",""],[1,"73","6","Agricultural Production and Productivity Enhancement Program","Agricultural production and productivity enhancement program through proper land utilization:",""],[1,"74","1","Local Agricultural Infrastructure and Service Support Program","At the local level, develop agricultural infrastructure, expand and operate them through public- private-cooperative cooperation.",""],[1,"74","1","Agricultural Input and Technology Access Support","Ensure availability of hybrid genomes, seeds, stocks and fertilizers.",""],[1,"74","1","Farmer Access to Agricultural Inputs and Skills Program","Establish farmers' access to agricultural inputs, tools, equipment, technology, knowledge and skills through various stakeholder agencies.",""],[1,"74","1","Agricultural Research and Extension Linkage Mechanism","Build a mechanism to maintain inter-linkages between agricultural research, education and extension.",""],[1,"74","1","Minimum Support Price and Agricultural Marketing System","Ensure the purchase of products by fixing minimum support price of basic agricultural produce within the date set by maintaining a calendar.",""],[1,"74","1","Private Sector Agricultural Value Chain Partnership","Collaborate with the private sector for purchase, storage, quality monitoring, branding and export of agricultural produce, which is helpful in stabilizing the price of agricultural produce in the market, encourage and promote contract farming and land consolidation by formulating necessary laws.",""],[1,"74","1","Production-Based Grants Institutional Development","Ensure institutional development of production-based grants system.",""],[1,"74","1","Market-Oriented Agricultural Production System","Develop a market-oriented production system and link it to the product and the market.",""],[1,"74","1","Indigenous Products Departmental Stores","Operate departmental stores that deal with indigenous products.",""],[1,"74","1","Agricultural Marketing and Cost Reduction Initiative","Emphasize on agricultural produce marketing and cost reduction.",""],[1,"74","1","Local Street Market Promotion","Promote local street market, make arrangements for both grants and loans in agriculture, simplify procedure in credit, banking and insurance for increased access of farmers.",""],[1,"74","1","Skills- and Project-Based Agricultural Lending","Make arrangements to extend loans on the basis of skills, educational qualification and the project itself.",""],[1,"74","1","Agri-Technology Promotion for Entrepreneurship and Employment","Promote latest agri-technologies for entrepreneurship development and employment creation in order to raise attractiveness of the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"74","1","Subsidized Electricity for Farmers","Provide power at subsidized rates to farmers.",""],[1,"74","1","Agricultural Extension Service Capacity Upgrade","For delivery of agriculture extension service, make arrangement for minimum requirements such as physical structure, infrastructure and technical human resources.",""],[1,"74","3","Agricultural Modernization and Commercialization Program Restructuring","Agricultural modernization and commercialization program: Restructure agricultural programs which are in operation at present and run them in a new",""],[1,"75","1","Domestic Agricultural Product Market Expansion","Increase consumption of domestic products to ensure market for agricultural products.",""],[1,"75","1","Fresh Vegetable and Fruit Export Program","Launch program to export fresh vegetables and fruit to the Gulf countries.",""],[1,"75","1","Agro-processing Industry Facilitation","Facilitate the establishment of industries for processing of agricultural products and those that use agricultural produce as raw materials.",""],[1,"75","1","Provincial Agro-industrial Park Development","Establish agro- industrial parks in all seven provinces.",""],[1,"75","3","Seeds and Plant Stocks Development Program","Program for development of seeds and plant stocks, fertilizers and agricultural tools: Develop and produce seeds in collaboration with the private sector.",""],[1,"75","3","Agricultural Human Resource Management and Skills Enhancement","Management of agricultural human resources and skill enhancement.",""],[1,"75","3","Specialist Agricultural Services Support Program","Support for development of specialist human resource and easy availability of agricultural technical services.",""],[1,"75","3","Large Commercial Farm Operations","Operation of large commercial farms.",""],[1,"75","3","Agricultural Implements Supply Program","Supply of agricultural implements through domestic production and imports.",""],[1,"75","3","Veterinary Vaccine and Medicine Supply","Ensure supply of vaccines and medicines.",""]],"15":[[1,"123","4","Year-Round Irrigation Expansion Through Reservoir Dams and Water Diversion","The Irrigation Policy, 2024 has emphasized on expanding irrigation facilities round the year by developing multi-purpose reservoir dams and inter-watershed water diversion projects and ensuring their effective management.",""],[1,"123","5","Large-Scale Irrigation Project Development and System Restoration","According to the irrigation master plan, the irrigated agricultural area is expanding through gradual development of large and comprehensive irrigation projects, restoration and maintenance of irrigation system and development of irrigation system based on new technology.",""],[1,"123","5","River Basin Plan and Diversion Project Construction","The river basin plan is being developed and the construction of river basin diversion projects is underway with the goal of providing irrigation facilities round the year.",""],[1,"127","1","Year-Round Irrigation Facility Expansion","Provide yearlong irrigation facility in arable land.",""],[1,"127","1","Maintenance of Existing Irrigation Infrastructure","Carry out regular maintenance of existing irrigation structures.",""],[1,"127","3","Year-Round Irrigation Facilities for Arable Land","Provide necessary irrigation facilities to arable land throughout the year.",""],[1,"127","3","Agriculture and Irrigation Investment Return Optimization","Accrue expected returns from investment in agriculture and irrigation.",""],[1,"127","3","Timely and Cost-Controlled Irrigation Project Delivery","Carry out irrigation projects within timeframe and estimated cost.",""],[1,"130","3","Cluster-Based Tubewell and Lift Irrigation Expansion","Sink shallow and deep tubewells on the basis of clusters in arable land of Terai-Madhesh region; use lift irrigation on plateaus by the side of rivers; build water collection ponds and small and medium reservoirs in other terrains to utilize latest mechanical technology.",""],[1,"131","6","Irrigation Infrastructure Construction, Expansion and Upgrading","Carry out study and construct and upgrade irrigation systems identified by the Irrigation Masterplan.",""],[1,"131","6","Surface, Tubewell and Lift Irrigation Projects","For expansion of irrigated land, run surface, tubewell and lift irrigation projects as part of the transformative program.",""],[1,"133","6","Integrated River Basin-Based Irrigation and Water Resources Management Program","Integrated river basin-based irrigation and water resources management program: Depending on the nature of basin, provide irrigation facilities in all irrigable agricultural land of the country.",""],[1,"133","7","Water Resource Conservation and Management Program","Water resource conservation and management program: Construct water storage ponds in marginalized arable areas where there is no possibility of irrigation from traditional water sources and expand irrigation facilities through other alternative means,",""],[1,"134","1","Hilly Region Irrigation and Water Storage Projects","Carry out projects related to water storage ponds, lift irrigation and utilization of underground water sources in the hilly regions; recharge underground water resources in Chure-Bhawar and other potential areas, and implement Chure conservation work with priority.",""],[1,"136","2","Irrigation Infrastructure Development Program","Irrigation infrastructure development program: As identified by the Irrigation Master Plan, launch surface irrigation, tubewell irrigation and lift irrigation with priority.",""]],"16":[[1,"221","2","Climate Change Policy and Adaptation Framework Implementation","To enhance climate resilience, National Climate Change Policy, 2019, Environmental Protection Act, 2019 and Regulations, 2018, National Framework on Local Adaptation Plans of Action, 2019, Climate Resilience Plans and Budget Guidelines, 2020 and Gender and Social Inclusion Strategy and Action Plan for Climate Change ( 2020 - 2030) have been formulated and put into implementation.",""],[1,"221","2","National Adaptation Plan and NDC Reporting Implementation","Cost estimates of the Second Nationally Determined Contribution reporting requirement and implementation of the National Adaptation Plan have been prepared.",""],[1,"221","2","Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Programme Implementation","Strategic priorities and sectoral targets for climate change mitigation and adaptation programs are being implemented.",""],[1,"221","3","Climate Indicators in National and Provincial Budgets","Since F.Y. 2011/12, climate indicators have been put into practice in the national budget and this has now been extended down to the provincial level.",""],[1,"221","3","Provincial Climate Change Strategies and Action Plans","Provincial level climate change strategies and action plans have been prepared, while around 263 local adaptation plans are being implemented at the local level.",""],[1,"221","3","Green Climate Fund Assistance Agreement","Aiming at mitigation and adaptation, an agreement has been reached for assistance worth US $ 87 million from the Green Climate Fund, while three indigenous organizations have been recognized for receiving financial support from the Green Climate Fund.",""],[1,"221","3","World Bank Carbon Trade Agreement","Similarly, an agreement has been signed with the World Bank for carbon trade worth US $ 45 million.",""],[1,"222","1","Thematic Environmental Policy Reform","Undertake thematic policy reforms to make laws biodiversity friendly, climate change adaptive and green economy or green enterprise friendly.",""],[1,"222","1","Multi-level Environmental Coordination Mechanism","Since the environment and climate change are interrelated issues, establish effective mechanisms at all three levels of government for coordination.",""],[1,"222","1","Climate Mitigation and Adaptation Capacity Expansion","Expand capacity for mitigation and adaptation to climate change, increase access to established international climate finance as well as establish reliable and up-to-date data systems for mobilizing cooperation.",""],[1,"222","1","Climate Project Preparation and Institutional Capacity Development","Develop human resources capable of preparing and implementing projects and enhancing the institutional capacity of all three levels of government.",""],[1,"222","1","NDC and NAP Implementation and Monitoring Arrangements","Ensure effective implementation, monitoring and inter-agency coordination of Nationally Determined Contribution and National Adaptation Plan.",""],[1,"222","2","Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Promotion","Climate change mitigation and adaptation promotion: Increase knowledge and public awareness of adverse impacts of climate change on water resources, health, tourism, energy, forestry, biodiversity and infrastructure sectors.",""],[1,"222","3","International Climate Advocacy and Leadership Initiative","Nepal, therefore, should effectively raise its voice on climate change concerns in international forums.",""],[1,"222","4","Localization of Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Action Plans","Localize climate change mitigation and adaptation national implementation action plans as well as Sustainable Development Goals.",""],[1,"222","4","Local Adaptation Planning","Prepare and implement local adaptation plans.",""],[1,"222","4","Local Environmental and Climate Data System","Establish a system of local level forest, environment, biological diversity and climate-related data collection.",""],[1,"222","4","Community Adaptation Capacity Building","Increase adaptation capability of local communities.",""],[1,"223","4","Climate-Sensitive Investment Mainstreaming","Make household, private and public investments environmentally friendly and climate sensitive to promote climate sensitivity.",""],[1,"223","4","Adaptive Capacity Support for Vulnerable Communities","Enhance adaptive capacity of vulnerable communities.",""],[1,"223","4","Local Adaptation Plan Expansion","Mainstream climate resilience in the development process by extending the local adaptation plan to all provinces and local levels as well as the community level.",""],[1,"223","4","Nature-Based Adaptation and Low-Carbon Technology Incentives","Promote the use of traditional knowledge, technology and local products, including nature-based solutions, ecosystem-based adaptation, and provide incentives in the adoption of technologies to reduce carbon emissions.",""],[1,"223","5","International Climate Change Forum and Negotiation Capacity Building","Regularly organize an international forum on climate change in Nepal. Ensure capacity-building of Nepal's negotiating team.",""],[1,"225","1","Climate Finance Mobilization for Green Resilient and Inclusive Development","Increase access to climate finance, using green bonds.",""],[1,"225","1","Climate Finance Fund Establishment","Establish a climate finance fund.",""],[1,"225","1","Climate Governance Coordination and Institutional Activation","Determine the areas of cooperation, respective roles and bases for investment between the three levels of government, private sector and development partners.",""],[1,"225","2","Localization of Environmental Protection and Climate Change Issues","Localize environmental protection and climate change issues.",""],[1,"225","2","Strengthening Local-Level Environmental Governance","Make the local level competent and responsible.",""],[1,"225","2","Mainstreaming Environment and Climate Change Across Policies and Budgets","Mainstream environment and climate change issues in policies, plans, budgets and programs of all levels and sectors.",""],[1,"225","5","Green Economy Promotion Program","Green economy promotion program: Encourage banks and financial institutions to invest in green projects.",""],[1,"226","1","Local Climate Risk Reduction Infrastructure","Build risk reduction infrastructure at local levels that are most vulnerable to climate change and promote climate-friendly agriculture and indigenous crops.",""],[1,"226","2","Special Programs for Directly Affected Communities","Conduct special programs targeting directly affected communities including women.",""],[1,"227","2","Climate Risks and Loss and Damage Reduction Program","Climate risks and loss and damage reduction program: Update infrastructure standards based on future climate projections.",""],[1,"227","3","Local Adaptability Promotion Program","6) Local adaptability promotion program: Build capacity of all local levels to prepare and implement adaptation plans.",""],[1,"227","4","International Climate Finance Access Program","Program to increase access to international climate finance: Develop institutional capacity to mitigate carbon emissions, to enhance climate adaptability and to lay a claim for investment over loss and damage caused by climate change through international climate finance mechanism.",""],[1,"227","4","Climate Diplomacy and International Advocacy Initiative","Mobilize climate diplomacy to establish the agenda of landlocked mountainous developing countries with high risks and vulnerability in the international policy-making process on climate change.",""],[1,"227","4","Sagarmatha Sambad Climate Awareness Program","Lauch 'Sagarmatha Sambad' program with a view to raise sensitivity about climate risks and",""],[1,"228","11","Green Climate Bond Issuance","Issuance of green climate bonds",""],[1,"241","1","Restructuring of Challenge, Mixed, Green, and Climate Funds","Restructure challenge funds, mixed funds, green bonds, climate change funds, green environment facility, non-resident Nepalese investment, foreign direct investment and private investments in the interest of Nepal.",""],[1,"241","1","Climate Finance Mobilization and Access Preparation","Mobilize resources from the Global Climate Fund, Adaptation Fund, Global Environment Facility and other multilateral, regional and bilateral funds in all areas related to climate change, and make special preparations to secure easy and meaningful access to such funds.",""]],"17":[[1,"223","1","Endangered Species Conservation and Habitat Protection","To make conservation of endangered wildlife and plants on the verge of extinction effective, improve protection of wildlife habitat, food chains and movement range.",""],[1,"223","1","Human-Wildlife Conflict Reduction Measures","Reduce human- wildlife conflicts.",""],[1,"223","1","Watershed Protection and Water Source Conservation","Minimize drying up of water sources and deepening of groundwater levels by protecting watershed areas.",""],[1,"223","1","Disaster Mitigation for Soil Erosion, Floods, and Landslides","Mitigate disasters such as soil erosion, floods and landslides.",""],[1,"223","1","Forest Fire Prevention and Suppression Capacity","Discourage arsonists, and increase capacity to put out forest fires.",""],[1,"223","1","Community Participation in Biodiversity Conservation","Increase the participation of local communities in conservation of biological diversity.",""],[1,"223","3","Sustainable Biodiversity Management System","Adopt a sustainable management system of biological diversity in the development process.",""],[1,"224","2","Forest Encroachment, Illegal Logging and Poaching Control","Control encroachment of forest areas, illegal logging and poaching of wild animals while sustainably managing forests.",""],[1,"224","2","Forest Administration Capacity and Community Mobilization","Make forest administration more competent and responsible as well as mobilize community to the maximum extent.",""],[1,"224","2","Endangered Species Identification and Protection","Identify, keep record and protect endangered fauna and flora.",""],[1,"224","2","Traditional Knowledge Protection for Ecosystem-Based Adaptation","Protect and promote traditional knowledge and skills in the community for ecosystem-based adaptation and equitable distribution of benefits from forests and biological sectors.",""],[1,"224","3","Endangered Species Protection and Record-Keeping","Protect and keep records of endangered flora and fauna reaching the verge of extinction.",""],[1,"224","3","Climate-Resilient Protected Area Management Planning","Adopt a climate-resilient framework while preparing the management plan of protected areas.",""],[1,"224","3","Wetland and Watershed Protection","Protect wetlands and watershed areas.",""],[1,"224","3","Human-Wildlife Coexistence Initiative","Build human-wildlife co-existence.",""],[1,"224","3","Biodiversity-Sensitive Forest Infrastructure Development","Protect the sensitivity and importance of biological areas while building infrastructure in the forest areas.",""],[1,"224","3","Community-Based Anti-Poaching and Deforestation Control","Encourage provincial mechanisms and local communities to control poachers and deforestation more effectively.",""],[1,"226","3","Sustainable Forest Management and Commercial Use Program","Sustainable forest management and commercial use program: Ensure effective control of encroachment of forest areas, invasive species, forest fires and damage caused by them.",""],[1,"226","4","Sustainable Biodiversity Conservation Program","Program for sustainable conservation of biological diversity: Expand the scope of eco-tourism based on forests and protected areas, and increase optimum participation of local communities in forest conservation.",""]],"18":[[1,"71","2","Commercial Development and Value Addition for Herbs, Timber and Herbal Products","Properly utilize domestic timber products to substitute imports.",""],[1,"71","2","Herbal Product Commercialization Support Measures","For commercialization of herbal products, take measures such as development of appropriate technology, determination of pocket areas, supply of quality seeds and plants, providing technical assistance and capacity building support.",""],[1,"71","2","Herbs and Timber Value Chain Development Initiative","Develop value chains for these products through regular market, processing of herbs, establishment of industry, increasing financial access and certification of products standards.",""],[1,"75","2","Community-Based Fruit Cultivation and Floriculture Program","Run cummunity-based program on fruit cultivation and floriculture on both sides of highways and big roads.",""],[1,"75","2","High-Value Agricultural Produce Promotion Program","Encourage high price range agricultural produce.",""],[1,"75","2","Community-Based Roadside Tree Planting Program","Conduct community-based program to plant fruit trees on the right and left sides of highways and major roads.",""],[1,"75","2","Medicinal Herb Commercial Cultivation and Export Program","Launch special program for herbal cultivation to promote commercial cultivation of medicinal herbs, their processing and export.",""],[1,"75","2","Joint Public-Private Herbal Cultivation Farms","Select appropriate land and establish big scale herbal cultivation farms with joint participation of local communities and the private sector.",""],[1,"75","2","Public and Community Land Leasing Arrangement for Herbal Farms","Make arrangements for providing public land or public, community and leasehold forest lands on lease for this purpose.",""],[1,"75","2","Yarsagumba Cultivation Research and Feasibility Study","In highland pastures in the Himalayan region, carry out research and feasibility study for potential cultivation of 'Yarsagumba' (Cordycep Sps.) and other similar high value medicinal and herbal plants.",""],[1,"75","2","Herbal Medicinal Farm Operation and Export Modality Development","On the basis of study, delineate modality for herbal medicinal farm operation, production, branding, and subsequent export.",""],[1,"75","2","Processed Herbal Extract Export Arrangement","Make arrangements for export of abstracts after processing of relevant plants.",""],[1,"76","3","Herbal Products Commercialization Program","10)Herbal products commercialization program for prosperity: Develop technology for high-value herbs.",""],[1,"76","4","Rational Forest Resource Utilization and Replantation Programme","To increase production, employment and income opportunities by utilizing forest resources on a rational basis, cut down trees which have naturally fallen down or those which have grown old and rugged, and use timber from them in the construction and furniture industry.",""],[1,"77","1","Agro-Forestry Entrepreneurial Activity Facilitation","facilitate the running of agriculture-oriented entrepreneurial activities in forests and forest-oriented entrepreneurial activities on agricultural land.",""],[1,"223","2","Sustainable Forest Management and Wood Product Self-Reliance","Control encroachment of forest areas and invasive species, increase production and productivity of forest areas.",""],[1,"223","3","Green Investment Facilitation","Identify areas of green investment and facilitate it.",""],[1,"223","3","International Climate Finance Access Expansion","Increase Nepal's access to international climate finance.",""],[1,"223","3","Climate-Friendly Development Mainstreaming","Mainstream climate-friendly development.",""],[1,"223","3","Green Economy Localization and Technology Promotion","Localize the concept of green economy, relevant technologies and programs.",""],[1,"223","3","Forest Sector Value Addition and Revenue Sharing","Increase the contribution of forest sector to GDP from the existing three percent by linking forest management with sustainable economic benefits.",""],[1,"223","3","Equitable Forest Revenue Distribution","Ensure equitable distribution of revenue from the forest sector.",""],[1,"224","2","Community Forest Entrepreneurship and Carbon Stock Enhancement","Increase carbon stocks by improving the quality of forests as well as linking community-based forest management to entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"224","2","Forest Resource Import Substitution and Green Enterprise Promotion","Substitute timber imports by increasing production and productivity of forest areas and promoting green enterprises based on forest resources.",""],[1,"224","2","Medicinal Herb Commercial Management Framework","Lay the foundation for sustainable and commercial management of medicinal herbs.",""],[1,"224","3","Climate-Smart Livelihoods for Marginalized Communities","Activate the poor, underprivileged, tribal and marginalized communities through climate-smart agriculture, forestry and other resource-based income generation opportunities.",""],[1,"224","4","Forest Sector Commercialization and Private Forestry Promotion","Increase contribution of the forest sector to GDP. Recognize private forestry as an industry.",""],[1,"224","4","Timber Self-Reliance and Value Addition Initiative","Bring self-reliance in timber and timber-based products. Commercialize and add value to herbal products.",""],[1,"224","4","Agroforestry Land Use Policy Arrangements","Make policy arrangements for the use of degraded forest areas, unused government and public land and vacant land areas for agroforestry.",""],[1,"224","4","Community Forest Management Review","Review the system of recognition of community forest management.",""],[1,"224","4","Clean Energy Investment Expansion","Reduce dependence on imported energy by increasing investment, production and consumption of clean energy.",""],[1,"224","4","Green Economic Growth Framework","Develop and implement a green economic growth framework based on natural resources.",""],[1,"224","4","Electric Mobility Services Promotion","Promote services and businesses that consume electricity in travel and transportation.",""]],"19":[[1,"127","4","River and Water-Induced Disaster Management","Address the disaster risks of floods and inundation in the settlements of Terai and inner-Terai and landslides in the hilly regions.",""],[1,"127","4","Legal Custodianship for Water Reservoir Protection","Designate custodians as clearly defined by law for the protection of water reservoirs such as rivers, lakes and ponds, including underground water sources.",""],[1,"127","4","Riverbank Zoning and Vulnerability Management","Apply measures such as conservation and demarcation for zoning of the river banks; identify vulnerable areas and manage them properly.",""],[1,"127","4","River Jurisdiction and Coordination Framework","Classify rivers and distribute jurisdiction for river management among federal, provincial and local levels with proper coordination.",""],[1,"127","4","International River Cooperation and Utilization","Manage and utilize international rivers for mutual benefits.",""],[1,"130","3","River Protection and Sustainable River Management Framework","Protect and utilize the river as a natural, cultural, tourism and heritage resource.",""],[1,"130","3","River Management Law Enforcement","Enact and implement river management laws.",""],[1,"130","3","Integrated River Sustainability Management Measures","Ensure sustainable management of rivers through measures like sediments management plan, extraction standards, delineating the flow course, and using latest technology.",""],[1,"130","4","Integrated Disaster Management","Integrated disaster management: Minimize damage/risks from disasters using local resources.",""]],"20":[[1,"222","5","Scientific Pollution Control and Sustainable Waste Management","Reduce pollution in water, air and soil on a scientific basis.",""],[1,"224","1","Air Emissions and Environmental Standards Regulation","Make monitoring and regulation effective by determining the standards of air-polluting emissions and environmental consequences of all sectors.",""],[1,"224","1","Clean Energy Conversion and Green Technology Investment","Increase investment in clean energy conversion and environmentally friendly technologies.",""],[1,"224","1","Polluter Pays Principle Enforcement","Enforce the polluter pays principle.",""],[1,"224","1","Public-Private Partnership Waste Management Reform","Make waste management cost effective through public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"224","1","Extended Producer Responsibility for Hazardous Waste","Make producers or importers and polluters responsible for industrial, hospital and hazardous wastes management, as well as implement the concept of extended producer responsibility and cut down industrial emissions.",""],[1,"224","1","Pesticide Use Control and Consumer Education","Control the use of pesticides and conduct consumer education.",""],[1,"226","2","Mandatory Rainwater Harvesting Building Code Reform","Amend the building code to make rain water harvesting mandatory, and encourage the use of local environment-friendly building materials.",""],[1,"226","2","Green Materials and Plastic Substitution Initiative","Increase the use of products based on green raw materials, displacing plastic products.",""],[1,"226","5","Pollution Control Program for a Healthy Society","Pollution control program for healthy society: Determine and update pollution and emission standards of all sectors, including the industry, and expand pollution",""],[1,"227","1","Environmental Monitoring and Regulation Capacity Enhancement","measurement centers to enhance environmental monitoring and regulation capacity.",""],[1,"227","1","Cross-Border Pollution Monitoring","Monitor pollution entering Nepal from across the border.",""],[1,"227","1","Environmental Compliance Enforcement","Ensure effective compliance with environmental study reports.",""],[1,"227","1","Private-Sector Waste Management Reform","Make waste management cost effective and sustainable by involving the private sector; utilize waste reduction, reuse and recycling.",""],[1,"227","1","Waste Disposal Prohibition and Landfill Tax","Prohibit dumping wastes in streams and rivers or burning in forests and open areas.",""],[1,"227","1","Plastic Control Measures","Control plastic items.",""],[1,"227","1","Riverbed Mining Regulation","Implement transparent and scientific criteria for mining in riverbeds and extraction of mineral resources.",""],[1,"227","1","Organic Fertilizer Promotion Action Plan","Prepare an action plan to increase use of organic fertilizers and reduce the use of chemical fertilizers and pesticides.",""]],"21":[[1,"127","2","Clean Drinking Water Access and Source Protection","Ensure availability of clean drinking water to all citizens.",""],[1,"127","2","Water Source Protection from Waste Contamination","Keep all water sources separate from man-made wastes to protect the sources.",""],[1,"127","2","Waste-to-Value Resource Recovery Initiative","Convert waste into money.",""],[1,"130","5","Waste Management Localization and Project Implementation","Localize waste management and run projects; conserve all sources of water and carry on construction activities.",""],[1,"130","5","Water Source Conservation and Construction Activities","conserve all sources of water and carry on construction activities.",""]],"22":[[1,"148","4","Urban Potable Water Supply Expansion","Ensure potable water supply in cities using local and other available sources.",""],[1,"148","4","Co-financed Urban Water and Sanitation Expansion","In urban centers and newly urbanizing areas, follow the principles of co-financing, cost sharing and/or cost recovery to expand water supply and sanitation services.",""]],"23":[[1,"36","2","Export Promotion and Trade Deficit Reduction Strategy","Increase the share of exports in foreign trade; reduce the trade deficit, promote export trade by increasing domestic production and diversification of tradable goods and services.",""],[1,"36","2","Domestic Production and Import Management Initiative","Increase domestic production to meet domestic consumption needs and manage imports so as to reduce trade deficit.",""],[1,"36","2","Foreign Investment Attraction and Balance of Payments Support","Attract foreign investments for favorable international investment position.",""],[1,"36","2","Remittance Formalization and Productive Mobilization Measure","Ensure remittance inflows through official channel and mobilize them in productive sectors and capital formation.",""],[1,"39","2","Transparent Transport and Supply System Measures","Maintain transparency in the transportation system so that the products can be easily supplied to the consumers.",""],[1,"39","2","Trade Facilitation at Transit Points","Ensure simplified procedures and trade facilitation measures at the transit points to reduce the transportation cost of foreign trade and ensure easy access to supplies.",""],[1,"39","2","Competitive Supply System Regulatory Arrangements","Ensure policy and systematic arrangements for a competitive environment in the supply system with the presence of government.",""],[1,"40","2","Export Promotion Strategy Development and Implementation","Develop country-specific and commodity-specific export promotion strategies and implement them.",""],[1,"40","2","Trade Competitiveness Enhancement Measures","Enhance competitive capacity by using appropriate technology, domestic labor, and raw materials, and lower production costs while focusing on exporting goods with high-value and low- volume to lower transport costs.",""],[1,"40","2","International Trade Infrastructure Development","Emphasize on infrastructure development for the promotion of international trade.",""],[1,"40","2","Smooth Transition Strategy Implementation","Implement Smooth Transition Strategy to mitigate the potential impact on international trade after graduation into a developing country.",""],[1,"40","2","Trade Diplomacy and Agreement Implementation","Make diplomatic efforts to promote exports and implement bilateral, regional, and multilateral trade and transit agreements.",""],[1,"42","3","Competitive Market and Supply Chain Strengthening Program","Competitive market and supply chain strengthening program: Promote a healthy competitive market and protect consumer interests.",""],[1,"63","1","Export Promotion and Import Management Program","Programs of export promotion and import management will be implemented with a view to mitigating impact of LDC graduation on export trade and is expected to lower down the trade deficit.",""],[1,"72","3","Trade Quality and Diversification Initiative","To maintain balance in the country's international trade, increase the quality of products produced in the country and diversify countrywise and commodity-wise trade.",""],[1,"72","3","Productivity and Competitiveness Upgrade through Modern Technology and Clean Energy","Increase productivity and competitiveness by using modern technology and clean energy, which leads to lowering production and transit costs.",""],[1,"72","3","Bilateral and Regional Trade Agreement Expansion","Sign bilateral and regional trade agreements with additional countries, and through review and effective implementation of existing agreements, increase export and manage imports in international trade.",""],[1,"72","3","International Trade Policy and Legislation Review","In order to promote investment-friendly environment, review Nepal's international trade policy and legislations, and additionally, promote international trade by emphasizing infrastructure development measures like special economic zones and dry ports.",""],[1,"72","3","Value Chain Development for Indigenous Nepali Products","Establish value chains with branding and patent rights for indigenous Nepali products and bring them in forward and backward linkages and networking in the international market.",""],[1,"77","5","International Trade Promotion Program","15) International trade promotion program: Apart from increasing the quality of manufactured goods, diversify trade on country-wise and commodity-wise bases.",""]],"24":[[1,"40","2","Domestic Production Substitution Policy","Identify goods that can be produced domestically at a lower cost, but are currently being imported in high quantities to increase domestic production.",""],[1,"40","2","Protective Revenue Policy for Domestic Production","Adoptrevenue policy that protects domestic production.",""],[1,"43","3","Import Substitution and Export Promotion Program","Import substitution and export promotion program: Increase production and productivity of the agricultural sector and agro-based industries.",""],[1,"77","3","Customs Tariff Adjustment for Domestic Competitiveness","Adjust customs tariffs in such a way that products produced domestically can withstand competition with imported goods of similar nature.",""],[1,"77","3","Tariff and Non-Tariff Measures for Domestic Sales","To ensure sale of goods that are produced in sufficient quantities within the country, utilize tariff and non-tariff instruments and review existing trade agreements.",""]],"25":[[1,"43","6","Tourism Promotion Program","Tourism promotion program: Develop tourism infrastructure, promote, expand, and stregthen the tourism market, attract quality investment, and diversify tourist activities and destinations.",""],[1,"70","3","Tourism Infrastructure Development and Expansion","develop and expand tourism infrastructure deemed necessary for the promotion of this sector.",""],[1,"70","3","Tourism Destination and Product Diversification Initiative","Identify, develop and diversify attractive destinations and new products/services.",""],[1,"70","3","Ecotourism and Related Industry Development","Develop and expand relevant industries and activities, including ecotourism, keeping close affinities with geographic and cultural diversities and ensuring optimum utilization of these unique features.",""],[1,"72","4","Tourism Sector Value Addition and Infrastructure Expansion","Increase the contribution of tourism sector to GDP by improving value addition and increased income generation from this sector.",""],[1,"72","4","Tourism Infrastructure Development and Investment Mobilization","Develop and expand tourism infrastructure by attracting domestic and foreign investments; develop and expand agro tourism on a regional basis for further promotion of this sector; commercialize locally produced tourism products.",""],[1,"73","1","Tourism Promotion Campaigns in Strategic Markets","Launch tourism promotion campaigns, targeting countries of strategic importance to promote the destination and available products and services in the source market.",""],[1,"79","4","Tourism Sector Development and Strengthening Program","22) Tourism sector development and strengthening program: Development of tourism products and their promotion and publicity.",""]],"26":[[1,"72","4","Ecotourism Integration Initiative","Connect the tourism industry to ecotourism activities in accordance with the concept of sustainable development.",""]],"27":[[1,"102","5","Free Basic Health Services Expansion","Provide free basic health services: Empower health service providers, and provide universal access to basic health services for free, ensuring quality, reliability and equitability.",""],[1,"102","6","Universal Quality Healthcare Access Expansion","Increase equitable access to quality healthcare in promotive, remedial, preventive, diagnostic, curative, palliative and restorative healthcare sectors.",""],[1,"102","6","Low-Cost Quality Healthcare Financing Approach","Adopt the concept of \"quality health care at low cost\" to lower financial risk of citizens in consumption of healthcare services.",""],[1,"103","4","Integrated Health System Development and Expansion","Develop and expand modern, homeopathic, natural and other alternative healthcare service system, etc. to forge out an integrated health system.",""],[1,"107","4","Basic and Community Health Service Strengthening Program","Basic and community health service strengthening program: Mobilize revenue from state coffers to make available free, accessible and quality basic health service for all.",""],[1,"107","4","Community Health System Activation","Make the existing 'community health system' such as community health workers, village clinics, women health volunteers, healthcare mothers' groups, etc. additionally active for increased access to health services and effective management of referral system.",""],[1,"107","4","Local Basic Hospital Establishment","On the basis of standard developed through criteria such as presence of specialist, specialized hospital, population size and disease burden at the federal and provincial levels, establish basic hospital at the local level and constitute citizens' health group at the ward level.",""],[1,"109","2","Multi-sectoral Health Service Delivery Program","Health service delivery program through multi-sectoral and multidimensional mechanisms: To address the large-scale levelwise and agnecy-wise determinants of health, build structure in multisectoral coordination and collaboration with co-funding and co-responsibility.",""]],"28":[[1,"103","9","Self-Reliance in Medicines, Pharmaceutical Products and Vaccine Production","Self-reliance in the production of medicines, pharmaceutical products and vaccines: Be self-reliant in the production of medicines, parmaceutical",""],[1,"104","1","Pharmaceutical Market Management","Manage market for pharmaceutical products.",""],[1,"104","2","Medicine and Pharmaceutical Product Regulation and Monitoring","Strengthen the mechanism working for registration, regulation and monitoring of production, supply and distribution of medicines and pharmaceutical products/equipments.",""],[1,"110","6","Health Service Regulation and Standards Framework","Establish standards for health related services and programs run by all sectors, including government, community and private.",""],[1,"110","7","Drug and Drug-Related Materials Production and Management Program","Drug and drug-related materials production and management program: Restructure and professionally revive Nepal Drug Limited and increase the production of drugs and drug related materials within the country.",""],[1,"110","7","Private Sector Pharmaceutical Production Promotion","Encourage pharmaceutical production from the private sector also to make the country self-reliant in medicine and",""],[1,"111","1","Medicines and Vaccines Production and Supply Chain Improvement","Increase the effectiveness of production, storage, sale, distribution and quality control of medicines and vaccines.",""]],"29":[[1,"102","2","Health Insurance Integration and Expansion","Interlink specialist and specialized health services with health insurance; integrate and mainstream social health security programmes for effective implementation.",""],[1,"103","2","Health Insurance System Restructuring and Coverage Expansion","Expand the coverage of the existing health insurance system in both the formal and informal sectors, avoid duplication and integrate and restructure programs such as social health protection program.",""],[1,"108","1","Integrated Health Insurance and Social Health Protection Program","Review the health insurance program and make radical changes in related policies, laws, regulations and institutional arrangements.",""],[1,"110","5","Targeted Equitable and Inclusive Health Program","Identify persons and communities having no access to health facilities, those who live in remote areas, who are indigent and backward, or belong to ethnic minority, and design and implement targeted program.",""],[1,"110","5","Free Health Insurance for Underserved Communities","Provide free health insurance to such communities.",""]],"30":[[1,"102","4","Provincial Epidemic and Disaster Management Mechanism","Development of a permanent mechanism down to the provincial level in order to manage epidemics and disasters properly:",""],[1,"102","4","Integrated Health Information Management System","Operationalize an integrated health information management system based on empirical findings and database for development of an effective system for preparedness and subsequent response to public health emergency.",""],[1,"109","1","Health Sector Integrated Management Information System Program","Health sector integrated Management Information System program: Bring health institution registration, health management information system, supply management information system, health human resource management information system, physical asset management and health infrastructure information system into an integrated digital system.",""],[1,"109","6","Climate-Resilient Health Program","Climate change resilient health program: Strengthen a comprehensive public health surveillance system with adequate investment that enables forecasting of epidemics and potential threats to public health, early identification, verification and immediate notification.",""]],"31":[[1,"103","8","Evidence-Based Health Management System","Keeping in mind the broad determinants of the health sector, formulate and implement policies, strategies, plans and programs based on facts and evidence.",""],[1,"103","8","Health Institutions as Academic and Service Delivery Centers","Develop health institutions as centres for academic knowledge and service delivery.",""],[1,"103","8","Institutionalized Health Research and Coordination Mechanism","Institutionalize study, research and exploration in coordination with all levels and parties.",""],[1,"104","4","Re-evaluation and Rationalization of Existing Programs","Re-evaluate and modify programs that have been running for years but have not been very effective, and do away with programs that are not justifiable.",""],[1,"110","4","Health Study, Research, and Policy Reform Mechanism","Establish and operationalize a study, research and policy reform mechanism in the Ministry of Health and Population.","Ministry of Health and Population"]],"32":[[1,"107","4","Adolescent Sex Education Programme","Provide sex education to adolescents, covering all genders.",""],[1,"107","4","School Health Worker Assignment and Healthy School Initiative","To ensure access to basic health services, make it compulsory to assign one health worker per school, maintain healthy school and inclusion of health and physical education in curriculum; develop coordination and collaboration with stakeholders in the field of education to this end.",""],[1,"107","4","Local Family Planning Service Delivery","Run family planning system at the local level.",""],[1,"109","5","Safe Motherhood and Reproductive Health Program","Safe motherhood and reproductive health program: Free examination of women for cervical cancer, breast cancer and uterine prolapse.",""],[1,"109","5","Sex-Selective Abortion Prevention Measure","Discourage sex-selective abortion.",""],[1,"109","5","Targeted Social and Cultural Harm Reduction Programs","Prioritize and manage targeted programs to address social and cultural bad practices such as chhaupadi (seclusion during menstrual period), premature wedlock, unwanted pregnancy, etc.",""]],"33":[[1,"101","1","National Science, Technology and Innovation Policy Implementation","During the Fifteenth Plan, a National Science Technology and Innovation Policy, 2019 has been formulated by identifying areas that can boost production and productivity of the country.",""],[1,"102","1","Integrated Science and Technology Research and Development Programme","Advance research and development in the fields of science and technology with an integrated and strategic approach.",""],[1,"102","1","University and Research Institution Coordination Mechanism","Enhance coordination between universities, research institutes, private sector and government to improve service delivery.",""],[1,"102","1","Global Research Network Access Initiative","Establish access to global networks of research and development and academic institutions for universities and institutions involved in scientific research.",""],[1,"106","2","Policy and Legal Arrangements for R&D and Innovation","In order to adopt research and development and innovation in all sectors of production, make necessary policy and legal arrangements.",""],[1,"106","2","Scientific Knowledge Management and Specialized Universities","Manage scientific knowledge, establish specialized universities as academic institutions to promote scientific research, technology development and innovation promotion.",""],[1,"106","2","Research-Industry Collaboration and Partnership Mechanism","Develop collaboration and partnership between research agencies, scientific professional societies and industries.",""],[1,"106","3","Innovation and Entrepreneurship Incubation and Acceleration Centers","Take measures for setting up incubation center for innovation and entrepreneurship development, accelerator center, technology park, rural innovation center, observation of celestial bodies, high mountain research, promotion of science and technology education.",""],[1,"106","3","Science and Technology Innovation Regulatory Framework","Establish an institutional measure to promote, facilitate and regulate innovation.",""],[1,"106","3","Research and Educational Network Expansion","Expand access to research and educational networks.",""],[1,"106","4","Special Incentives for Technology and Innovation Research","Provide suitable incentives to the private sector and government institutions for their exploration and research in the field of technology and innovation.",""],[1,"106","5","Technology Testing and Quality Management Adoption","Adopt various management methodologies like technology testing, accreditation, quality management system, innovation management system in the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"114","1","Science and Technology Research and Innovation Fund","Set aside two percent of the country's budget to establish and operate a special fund for science and technology research and innovation.",""],[1,"114","1","Manufacturing and Sustainable Infrastructure Research Unit","Establish research and technology development unit in the field of manufacturing industry and sustainable infrastructure.",""],[1,"114","1","Science and Technology Institutions Restructuring","Restructure National Academy of Science and Technology, B.P. Koirala Memorial Planetarium, Observatory and Science Museum Development Committee.",""],[1,"114","1","State-Level Technology Entrepreneurship Start-Up Zones","Establish and operate state-level technology entrepreneurship start-up zone.",""],[1,"114","1","Innovation Center Establishment and Operation","Establish and operate an innovation center.",""],[1,"114","1","Inclusive Research and Innovation Talent Mobilization","Mobilize and encourage talented scientists, technicians and youth force in practical research and innovative work, while effecting inclusive policy reforms.",""],[1,"114","1","Specialized Research Centers Development","Establish high altitude research center, space study center and nuclear research center.",""],[1,"114","1","Emerging Technologies Research Centers","Operate research centers in the field of emerging technologies such as atmospheric research center, robotics and artificial intelligence research centers.",""],[1,"114","2","Research and Technology Development Collaboration Program","Collaboration program in research and technology development: To promote collaboration, coordination and partnership in scientific research and innovation, utilize science diplomacy for forging agreement and understanding with various friendly nations as well as international organizations and associations.",""],[1,"114","3","Latest Technology Research and Application Program","Latest technology research and application program: To provide high-level services in crime investigation and dispensation of justice, introduce new methods of services.",""],[1,"117","4","Expansion of NAST Research Centers","Expansion of NAST research centers",""],[1,"117","8","Innovation Promotion Institutions Establishment and Regulation","Establishment, regulation of innovation promotion institutions (science cities/parks, incubators, accelerators, rural incubators, technology parks)",""]],"34":[[1,"33","4","Agro-Based Industry Establishment Initiative","Emphasizing on establishment of agro-based industries for easy supply of the industrial raw materials.",""],[1,"33","4","Industrial Market Access and Private Investment Promotion","Ensuring market for industrial products to attract private sector investment in establishing industries.",""],[1,"33","4","Import Substitution through Local Production Promotion","Reducing import dependency by promoting local production.",""],[1,"33","4","Integration of Forestry, Tourism, and Energy with Industry and Export Trade","Integrate forestry, tourism and energy with industries and export trade as a means to increase production and productivity.",""],[1,"34","3","Manufacturing Industry Promotion and Industrial Estate Development","Motivating manufacturing industries for enhancing domestic production rather than investment in distributive trade.",""],[1,"34","5","Private Sector Investment and Business Environment Support","Facilitating industrial ventures and businesses to establish and operate .. Enhancing business confidence as well as promoting investment and competitiveness.",""],[1,"34","5","Public-Private Partnership and Co-financing Framework","Developing a clear and collaborative model of public-private partnership, co-financing and collaboration among three tiers of government.",""],[1,"34","5","Private Sector Productivity Diversification and Specialization Initiative","Enhancing productivity by diversifying and specializing private sector investments to help Nepal upgrade into a developing country.",""],[1,"34","5","Private Sector Investment Promotion in Productive Sectors","Promoting private sector's investment towards the productive sector.",""],[1,"36","4","Public Enterprise Competitiveness and Governance Reform","Enhance competitiveness and business capacity of public enterprises.",""],[1,"38","4","Investment Facilitation and Legal Simplification for Priority Sectors","Simplify legal and procedural matters to increase domestic and foreign investments in areas such as energy, tourism, information technology, and others that have comparative advantages.",""],[1,"38","4","Domestic Production and Intellectual Property Promotion Initiative","Increase internal production and productivity by developing a culture of protecting intellectual property and consuming domestic products.",""],[1,"38","5","Manufacturing Industry Development Support","Ensure that the government's role in adequate funding in infrastructure development activities in areas like availability of raw materials, easy access to financial resources, support for marketing, and reducing production cost is fulfilled.",""],[1,"38","5","Youth Entrepreneurship Innovation and Startup Promotion","Encourage young entrepreneurs through innovation and startup promotion.",""],[1,"38","5","Policy and Institutional Facilitation for Entrepreneurs","Ensure policy and institutional facilitation to increase morale and motivation of entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"38","5","Special Economic Zone Strengthening","Strengthen special economic zones to implement an integrated",""],[1,"39","1","Industrial Villages Establishment and Operation","Establish and operate industrial villages as a coordinated effort among the levels of government.",""],[1,"39","1","Investment Promotion and SME Labor Mobilization","Create an environment that fosters investment and mobilizes the labor force mobilization in small and medium industries.",""],[1,"42","1","Infrastructure Development and Investment Enhancement Program","Infrastructure development and investment enhancement program: For the production-oriented sector, operationalize programs such as the construction of necessary infrastructure and establishment of their interlinkages, construction of industrial and commercial infrastructure, and conducting programe based on increased saving.",""],[1,"43","5","Industrial Promotion and Infrastructure Investment Program","11)Industrial promotion and investment in infrastructure development program: Operate large-scale industries at full capacity.",""],[1,"69","2","Industrial Sector Competitiveness and Investment Promotion","Identify and produce goods and services that have competitive edge and/or comparative advantage.",""],[1,"69","2","Industrial Value Chain and Intellectual Property Support","Ensure branding, patent right protection and forward and backward linkages of Nepali indigenous products in international value chains, and extend networking.",""],[1,"72","2","Industrial Investment Environment Reform","For increased establishment and expansion of the industry, prepare a suitable investment environment through amendment to the investment- related legislation, and attract foreign resources in addition to internal resources, for meeting rising investment requirements.",""],[1,"72","2","Mineral Exploration and Commercialization Programme","Increase investment in search, exploration and identification of potential mines that lie scattered across the country, and through systematic documentation of mines, bring them to commercial use.",""],[1,"72","2","Small and Medium Domestic Industry Promotion","Develop and promote small, medium and domestic industries in the fields of agriculture, forestry and mining.",""],[1,"77","2","Industrial Development and Investment Promotion Program","12)Industrial development and investment promotion program: Create investment-friendly environment by amending investment laws and regulations and encourage domestic and foreign investments.",""],[1,"77","3","Mining Exploration and Commercialization Framework","Search for, explore and identify mines, and commercialize mining industry in public-private-partnership framework.",""],[1,"77","4","MSME Development and Promotion Program","For development and promotion of micro, small and medium enterprises, interlink traditional knowledge, skills and experience and operationalize such enterprises.",""]],"35":[[1,"172","4","Private, Cooperative and Non-governmental Sector Production and Productivity Enhancement","Increase production and productivity with the involvement of the private, cooperative and non-governmental sectors.",""],[1,"172","4","Business and Investment Uncertainty Reduction Measures","Address business and investment uncertainties and constraints.",""],[1,"172","4","Production Cost Reduction and Market Access Expansion","Reduce production costs and increase market access.",""],[1,"172","4","Competition, Quality and Regulation Reform","Create an environment of healthy competition while reforming quality and regulation.",""],[1,"172","4","Investment Efficiency Improvement Measures","Increase effectiveness and efficiency of investment.",""],[1,"172","4","Regional and Local Market Access Facilitation","Establish easy access to the market by producing goods and services of regional and local characteristics.",""],[1,"173","1","Efficient and Poverty-Alleviation-Focused Public Expenditure Management","finance by focusing on efficient, productive, employment generating and poverty- alleviation-focused public expenditure.",""],[1,"173","1","Financial Discipline Promotion","Promote financial discipline.",""],[1,"176","1","Capital Expenditure Expansion","Increase capital expenditure.",""],[1,"177","2","Provincial and Local Comparative Advantage Identification and Investment Climate Improvement","Identify the areas of comparative advantage in the provincial and local levels based on study and review of available resources and potentials.",""],[1,"177","2","Investment-Friendly Infrastructure and Market Support","Create an investment-friendly environment by promoting economic and physical infrastructure, ensuring resource availability, and assuring market.",""],[1,"177","2","Rural Economy Monetization Through Financial Access","Monetize the rural economy by increasing access to financial services.",""],[1,"177","2","Formal Sector Expansion and Regulatory Simplification","Expand the formal sector through accounting of transactions, control of business diversion and illegal transactions, development of simple tax system, financial literacy and mobilization of effective integrated regulatory mechanism.",""],[1,"177","3","Integrated Natural Resources Investment and Utilization Framework","Promote identification, investment and utilization of natural resources by developing integrated laws and frameworks, and maintaining levelwise partnership.",""],[1,"177","3","Natural Resources Investment and Sharing Framework","The National Natural Resources and and Fiscal Commission should prepare a clear framework of investment, utilization and sharing of natural resources and put it into implementation.",""],[1,"177","3","Integrated Human Resource Development Plan","Develop and implement an integrated human resource plan for utilization of human resources with high skills and entrepreneurial culture.",""],[1,"231","1","Domestic Finance and Competitiveness Development","internal finance and competitive capacity should be developed, ensuring an irreversible and sustainable graduation.",""],[1,"234","4","SDG Resource Mobilization and Economic Diplomacy","Mobilize both domestic as well as external resources to meet the required financial resources, technology and human resources for the attainment of Sustainable Development Goals.",""],[1,"236","1","Domestic and International Finance Mobilization for Infrastructure and Manufacturing Projects","income by mobilizing domestic finance and international finance for projects in the infrastructure and manufacturing sectors.",""],[1,"237","1","Economic Diplomacy for Development Assistance Mobilization","Emphasize on economic diplomacy to address potential impacts on mobilization of international development cooperation.",""],[1,"237","4","SDG Financing and Investment Framework Development","Make assessment of expenditure needs and resource estimates and determine investment framework for implemention of the SDGs.",""],[1,"237","4","Alternative SDG Financing Instruments Study","Study financing of the SDGs and use alternative and new financial instruments in overall government investment.",""],[1,"237","4","Private and Cooperative Sector SDG Investment Mobilization","Determine priority areas for private and cooperative sector investment mobilization for SDGs.",""],[1,"237","4","Domestic and Foreign Investment Promotion for SDG Implementation","Create an investment environment, attract domestic and foreign investment in production enhancement and job creation, and mobilize resources for implementation of SDGs.",""],[1,"237","4","Public-Private Partnership Foreign Investment Mobilization","Mobilize more foreign investment through public- private partnerships.",""],[1,"237","5","Targeted Sustainable Development Investment Partnerships","Make private and household investment partnerships targeted to sustainable development.",""],[1,"237","5","Multi-Level SDG Implementation Coordination Framework","Develop effective partnership and collaboration between all three levels of government, the private, cooperative, community, non-governmental sectors and development partners for implementation of SDGs.",""]],"36":[[1,"235","3","Trade Policy and Trade Strategy Implementation","Implement the Trade Policy, 2015, Trade Logistics Policy, 2023, Nepal Integrated Trade Strategy, 2023 through programs.",""],[1,"235","3","Trade Facilitation and Logistics Action Plan","Formulate a time-bound action plan for implementation of the Trade Facilitation Master Plan and Trade Logistics Policy and implement it.",""],[1,"235","3","Trade Implementation Financing Strategy","Formulate a financial strategy for mobilization of financial resources required for implementation.",""],[1,"235","3","Trade Performance Monitoring and Evaluation","Carry out regular monitoring and evaluation of performance indicators.",""],[1,"235","3","Preferential Trade Agreement Participation","Participate in preferential trade agreements.",""],[1,"236","2","Trade Sector Institutional Capacity and Infrastructure Strengthening","Strengthen institutional capacity and infrastructure related to the trade sector to address potential impact on Nepal's total export trade after graduation from the least developed country.",""],[1,"236","2","Export Promotion for Comparative Advantage Goods and Services","Promote export of goods and services with comparative advantage and competitiveness.",""],[1,"236","2","Customs and Trade Cost Reform Package","To address price rise of Nepali goods after cut in duty free and quota free maket access, make reforms in customs, improve trade infrastructures and their expansion, lower cost of transit and take other suitable measures to reduce the cost of trade.",""],[1,"236","2","Product Quality and Productivity Improvement Initiative","Improve quality and productivity in order to increase competitiveness of products, emphasize on production according to demand of the world market.",""],[1,"236","3","Graduation-Focused Trade Negotiation and Export Diversification","Explore new opportunities and increase production and supply capacity of goods and services in order to offset potential losses in international trade after graduation of Nepal from least developed country category by 2026.",""],[1,"236","4","Service Trade Promotion Strategy","Since Nepal is a landlocked country, give emphasis on service trade.",""],[1,"236","4","Services Export Promotion Initiative","Promote export of services related to tourism, electricity trade, information technology and financial services.",""],[1,"238","3","Export Promotion Program","3) Export promotion program: Mobilize concessional loans for export-oriented industries, improve the quality of exportable goods and operate quality certification laboratories.",""],[1,"238","3","Export Market Diversification and Trade Access Expansion","Diversify products and markets to increase exports.",""],[1,"238","3","Export Market Research and Supply Chain Study","Study demand, production and supply chains of the global market for goods and services, and increase access of Nepali goods and services to the international market, and manage imports.",""],[1,"238","3","Traditional Skills and MSME Export Promotion","Conduct programs to promote the export of traditional skills, artifacts and products based on Nepali raw materials; promote micro, small and medium enterprises.",""],[1,"238","3","Export Services Human Resource and Infrastructure Development","Develop human resources and infrastructure for the export of services such as hydropower, information technology based services, tourism, higher education, health services.",""],[1,"238","4","Export Destination Diversification Program","Program for diversification of export destination countries: Diversify exports of domestic goods and services.",""],[1,"240","1","Bilateral Free Trade Agreement Study and Trade Preference Continuation Negotiation","Conduct detailed studies on bilateral free trade area agreements with the United States, China and other major trading partner countries.",""],[1,"240","1","Continuation of Duty-Free and Trade Preference Facilities","Take initiatives for continuation of duty free facilities received as the least developed country from Australia, Canada, Japan, Norway, Korea and Switzerland.",""],[1,"240","1","WTO and SAFTA Trade Concession Negotiation Arrangements","Make arrangements for negotiations with the World Trade Organization in cooperation with the group of the least developed countries to continue the duty free, quota free and other facilities available to the least developed countries for a certain period of time even after graduation.",""],[1,"240","2","Value Chain Development and Quality Testing Program","9) Value chain development and quality testing program: Develop value chains for goods and services of export potentials identified by the Nepal Trade Integration Strategy.",""]],"37":[[1,"42","2","Innovation and Entrepreneurship Development Program","Innovation and entrepreneurship development program: Ensure favorable facilitative policy measures and access to finance for those production-oriented sectors that can attain high-value addition and establish linkages with global value chains.",""],[1,"42","2","Credit Allocation for Innovation and Research","Ensure that a certain portion of the total credit of the financial institution flows to innovation and research.",""],[1,"53","5","Technology Adoption and Mechanization for Productivity","It is estimated that capital productivity will be raised by additional use of technology in agriculture and industrial productions.",""],[1,"77","3","Technology Development Fund for Start-ups","Encourage start-up ventures through technology development fund.",""],[1,"77","4","Traditional Knowledge and Technology Integration Initiative","Also interlink traditional knowledge, skill, experience and technology with innovative knowledge and techniques.",""]],"38":[[1,"85","1","Universal Social Protection Floor","It is necessary to establish sustainable and universal social protection floor by combining such factors as needs, rights and contribution-based social security program.",""],[1,"86","2","Contribution-Based Social Security Expansion","For this, strategies and programs that are being implemented include promotion of domestic employment, bringing to an end compulsion for foreign employment and making it safe and dignified, expansion of contribution-based social security and raising productivity through skill development.",""],[1,"87","2","Expansion of Contribution-Based Social Security Fund Coverage","Various efforts are ongoing to increase the number of establishments joining the Social Security Fund by collaborating with the private sector.",""],[1,"87","2","Integrated National Social Protection Framework","The Integrated National Social Protection Framework, 2023 has been launched with a view to manage increasing expenditure in this sector, promote contribution-based social security program and streamline the fragmented social protection program for raising effectiveness.",""],[1,"89","3","Social Security System Integration and Expansion","Integrate and manage the current structure and system of social security, reducing life- cycle risks, and bring citizens into the scope of social security.",""],[1,"89","3","Employment and Skills Support for Indigent and Unemployed Citizens","Create employment opportunities for indigent and unemployed citizens and help them gain skill and competence for jobs.",""],[1,"89","3","Contribution-Based Social Security Expansion","Enlarge the scope of contribution-based social security program to make it effective and inclusive of all types of workers.",""],[1,"89","3","Contribution-Based Productive Social Protection System","Establish contribution-based and productive social protection system.",""],[1,"89","3","Implementation of the Integrated National Social Protection Framework 2023","Fully implement Integrated National Social Protection Framework, 2023; lower down public responsibility to ensure financial sustainability.",""],[1,"92","1","Social Security Legal and Regulatory Reform","Make timely reforms in and amendments to the laws and regulations related to social security.",""],[1,"92","1","Integrated Social Security System Management","Integrate and manage the current structure and system of social security to facilitate the life and living of all concerned.",""],[1,"92","1","Integrated National Social Protection Framework Implementation","Effective implementation of the Integrated National Social Protection Framework, 2023.",""],[1,"92","1","Contribution-Based Social Protection Expansion","Expand the scope of social protection through contribution-based social security.",""],[1,"92","1","Social Security Fund Investment and Diversification","Transform and diversify the corpus of social security fund as a source for safe investment and mobilize it in productive and job creation areas.",""],[1,"92","1","Labor Market Skills Development for Disadvantaged and Unemployed Citizens","Targetting disadvantaged and unemployed citizens, develop their skills and competence according to employment services and demand of the labor market.",""],[1,"92","1","Migrant Worker Basic Social Security Financing","Manage financial responsibility for basic social security of citizens who constitute migrant workers as deemed necessary during their active work life and after retirement.",""],[1,"95","1","Integrated Social Protection Mechanism","Integrate existing social protection programs that remain fragmented and develop an integrated social protection mechanism that can be implemented on a sustainable basis.",""],[1,"95","1","Expanded Productive Social Protection Access","Increase access to productive social protection and avoid duplication.",""],[1,"95","1","Voluntary Renunciation of Social Security Benefits","Encourage financially well-placed individuals to renounce their social security allowance and pension voluntarily.",""],[1,"95","2","Social Security Scheme Reform and Expansion","Ensure basic level social security from the state level; make social security schemes contributor-friendly and transform them from social-support based to contribution and need-based.",""],[1,"95","2","Social Security Investment Mobilization Mechanism","Mobilize and promote investments from Social Security in high return sectors.",""],[1,"95","2","Universal Social Security Coverage Expansion","Expand the involvement of workers working in all sectors in social security, include in its fold workers in foreign employment, people in self-employment living abroad, those in informal sector and self-employment domestically, and give it a continuity.",""],[1,"95","2","Social Security Benefits Upgrade","Upgrade the facilities under security schemes.",""],[1,"95","2","Formalization of Informal Employment for Social Security","Bring informal employment within the formal sector into the realm of social security.",""],[1,"95","3","Integrated Life-Cycle Social Security System","Develop for implementation of an integrated social security system based on insurance and life cycle to meet basic needs in the areas of health, education, employment, housing and caregiving.",""],[1,"187","4","Integration and Rationalization of Social Security Programs","Eliminate duplication in social security programs operated by the federal, provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"187","4","Disaster- and Epidemic-Responsive Social Protection Expansion","Reduce the possibility of additional chunk of population fall below the poverty line due to disasters, epidemics, climate change, etc., and include the target group within the fold of social security.",""],[1,"187","4","Integrated and Sustainable Social Security Reform","Make social security program complete, sustainable and productive by integrating it to bring the target group at the center.",""],[1,"188","5","Social Security Program Implementation for Poor Households and Vulnerable Communities","Ensure effective implementation of social security programs for poor households and communities that need protection from the state.",""],[1,"188","5","Contribution-Based Social Security Plan","Emphasize on the implementation of contribution-based social security plan to guarantee social security to all citizens.",""],[1,"188","5","Integrated Social Security System Development","Development of disaggregated data, implementation of integrated social security structure, coordination between three levels and effective monitoring to make the social security program effective.",""],[1,"188","6","Risk Reduction Insurance Expansion","Make arrangements for insurance for life, property, crops, business, etc. of poor families, farmers, poor households and small entrepreneurs to reduce losses caused by disasters, epidemics, climate change, and",""],[1,"189","1","Expansion of Health Insurance Coverage","Broaden the scope of health insurance and implement it at all local levels by increasing the quality of service.",""],[1,"189","5","Basic and Essential Goods and Services Access Program","Access to basic and essential goods and services program: Make availability of food at a concessional rate to households with state facility cards.",""],[1,"190","2","Poverty Alleviation Program through Social Security","Provide micro credits, social safety nets for risk reduction, food and nutrition security, minimum employment, targeting poor households.",""],[1,"190","2","Expansion of Community-Level Contribution-Based Social Security","Extend the contribution- based social security program down to the community level.",""]],"39":[[1,"185","2","Poverty Alleviation and Inequality Reduction Programs","poverty alleviation and inequality reduction programs have come to the centerstage.",""],[1,"185","2","Inclusion and Affirmative Action Policies","Through implementation of policies on inclusion and affirmative action, participation of marginalized and disadvantaged communities in the state mechanisms is on the rise.",""],[1,"186","3","Targeted Poverty and Inequality Reduction Programs","Conduct targeted programs by mapping poverty and inequality: Carry out and update identification of the really poor households and get disaggregated data based on ethnic groups, language, geography and gender.",""],[1,"187","5","Equitable Participation and Representation in Governance Mechanism","Ensure equitable representation and meaningful participation in activities like policy, planning, budget formulation, implementation and monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"187","5","Universal Access to Public Services and Facilities","Ensure access of all citizens to public services and facilities.",""],[1,"187","5","Multi-Stakeholder Partnership and Coordination for Poverty Reduction","Enhance partnership and coordination of government, private, cooperative, community and non-governmental sectors to reduce poverty and inequality.",""],[1,"187","5","Fair Distribution of Development Outcomes Initiative","Create a society free from exploitation by ending economic inequality through fair distribution of outcomes obtained from development.",""],[1,"187","6","Special Programs for Identified Poor Households","Conducting special programs targeting identified poor households: Identify poor households and update integrated and disaggregated data in coordination with the local level.",""],[1,"187","6","Automated Data-Driven Poverty Targeting Policy Framework","Make policies, plans and programs targeted to the poor based on automated data system.",""],[1,"188","2","Income Redistribution Strategy","Adopt income redistribution strategies to reduce inequality between the rich and poor.",""],[1,"188","2","Subsidized Basic and Essential Services for Poor and Marginalized Households","Distribute basic and essential services to individuals and families of the poor and marginalized communities in a subsidized manner to lead a dignified life.",""],[1,"189","2","Target Group Participation and Positive Discrimination Measures","Ensure participation of the target groups in political, administrative, judicial and other fields through methods such as positive discrimination, proportional representation, reservation.",""],[1,"189","2","Private, Cooperative, and Non-Governmental Positive Discrimination Implementation","Encourage the private, cooperative and non-governmental sectors to implement the policy of positive discrimination.",""],[1,"189","2","Cross-Sector Partnership and Coordination for Poverty and Inequality Reduction","Enhance the partnership and coordination of the government, private, cooperative, community and non-governmental sectors for reducing poverty and inequality.",""],[1,"189","3","State Facility Identity Card Distribution Program","State facility identity card distribution program: After completing the identification of poor households and ID card distribution program, distribute state facility ID cards to the identified poor.",""],[1,"189","3","Integrated Social Protection and Service Access Card","Eliminate duplication by gradually including social security and other service facilities provided by all three levels of government in the state facility identification card.",""],[1,"189","3","Targeted Program Preference for Cardholders","Give preference to poor households who have state facility ID cards when conducting targeted programs in coordination with the local level.",""],[1,"189","4","Social and Cultural Transformation Against Discrimination","Carry out social and cultural transformation to reduce existing discrimination and social bad practices.",""],[1,"190","5","Empowerment and Capacity Development Program","Empowerment and capacity development program: Provide training and orientation for the protection, upliftment, empowerment and development of the poor, Dalits, landless squatters, minorities, endangered and marginalized groups.",""],[1,"191","1","Targeted Class Participation and Affirmative Action Expansion","Promote people's participation in targeted class focused programs and development.",""],[1,"191","1","Reservation and Affirmative Action Expansion in Non-State Sectors","Extend reservation and affirmative action programs in the private, cooperative and non-governmental sectors.",""],[1,"191","1","Reservation System Review and Improvement","Review and improve the reservation system.",""],[1,"191","1","Poverty Benefit Access Improvement","Improve access of the poor to equitable distribution of benefits.",""],[1,"191","1","Poverty Reduction Program Coordination Mechanism","Establish mechanisms to coordinate poverty reduction programs.",""],[1,"191","1","Remote Service Delivery Expansion","Increase access to basic goods and services by using methods such as mobile services and electronic means to provide services to remote areas from the local level.",""],[1,"214","3","Equitable Inclusion Program","Equitable inclusion program: Ensure equitable distribution and easy access of the deprived groups and communities to services, resources and means made available by the state, such as in agriculture, education, health, industry, employment, justice sectors etc.",""]],"40":[[1,"155","2","Human Trafficking Prevention, Rescue, Protection and Rehabilitation","Human Trafficking and Transportation (Control) Act, 2007 and subsequent Regulation, 2008 are being implemented for prevention, rescue, protection and rehabilitation of the victims and for actions in regard to legal remedies.",""],[1,"155","2","Palermo Protocol Implementation for Trafficking Prevention and Suppression","Nepal has ratified the complementary Protocol (Palermo Protocol) of the United Nations Convention against Transnational Organized Crime, which deals with the prevention, suppression and punishment of trafficking in persons, especially women and children.",""],[1,"155","5","Social Evils and Harmful Practices Elimination Campaign","Eliminate social evils and social bad practices such as child marriage, polygamy, forced marriage of sexual and gender minorities, chhaupadi (seclusion during menstrual cycle), dowry, untouchability, witchcraft accusations, etc.",""],[1,"156","1","Violence Prevention and Access to Justice Measures","Eliminate all forms of violence, discrimination and exploitation, including domestic violence against women, and make access to justice easy, affordable and accessible.",""],[1,"156","1","Gender-Based Violence and Trafficking Control Measures","Adopt effective measures for control and prevention of gender-based violence, human trafficking and transportation, human smuggling, kidnapping, etc. in their changing dimensions, forms, methods and routes used.",""],[1,"158","2","Male Participation Network for Gender-Based Violence Prevention","For elimination of all types of gender-based discrimination, violence and exploitation, activate and mobilize male participation network in federal, provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"159","3","Coordination and Partnership Mechanism for Victim Rescue and Social Integration","For rescue, protection, rehabilitation and social integration of victims of gender violence, human trafficking and transportation, child labor, sexual abuse, etc., make sure to develop coordination and partnerships at the family and community levels as well as at the different levels of government and relevant agencies.",""],[1,"160","2","Gender-Based Violence Elimination and Relief Funds","Establish gender-based violence elimination funds and inter-level relief and rehabilitation funds at all three levels of government with a view to providing rescue and relief as well as free legal assistance, psychosocial counselling, skill oriented program and social integration to victims of violence or for those who have been impacted by violence.",""],[1,"160","3","National Implementation Action Plan to End Social Harmful Practices","Formulate and implement a national implementation action plan to end social bad practices and social evils such as child labor, gender violence, sexual abuse, prostitution and witchcraft accusations, chhaupadi, menstrual discrimination, etc.",""],[1,"161","2","Gender Equality Monitoring and Violence Elimination Program","5) Gender equality, economic empowerment and violence elimination program: Establish a strong and common system for continuous monitoring and evaluation of gender equality initiatives in the community.",""],[1,"161","2","Gender-Based Discrimination and Violence Elimination Measures","Eliminate gender-based discrimination and violence.",""],[1,"161","2","Self-Defense Training for Girls","Conduct self-defense training programs for all girls.",""],[1,"161","4","Regulation and Enforcement Against Online Violence","Make legal arrangements for regulation and control of violence that is being perpetrated by misuse of information technology and social networks, and strictly enforce it.",""],[1,"162","2","Targeted Programs to Eliminate Domestic Violence and Discrimination","For elimination of domestic violence and all other kinds of discrimination, violence, exploitation, social bad practices and social evils, superstition, racial discrimination, deprivation and other evils, launch special and targeted programs.",""],[1,"162","2","One-Stop Crisis Management Center Upgrading","Upgrade one-stop crisis management centers to increase effectiveness of service delivery in health treatment and legal remedies of victims of domestic and gender-based violence, as well as in rehabilitation and social integration.",""],[1,"163","4","Men's Participation Networks for Gender-Based Violence Prevention","Mobilize men's participation networks to prevent gender-based violence.",""]],"41":[[1,"154","2","Disability Rights Convention Implementation","The Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, 2006 and the Asia and Pacific Regional Periodic Strategy and Action Plan on Disability are also being implemented.",""],[1,"154","4","Implementation of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act and Regulation","The Act Related to Rights of Persons with Disabilities, 2017 and subsequent Regulation, 2020 are being implemented.",""],[1,"160","5","Disability-Friendly Life Facilitation Program","Disability friendly life facilitation program: Prepare and implement national standards for the operation of private and public care centers, residential rehabilitation",""],[1,"161","1","Disability-Friendly Information Access Standards and Interpreter Services","To increase access to information for people with intellectual disabilities, autism, deafness, blindness and multiple disabilities, create and implement service standards and procedures that includes pictorial, simple large print, touch signals and sign language, and provision of interpreters.",""],[1,"161","1","National Disability Prevention and Rehabilitation Expansion","Gradually expand the disability prevention and rehabilitation program to all the provinces.",""],[1,"161","1","Disability-Friendly Mass Media and Technology Accessibility Measures","Ensure accessibility of people with disabilities to mass media, information and technology by making arrangement for availability of services and equipment and conducting a disability-friendly facilitation program.",""],[1,"164","2","Universal Accessibility and Auxiliary Materials Program","Make public places, public service offices and other infrastructure based on a universal framework to be friendly to people with disabilities, senior citizens, children, gender and sexual minorities.",""],[1,"164","2","Resettlement, Health Care, and Auxiliary Materials Supply","Arrange the production and supply of short-term and long-term resettlement, health care and auxiliary materials.",""],[1,"164","2","Disability Data Collection and Assisted Living Support","Collect data on persons with total disabilities and provide assisted living.",""]],"42":[[1,"155","1","Child Search and Rescue Service and Child Helpline","For emergency rescue of children under distress and their protection and management, Child Search and Rescue Service '104' and Child Helpline '1098' have been in operation.",""],[1,"155","1","Implementation of the Act Related to Children and Subsequent Regulation","The Act Related to Children, 2018 and subsequent Regulation, 2022 are being implemented.",""],[1,"161","3","Child Rights Protection and Promotion Program","6) Child rights protection and promotion program: To end all forms of child labor, implement mandatory pre-inspection to ensure child labor-free workplaces at the time of approval and renewal of all industries, factories, businesses.",""],[1,"161","3","Alternative Care Arrangements for Vulnerable Children","Make arrangements for alternative care by local level governments for abandoned, orphaned and parentless children and children in need of special protection.",""],[1,"161","3","Child-Friendly Local Governance Promotion Program","Promote and strengthen children's rights through programs that promote child-friendly local governance.",""],[1,"161","3","Children's Participation Institutions Expansion","Through establishment and operation of institutions like children's clubs, child network, adolescents groups, scout, etc. and their expansion, increase children's participation in learning and understanding of social responsibility and self-help lifestyle.",""],[1,"161","4","Child Correctional Home Standards and Management Reform","Effectively operate and manage child correctional homes by fixing minimum standards for operation of services by classifying them on the basis of minimum standards.",""],[1,"162","1","Deinstitutionalization of Child Care and Last-Resort Care System","Discourage institutional residential care in orphanages and implement a system of care only as a last resort.",""],[1,"162","1","Child- and Parent-Friendly Juvenile Justice Reform","Make juvenile justice system simple, easy and child and parent friendly.",""]],"43":[[1,"70","6","Pocket Agricultural Production Program in Food-Deficit Remote Areas","Bring pocket program for agricultural production in food-deficit remote areas.",""],[1,"71","1","Concessional Quality Food Supply for Indigent Households","quality food to indigent households at concessional rates.",""],[1,"71","1","Post-Harvest Loss Reduction and Safe Storage Provision","For minimization of post- harvest loss of food crops, vegetables and fruit, etc. and to maintain their quality, make provision of safe storage and supply.",""],[1,"71","1","Food Habit Refinement and Food Culture Exchange Initiative","Refine food habits in coordination with the local levels and, through the exchange of food culture among different ethnic groups, communities and regions, conserve diversity of food and food habits.",""],[1,"71","1","Agricultural Modernization and Self-Reliance Investment Package","Ensure enhanced investment, infrastructure, agricultural inputs and the latest technology in the agriculture and animal farming sectors so as to enhance self- reliance in basic food items through modernization, diversification and commercialization.",""],[1,"76","2","Clean and Nutritious Food Promotion Program","Clean and nutritious food promotion program: To ensure food and nutrition security, emphasize on original and indigenous produce.",""]],"44":[[1,"153","2","Proportional Inclusion and Human Rights Institutionalization","For institutionalizing the achievements made in the human rights regime so far by consolidating coordination and collaboration between federal, provincial and local levels, emphasis is laid on removing social, economic, and political barriers faced by those communities who are traditionally marginalized and deprived.",""],[1,"153","2","Empowerment Support for Deprived Communities","Providing to these deprived groups and communities opportunities in health, education, housing, skill development and employment, and prior rights over resources, and mobilizing power and resources at the disposal of the state for empowerment of citizens and their overall development shall be the priority of this plan.",""],[1,"154","1","Mainstreaming of Indigenous Peoples Policies and Special Measures","Nepal has ratified or adopted these documents and has subsequently been implementing policies, special measures and programs contained therein.",""],[1,"155","3","Policy, Legal, and Institutional Reform Measures for Social Inclusion","there are various constitutional commissions related to empowerment and social inclusion which are involved in effective implementation of the issues of target groups through policy, legal and institutional reform measures.",""],[1,"156","3","Target Group Participation and Inclusive Governance Mainstreaming","Increase leadership and participation of target groups and communities by enhancing coordination, collaboration and partnership of federal, provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"157","4","Mainstreaming and Localization of Gender Equality and Social Inclusion","Internalize, mainstream and localize the concerns of these groups and communities by reflecting them in policies, laws, plans and programs and institutional structures.",""],[1,"157","5","Basic Empowerment, Inclusion, and Mobilization Programs","Implement basic programs of empowerment, inclusion and mobilization based on affiliation, coherence and complementarity with the policies and priorities of the local level.",""],[1,"157","5","Proportional Inclusion in State Institutions","Adopt the strategy of proportional inclusion in all levels and bodies of the state based on demographic ratio and ability.",""],[1,"157","5","Gender Empowerment, Disability, and Social Inclusion Mainstreaming","Adopt the strategy of 'gender empowerment, disability and social inclusion' in every process of development.",""],[1,"157","5","Phasewise Comprehensive Empowerment Package","Manage a complete package of empowerment in a phasewise manner, taking into account factors like identity of target",""],[1,"159","6","Positive Discrimination Policy for Disadvantaged Ethnic Groups and Communities","Adopt the policy of positive discrimination targeting certain ethnic tribes, groups and communities that are weak in",""],[1,"160","2","Governance Arrangements and Policy and Legal Reforms Program","Undertake amendments to relevant laws in the following issue domains: fundamental issues of target groups, communities and gender and safe motherhood and reproductive health; gender- based violence; curbing human trafficking and transportation; eliminating child labor; curbing sexual abuse; issues related to adolescents, and laws that show conflicts of interests in political representation.",""],[1,"163","3","Social Awakening and Awareness Campaign Program","Conduct social awareness campaigns and relevant programs against traditional harmful practices, social evils, corruption, violence and exclusion and discriminatory social and cultural values.",""],[1,"164","4","Indigenous Languages, Culture, Preservation and Promotion Programs","Launch special programs for preservation and promotion of indigenous languages, culture,",""],[1,"165","1","Protection and Promotion of Indigenous Languages","Protect and promote indigenous peoples and their languages which have reached on the verge of extinction.",""]],"45":[[1,"111","3","Teacher Provision for Core Subjects","Make available English, maths and science teachers.",""],[1,"111","3","School Extracurricular Activities Expansion","Conduct sports and arts as well as yoga and meditation as extracurricular activities right from school level.",""],[1,"111","5","Early Childhood Development and Education Program","Effectively implement program related to early childhood development and education down to the local level.",""],[1,"111","6","Implementation of the School Education Sector Plan 2022-32","Implement the School Education Sector Plan (2022-32).",""],[1,"111","6","School Internet Access Expansion","Ensure Internet access at all schools.",""],[1,"111","6","Principal and Teacher Professional Development Scheme","Carry out scheme for professional development of principals and teachers.",""],[1,"111","6","Student-Teacher Ratio Review and Subject Teacher Staffing Provision","Review student- teacher ratio and make sure that provision for minimum positions for subject teachers is",""],[1,"112","1","Direct Entry Pathway for Talented University Graduates into Teaching","Make provision for direct entry of talented university students into the teaching profession.",""],[1,"112","1","School Consolidation and Residential School Arrangement","Consolidate schools in consideration of number of students and geographical distance; make arrangement for residential school according to need.",""]],"46":[[1,"102","1","Strengthen Monitoring and Supervision of Technical Schools","Make monitoring and supervision of technical schools effective.",""],[1,"113","1","Technical and Vocational Education Program","Technical and vocational education program: Restructure the Technical and Vocational Education Council to suit the federal structure.",""]],"47":[[1,"105","5","Research-Focused Higher Education Specialization","Make higher education an area of specialization with focus on research.",""],[1,"105","5","Distance Learning System Development","Using modern technology, prioritize and develop a system of distance learning so that students from remote areas and those from abroad can also study.",""],[1,"111","3","Provincial University Consolidation Reform","bring all the universities and their campuses under the umbrella of one university in each provincial setting.",""],[1,"111","3","University Competitiveness Enhancement","Make universities competitive.",""],[1,"111","3","Higher Education Research Linkage Initiative","Link higher education with research.",""],[1,"112","1","Non-formal Education and Lifelong Learning Arrangements","Make arrangements for non-formal education and lifelong learning.",""],[1,"112","1","Mainstreaming Traditional Education Institutions","For production of virtuous human resources, mainstream traditional education like Gurukul, Ashram, Gumba, Madrasa.",""],[1,"112","3","Higher Education Reform Program","Higher education reform program: To make higher education internationally competitive, carry out reforms in curriculum and management.",""],[1,"113","6","University Restructuring Program","University restructuring program: Restructure universities in accordance with the spirit of federalism in order to maintain quality and academic calender in higher education.",""],[1,"113","8","University Grants Commission Structural Transformation","Transform the University Grants Commission in the form of Higher Education Commission to raise quality of higher education as per the call of time.",""]],"48":[[1,"105","5","Education Sector Investment Expansion","Increase investment in the education sector at all levels.",""],[1,"105","5","Student Facilitation Programmes","Implement student facilitation programs such as day meals and scholarships under integrated system.",""],[1,"105","5","Higher Education Cost-Sharing and Resource Mobilization","Adopt policy of cost partnership in higher education and mobilize, inter alia, resources of the private sector, development partners and non-resident Nepalis also in education.",""],[1,"105","5","Research and Development Budget Allocation","Ensure that 2 percent of the total budget will be spent on research and development by the end of the plan period.",""],[1,"113","5","Foreign Student Attraction Program","Program to attract foreign students: Come to a program to attract foreign students to study in Nepal by setting certain standards.",""],[1,"113","5","Foreign Investment Prioritization in Education","Give priority to foreign investment in education.",""]],"49":[[1,"104","5","Educational Policy and Institutional Reform Package","Bring out necessary policies, laws, guidelines, procedures and standards for educational reforms.",""],[1,"104","5","Education Quality and Outcome Improvement Initiative","Increase educational outcome at all levels, reduce the growing trend of going abroad for higher education by making the education system of Nepal qualitative, productive and employment-oriented.",""],[1,"104","5","Education Governance Roles Rationalization","Based on the organization and management survey, remove the ambiguity and duplication of roles between different agencies.",""],[1,"105","2","Educational Calendar and School Supervision System","Develop and implement educational calendar, make institutional arrangements for supervision, monitoring and inspection of educational institutions.",""],[1,"105","2","Intergovernmental Education Coordination Mechanism","Ensure coordination and collaboration between the three levels of government in supervision and monitoring.",""],[1,"105","2","Education Human Resource Mapping and Adjustment","Ensure management of minimum human resource required at educational institution by mapping and adjusting.",""],[1,"105","2","Integrated Education Information System Strengthening","Strengthen integrated educational information system to strengthen the monitoring and reporting system.",""],[1,"106","1","Educational Governance and Assessment Reform","Make effective national test of student achievement, reading and maths skills test, and early learning and development level test and the performance test of educational agencies and educational institutions.",""],[1,"111","6","School Education Reform Program","School education reform program: Formulate an umbrella legislation to ensure inter-linkages and quality in all three levels of education system.",""],[1,"112","1","Local-Level Teacher Support and School Supervision System","Manage teacher support system and school supervision through the local level.",""],[1,"112","1","Intergovernmental Coordination for Compulsory and Free Education Act Implementation","Enhance coordination and collaboration between the three levels of government for implementation of the Compulsory and Free Education Act.",""]],"50":[[1,"94","3","Youth Mobilization Programme in Nation Building","Conduct \"Youth Mobilization Programme in Nation Building\" to mobilize youth force and enhance their capacity.",""],[1,"106","6","Youth Character and Civic Values Development Initiative","Develop nationalism, morality, discipline, pride for local culture, voluntary spirit and good manners among the youths.",""],[1,"107","1","Youth Participation and Capacity Development Initiative","Increase meaningful participation of the youths in policy making at all levels.",""],[1,"107","1","Youth Volunteer Program","Launch volunteer program.",""],[1,"115","2","Youth Internship and Volunteerism Mobilization Programme","Youth mobilization through programs such as internships and volunteerism.",""],[1,"115","2","Youth Social Activism Mobilization Initiative","mobilizing youths as social activists.",""],[1,"115","2","Scouts and National Cadet Corps Strengthening","Enhance the effectiveness of Scouts and National Cadet Corps.",""]],"51":[[1,"70","1","Energy Transmission and Distribution Expansion","install and expand necessary transmission and distribution lines for produced electricity and increase domestic consumption as well as export; utilize new sources and opportunities of renewable energy.",""],[1,"71","3","One-Door Hydropower Investment Facilitation System","Adopt a one-door system of investment facilitation in hydropower sector to increase power generation and raise level of production and productivity.",""],[1,"71","3","Energy Sector Concessions","Make provision of concessions in the energy sector.",""],[1,"71","3","Environmental Assessment and Land Acquisition Simplification","Introduce facilitative measures and procedural simplification in environmental assessment studies and land acquisition.",""],[1,"71","3","Non-Resident Nepali Investment Mobilization","Attract investment from non-resident Nepalis.",""],[1,"71","3","Independent Power Producer Empowerment","Empower independent power producers.",""],[1,"71","3","Electric Equipment Subsidy and Concession Scheme","provide subsidies and concessions in the use of electric equipment.",""],[1,"71","3","Transmission and Distribution System Upgrade","Upgrade transmission and distribution systems.",""],[1,"71","3","Private Sector Participation in Energy Trading Law","Make legal provisions for private sector participation in energy trading.",""],[1,"71","3","Hydropower Reservoir and Multipurpose Project Development","Build reservoirs and multi-purpose projects in the hydropower sector.",""],[1,"71","3","Industrial Corridor Power Distribution Service Expansion","Ensure regular and quality distribution service for development and expansion of industrial corridors.",""]],"52":[[1,"45","1","Hydropower Production Expansion and Electricity Export Growth","It is estimated that with a significant increase in hydropower production, there will be a corresponding high increase in the consumption and use of electricity by all sectors of the economy, and there will be a gradual increase in the amount of electricity export.",""],[1,"69","3","Electricity Production and Consumption Investment Mobilization","Ensure adequate investment to produce sustainable and quality energy.",""],[1,"78","4","Hydropower Development and Expansion Program","18) Hydropower development and expansion program: Increase government investment for the development and expansion of the energy sector.",""],[1,"123","4","Hydroelectric Power Development Expansion","It is necessary to develop and expand hydroelectric power according to the hydropower master plan being formulated by the Water and Energy Commission.","Water and Energy Commission"],[1,"126","4","Electricity Generation, Transmission and Distribution Expansion","Make arrangements for maximum use of electricity in economic development through generation, transmission and distribution of electricity in proportion to the current and future annual electricity demand growth rate.",""],[1,"126","4","Electricity Export and Power Trade Promotion","After meeting domestic electricity demand, export surplus electricity as a commodity by promoting power trade at bilateral, sub-regional and regional markets.",""],[1,"126","4","International Power Trade Infrastructure Development","Also build necessary structures for intenational power trade.",""],[1,"129","6","Sustainable Power Infrastructure Development","Developing sustainable infrastructure for power generation, transmission, consumption and trade: Increase domestic access to and demand for energy.",""],[1,"130","1","Energy Diplomacy for Green Energy Financing","Conduct energy diplomacy to utlize green energy as a tool for mobilizing financial resources.",""],[1,"130","1","Reservoir-Type and Multipurpose Hydropower Projects","In order to balance demand and supply of power during the dry season, develop reservoir type and multipurpose projects as transformative projects for increasing production.",""],[1,"133","4","Investment Mobilization for Reservoir-Dam Hydropower and Transmission Lines","Program for mobilization of investment for reservoir-dam projects and international transmission lines:",""],[1,"133","5","People's Hydropower Program","People's hydropower program: For sustainable and reliable development of hydropower, develop projects of national importance such as Chainpur-Seti hydropower project, Tamakoshi fifth hydropower project, Ghunsakhola hydropower project, Simbuwakhola hydropower project, etc. through participation of the people and the use of remittances received from non-resident Nepalis and foreign employment.",""]],"53":[[1,"71","3","Renewable Energy Promotion Initiative","Promote renewable energy sources such as solar and wind energy.",""],[1,"78","5","Renewable Energy Promotion Program","Renewable energy promotion program: Increase the share of renewable energy in total energy mix.",""],[1,"79","1","Renewable Energy Generation and Fossil Fuel Substitution","Generate power from sources like solar, wind and hydrogen.",""],[1,"126","4","Alternative Energy Expansion and Community Ownership","Make sustainable use and expansion of alternative energy, ensure technology transfer and establish community ownership; lower carbon emissions by raising the consumption of alternative energy.",""],[1,"129","6","Fossil Fuel Subsidy Reduction and Electricity Demand Incentives","In order to bring down consumption of petroleum products and L.P.G. gas, and as a way of import substitution, gradually reduce subsidies provided on these commodities.",""],[1,"129","6","Alternative Energy Promotion and Master Planning","Encourage alternative energy (other than hydropower) such as solar energy, wind energy, hydrogen energy and other energy mix, and prepare a master plan in this respect for implementation",""],[1,"130","1","Green Energy Roadmap and Action Plan","Attach priority to green energy for promotion of green economy and develop roadmap and action plan for implementation.",""],[1,"137","15","Biogas Plant Installation and Waste-to-Energy Generation","Installation of institutional, community, urban and commercial biogas plants and energy generation from waste",""],[1,"226","1","Electric Cooking and LPG Subsidy Rationalization","Encourage the use of electric stoves, while reducing the existing subsidy on L.P.G.",""],[1,"226","1","Electric Vehicle Promotion in Public Transport","Continue to promote electric vehicles to increase electricity consumption.",""],[1,"226","1","Time-of-Use Electricity Tariff Reform","determine electricity charges based on time and consumption to increase consumption during lean hours.",""],[1,"226","1","Groundwater Green Tax","Impose a green tax on commercial users of groundwater.",""]],"54":[[1,"70","2","Integrated Infrastructure Development and Maintenance","Based on need forecasting, build infrastructure for production and productivity growth.",""],[1,"73","2","Rural-Urban Transport and Transit Linkage Expansion","Shorten time and space to increase production and productivity; connect sectors of production with markets by expanding transport and transit facilities.",""],[1,"73","2","Rural-Urban Transport and Communication Connectivity Improvement","Increase transport and communication links to maintain balance and coordination between rural and urban economies.",""],[1,"78","2","Multimodal Transport System Development Program","Make policy and regulatory provisions for development of multimodal transport system based on integrated transport plan.",""],[1,"78","2","National Highway Construction and Expansion Program","Construct and expand highways that link national cities, provincial capitals and economic centers.",""],[1,"78","2","Mid-Hill, North-South Highway, and Industrial Corridor Construction Program","Carry out program of building mid-hill highway, North-South highway, industrial corridors.",""],[1,"121","3","Transport Infrastructure Policy, Regulation, and Program Implementation","In order to make transport infrastructure sector organized, policies, regulations and programs are being implemented.",""],[1,"121","3","Strategic Roads Network Project","Among national pride and transformative projects which have been ongoing include strategic roads network, East-",""],[1,"122","2","Priority Tunnel Road Development","In view of Nepal's difficult geographic terrains, tunnel roads should fall under priority for safe and reliable transport.",""],[1,"122","2","Siddhababa and Tokha-Chhare Tunnel Road Projects","Siddhababa tunnel road and Tokha-Chhare tunnel road projects are under construction.",""],[1,"128","4","Transport Infrastructure Expansion and Modernization","Expand structures such as roads with modern and innovative technologies, bridges, tunnels, flyovers, underpasses and other means of alternative transport.",""],[1,"129","5","National Highway and Strategic Road Expansion","For expansion of national highways and strategic roads, amend and integrate relevant laws related to infrastruture development and make this sector sustainable and productive.",""],[1,"132","1","Integrated Transport System Development Program","Integrated transport system development program: Develop an integrated transport system in Kathmandu Valley and manage modern and affordable means of transport.",""],[1,"132","3","Integrated Public Transport System through Public-Private Partnership","Operate an integrated public transport system through public-private partnership and coordination.",""],[1,"132","3","Electric Bus and Alternative Transport Services in Major Cities","In big cities including the Kathmandu valley (river corridors, inner and outer ring roads), operate electric buses or alternative means of transport services in collaboration with provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"132","3","Hetauda-Kathmandu Ropeway Modernization and Operation","Modernize and operate the Hetauda-Kathmandu ropeway.",""],[1,"132","3","Pokhara-Kathmandu Rapid Transport Infrastructure","Build infrastructure for Pokhara-Kathmandu rapid transport service.",""],[1,"132","3","Nijgadh International Airport Expansion","Expand Nijgadh international airport and its related access routes and proceed with the work with business plan.",""],[1,"132","3","Siddhababa and Other Proposed Tunnel Road Construction","Carry out construction of Siddhababa tunnel and other proposed tunnel roads such as Hemza-Nayapul, Bhirkate-Kaligandaki, Leuti-Dharan, Daunne, Malekhu-Lothar, where feasibility study has been done.",""],[1,"150","1","Strategic Urban Roads Construction and Expansion","Construction and expansion of strategic urban roads",""],[1,"150","3","Strategic Bus Park Construction","Construction of bus park with strategic importance",""]],"55":[[1,"126","1","Air Transport Safety and Accessibility Improvement","Make air transport safe, regular, affordable and accessible.",""],[1,"126","1","International Confidence Building for Air Transport Sector","Gain more confidence of the international community on the entire air transport sector.",""],[1,"126","1","Nepal Airlines Corporation Service Upgrade","Develop Nepal Airlines Corporation as a service provider of international reputation.",""],[1,"133","3","National Flag Carrier Service Expansion and Reliability Enhancement Program","For expansion of services and facilities in the air service sector, look at the pressure on increased demand and continue adding latest technologies that conform to the international standards of aviation infrastructure development.",""]],"56":[[1,"122","3","Bardiwas-Simara Railway Track Construction","Railway track is being constructed on Bardiwas-Simara section.",""],[1,"128","4","Railway and Waterway Development for Trade Access","To increase access for transport and trade, develop railways and waterways so as to contribute to the national economy.",""],[1,"128","4","Waterway Infrastructure for Tourism Promotion","Develop structures for waterways for tourism promotion and potential growth in the economy by promoting tourism through the development of railway services and water transport to expand access to transport and trade.",""],[1,"128","4","Waterway and Ropeway Governance Reform","Make policy, legal and institutional reforms for safe and reliable management of waterways and ropeways based on potential.",""]],"57":[[1,"123","6","Digital Nepal Framework Implementation","Digital Nepal Framework is being implemented effectively with the objective of building digital infrastructure.",""],[1,"126","5","Digital Ecosystem Development","Build a digital ecosystem for development, expansion and use of reliable, safe, sustainable and accessible modern communication and information technology.",""],[1,"126","5","Interconnection of Information Technology Systems","Maintain interconnections between information technology systems.",""],[1,"126","5","Telecommunication Infrastructure Expansion","Make telecommunication services easy, accessible and qualitative by developing, expanding and co-using telecommunication infrastructure.",""],[1,"126","5","National Satellite Procurement","Procure Nepal's own satellite.",""],[1,"134","2","5G and Broadband Expansion Program","Adopt and expand 5G and broadband connection to increase speed, capacity and agility.",""],[1,"134","2","High-Capacity Digital Platforms Development","Build and operate high-capacity platforms.",""],[1,"134","2","IT Skills Development and Youth Support Initiative","Produce skilled human resources in information technology by increasing opportunities for studies, training and expanding practical knowledge in this area.",""],[1,"134","2","ICT Hub Development Initiative","Develop Nepal into an information and communication technology hub.",""],[1,"134","3","Digital Nepal Framework Implementation Program","Digital Nepal Framework implementation program: Carry out necessary update and mdification in the infrastructure projects under the Digital Nepal Framework and build a digital ecosystem.",""],[1,"134","3","Digital Transformation Project Development and Priority Implementation","Develop necessary digital transformation projects in the information technology sector, prepare a classified list in the national project bank and implement them on a priority basis.",""],[1,"134","5","Specialized Information Technology Services Program","Provide specialized information technology services including digital forensics, data protection, data processing, technology testing, electronic signature, system development, consulting services and cloud services in an integrated manner.",""],[1,"134","5","Technology Research Hub for Communication and Information Technology","Create a technology research hub to explore, research, develop and innovate the latest technologies developed in the field of communication and information technology and to promote investment in this field by enhancing collaboration and partnership with universities, educational institutions and the private sector.",""],[1,"134","5","Capacity Development for Public Representatives and IT Human Resources","Enhance the capacity of people's representatives, employees and information technology-related human resources at the federal, provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"135","1","Telecommunication Infrastructure Management and Co-utilization Program","Identify the radio frequency spectrum needed for the development and expansion of wireless broadband services, and establish and operate Nepal's own geo-satellite during the plan period.",""],[1,"135","4","Postal Infrastructure Restructuring and Transformation Program","Implement \"One Local Level, One Smart Post\" program by managing existing postal service infrastructure and assets and linking them with the local level.",""]],"58":[[1,"53","5","Digital Governance and Economic Modernization Initiative","For this, adoption of modern and latest technology including information technology and electronic governance, along with mechanization and modernization of the economy, in sectors such as education, health, human capital formation, agriculture, industry and forestry, is necessary.",""],[1,"73","5","Information Technology Adoption for Production Efficiency","Emphasis on the use of information technology: increase the use of modern information technology for raising the capacity and efficiency of the means of production.",""],[1,"80","1","Information Technology Infrastructure Development and Expansion","Development and expansion of infrastructure for information technology for raising efficiency of means of production such as labour, land and capital.",""],[1,"80","1","Information Technology Adoption for Sectoral Productivity","For raising productivity of sectoral production cycle and substantive areas with forward and backward linkage that have links with production, ensure use of information technology.",""],[1,"207","3","Integrated E-Governance System Development","Develop a system to collect information in an integrated manner instead of collecting the same type of information repeatedly.",""],[1,"207","3","Interagency IT and Database Interlinkage","Establish interlink between information technology and database systems used by various agencies.",""],[1,"207","3","Public Service Work Culture Improvement","Develop a work culture that provides sustainable and reliable services.",""],[1,"207","3","IT and Cybersecurity System Strengthening","Strengthen the existing information technology system from the point of view of technical and cyber security.",""],[1,"207","3","Functional and Institutional E-Governance Expansion","Develop and expand functional and institutional e-governance.",""],[1,"209","2","Digital Public Service Delivery Improvement","Improve the quality of service delivery by making the best use of electronic means and new technologies.",""],[1,"211","4","E-Governance Policy and Legal Arrangements","Maintain e-governance in all aspects of governance by making policy and legal arrangements.",""],[1,"211","4","Citizen E-Governance Familiarization Program","Plan and implement a program to familiarize common citizens with the electronic system.",""],[1,"212","2","Public Service Delivery Quality Improvement Program","Program for improvement of quality of public service delivery: Make public service and personnel administration related to service delivery more people-centric and results- oriented by formulating a special public service performance law.",""],[1,"215","3","Customer-Friendly Public Service Delivery System","Ensure development and implementation of faceless and cashless system using modern information system in service delivery.",""],[1,"215","3","Alternative Public Service Delivery Tools","Use new alternative tools for public service delivery.",""],[1,"215","3","Public Personnel Capacity and Motivation Reform","Build a responsible, motivated and loyal personnel system to enhance creativity and efficiency in performance.",""],[1,"226","2","E-Governance Expansion and IT Industry Promotion","Expand electronic governance in government processes and promote information technology industries.",""]],"59":[[1,"124","2","National Cyber Security Center","With the enforcement of National Cyber Security Policy, 2023, a National Cyber Security Center has been established.",""],[1,"124","2","Separate Cyber Security Legislation","there is a need to enact a separate legislation to regulate this sector.",""],[1,"126","5","Safe and Resilient Cyberspace Initiative","Build a safe and resilient cyberspace.",""],[1,"131","1","Cybersecurity and Data Protection Strengthening","Upgrade and strengthen information technology and ensure security of electronic data.",""],[1,"131","1","Data Protection Legal and Institutional Reform","Create a safe and resilient cyberspace and enact necessary laws related to data protection, make collection, storage, protection and use of data effective.",""],[1,"134","2","Cybersecurity and Data Protection Measures","Enforce strong measures for cyber security and data protection.",""],[1,"134","4","Government Data Security and Safe Cyber Space Program","Government data security, safe cyber space and digital platform development program: For establishment and effective operation of data centers and disaster recovery centers in the government and private sectors, make arrangements for necessary policy and institutions.",""],[1,"134","4","Digital Platform Development Project for Public Service Integration","Implement digital platform development project to integrate information technology systems and electronic services related to public service delivery.",""],[1,"134","4","National Cyber Security Center and Safe Cyber Space Laws","Formulate necessary laws for safe cyber space and operate national cyber security center.",""]],"60":[[1,"124","2","Integrated Electronic Public Service Delivery System","An integrated electronic system has been implemented to promote paperless public service delivery.",""],[1,"124","2","Citizen App One-Door Service Platform","The number of government services associated with citizen Apps, which was developed with the objective of developing a one-door service system, has reached 62.",""],[1,"126","5","Digital Public Service Delivery Expansion","Enhance multi-use of information technology in public service delivery.",""],[1,"128","2","Digital Transformation Policy and Legal Framework","Internalize communication and information technology as an inter-related field and make necessary policy and legal arrangements to lay the groundwork for digital transformation.",""],[1,"130","6","Digital Ecosystem for Public Service Delivery","Make public service delivery sustainable, reliable and simplified by building a digital ecosystem in the communication and information technology sector; maintain interlinkages between systems.",""],[1,"130","6","One-Door State and Citizen Data Management System","Manage data and information through a one-door system by centralizing all accounts of the state and citizens.",""],[1,"176","2","Rural Electronic Governance Connectivity Expansion","Promote electronic governance by strengthening access to the Internet, radio and television in remote areas.",""]],"61":[[1,"145","2","Regional and Urban Spatial Planning and Strategic Investment","make it managed and effective through regional and urban spatial planning and strategic investments.",""],[1,"145","2","Rural-Urban Integration and Connectivity Strengthening","Make backward areas competitive by strengthening rural-urban integration and inter-connectivity and consolidation of regional relations.",""],[1,"145","2","Major City Economic Center Development","Develop the country's major cities, including the provincial capitals, as major economic centers.",""],[1,"145","2","Managed Residential Development and Transport-Centered Urban Planning","Encourage managed residential development, putting transportation at the centrestage.",""],[1,"145","2","Integrated Settlement Development and Squatter Settlement Management","Develop integrated settlement, relocate at-risk settlement and manage squatter settlements.",""],[1,"145","4","Urban Infrastructure Investment Roadmap","Identify and prioritize projects that can accrue maximum social and economic outcomes, as well as transformative urban infrastructure, and prepare a roadmap for multisectoral investments.",""],[1,"145","4","Urban Infrastructure Financing Mobilization","Mobilize grants as well as other alternative sources of finance for urban infrastructure development.",""],[1,"145","4","Urban Infrastructure Technology Integration","Internalize technologies based on innovation for construction and development of urban infrastructure.",""],[1,"145","4","Urban Planning and Technical Staffing Support","Provide human resource such as architect, city planners and other expert technicians at the federal, provincial and local levels as needed.",""],[1,"146","2","National and Provincial Urban Systems Strengthening","Strengthening the national and provincial urban systems: Interlink and integrate national, provincial and local towns and urban systems.",""],[1,"146","4","Alternative Financing for Urban Infrastructure Development","For construction and development of urban infrastructure, mobilize financial resources through alternative financial instruments, such as loans and grants, mixed financing, co-financing, green finance investment, blended finance and public-private partnership investments.",""],[1,"146","4","Legal Framework for Urban Infrastructure Implementation","Prepare a clear legal framework for implementation",""],[1,"147","1","Urban Traffic Regulation and Environment-Friendly Public Transport Development","To control and regulate traffic pressure and environmental pollution, use the latest technology of the public urban transport system and build relevant structures.",""],[1,"147","1","Urban Infrastructure Project Management","Manage urban infrastructure projects and develop environment-friendly urban transport system.",""],[1,"147","3","Strategic Town Development Program","Original and strategic town development program: Develop provincial capitals as towns with major economic centers.",""],[1,"147","3","Provincial Cultural City Development Initiative","Build an original and model city that reflects the local and indigenous culture and civilization in each of the seven provinces, keeping features such as open parks, museums, entertainment venues and commercial buildings, etc.",""],[1,"147","4","Model Rural Settlement Development Program","Model settlement development program: Develop systematic model rural settlements.",""],[1,"147","4","Heritage Settlement Record and Preservation Policy","Take policy initiatives to keep records of heritage settlements at the national, provincial and local levels and ensure their preservation and promotion.",""],[1,"147","4","Dense Heritage Settlement Preservation and Development","Pay attention to preservation and development of dense settlements with original heritage.",""],[1,"147","5","Integrated Urban Infrastructure Development","Bring reforms in the existing intensive urban development program to attract strategic investments based on spatial planning for the construction of integrated (physical, social, economic) infrastructure in cities.",""],[1,"147","5","Urban Utility Corridor Policy Initiative","Take policy initiatives to develop integrated urban infrastructure (utility corridors) in big cities.",""],[1,"147","5","Urban Regeneration and Residential Area Improvement","Improve residential areas and urban regeneration based on community land contributions.",""],[1,"147","5","Modern Bus Park Construction","Build bus parks based on modern technology.",""],[1,"148","1","Rural-Urban Integration and Inter-Connectivity Program","Rural-urban integration and inter-connectivity program: Connect all local level centers with paved road network.",""],[1,"148","2","Landless and Squatters Settlements Management Program","Landless and squatters settlements management program: identify geographically vulnerable settlements and relocate them.",""],[1,"148","3","New Town Planning and Expansion Programme","Carry out mid-term review of the new town projects and continue planned development and expansion of potential locations.",""],[1,"148","3","Legalization and Reform of New Town Projects","Transform such projects into planned urban and settlement development projects by providing them legal status, capacity building support and mobilization of increased investments, and functional reforms.",""],[1,"150","6","Government Office Building Retrofitting and New Construction","Retrofitting and new construction of government office buildings",""],[1,"173","2","Migration Policy Formulation and Settlement Planning","Assess the trends and nature of internal migration and formulate migration policies based on geographic location and demographic density, linking them to economic activities.",""],[1,"173","2","Integrated Settlement Development Programme","Promote integrated settlement development to reduce the pressure and cost of increasing needs for service and infrastructure triggered by unbalanced internal and external migration, scattered human settlements and unorganized urbanization.",""],[1,"173","2","Urbanization Management through Corridor and Cluster Development","development based on corridors and clusters to manage urbanization.",""],[1,"176","3","Rural-Urban Economic Linkage Promotion","Promote inter-linkages of rural-urban economy: Expand economic, social, cultural and commercial inter-linkages necessary for the development of partnership in the economic activities of rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"176","3","Rural-Urban Connectivity and Production Linkage Strengthening","Strengthen rural-urban linkage by maintaining rural-urban inter-connection between urban infrastructure and facilities and means of rural production and productivity.",""],[1,"176","3","Village-City Partnership and Local Harmony Initiative","Promote village-city partnership by maintaining inter-local level and ward and local level harmony.",""],[1,"176","3","Corridor and Cluster-Based Settlement Development","Promote intensive development of settlement and development of model based on corridors and clusters.",""]],"62":[[1,"124","3","Sustainable and Inclusive Infrastructure Development","While constructing and utilizing infrastructure, emphasis has been placed on making it sustainable, resilient, environment- friendly and inclusive without causing any harm to natural resources like water, land and forests.",""],[1,"127","1","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Planning","Adopt climate resilience in infrastructure planning process.",""],[1,"127","5","Systematic Urban Infrastructure Planning and Development","Ensure building urban infrastructure in a systematic and planned manner.",""],[1,"129","4","Circular Economy Infrastructure Development","implement economic, social, physical and natural infrastructure development activities through circular economy.",""],[1,"131","4","Circular Economy Housing and Urban Infrastructure Development","For development of modern urban and rural settlements, develop necessary infrastructure based on circular economy in a gender-sensitive, child-friendly, senior citizen and disabled-friendly manner.",""],[1,"146","3","Urban Spatial Planning and Development Regulation Reform","include spatial planning system in the Integrated Urban Development Act.",""],[1,"146","3","Integrated Urban and Settlement Planning Legal Reform","Incorporate land use and physical development regulation, land and financial instruments, and integrated urban infrastructure into the Integrated Urban and Settlement Planning Act.",""],[1,"146","3","Urban Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Adaptation Mainstreaming","Internalize disaster risk reduction and climate adaptation activities.",""],[1,"146","3","Urban Agriculture Promotion Initiative","Promote urban agriculture.",""],[1,"146","3","Urban Riverfront Environmental Improvement and Public Space Protection","Improve and beautify the environment of rivers and riverbanks, documenting, protecting and promoting public open spaces around them.",""],[1,"146","3","Urban Rainwater Harvesting and Groundwater Recharge System","promote rain harvest and other water collection technologies and recharge of underground water at regional, settlement, community and household levels so as to develop sustainable urban water management infrastructure.",""],[1,"146","3","Urban Security and Inclusive Community Safety Framework","Guarantee urban security for promotion of lively and resilient communities.",""],[1,"146","3","Comprehensive Urban Crime Prevention and Emergency Response System","Integrate comprehensive crime prevention strategy, robust emergency response system and inclusive infrastructure design to create an urban environment that is safe, accessible and favourable for all residents.",""],[1,"146","3","Urban Road Safety, Fire Prevention, and Building Code Compliance Measures","Reduce traffic accidents, prevent disasters such as fire, ensure compliance with building codes, keep electronic records of houses and street numbers.",""],[1,"149","4","Urban Environment Improvement, Safety and Disaster Resilience Program","13) Urban environment improvement, safety and disaster resilience program: For disaster risk reduction, carry out contemporary reforms in landuse planning and construction standards and building code, and regulate physical development activities.",""],[1,"150","4","Housing Construction for Target Groups and Disaster-Displaced Households","Construction of housing for target groups and disasters displaced households",""]],"63":[[1,"208","2","Investigation and Prosecution System Reform and Capacity Development","Make reforms and develop capacity in the investigation and prosecution system in view of complexities and new forms and dimensions of corruption.",""],[1,"208","2","Judicial System Institutional Improvement","Ensure institutional improvement of the judicial system and enhancement of judicial competence.",""],[1,"208","2","Legislative Bill Formulation Capacity Enhancement","Increase capacity for formulation of bills for legislation in all levels of government.",""],[1,"208","2","Free Legal Aid Provision","Provide free legal aid to the indigent parties.",""],[1,"208","2","Access to Justice Expansion","Increase simple and easy access to justice for all to make the legal regime effective with the promotion of human rights and fundamental rights, and ensuring their unrestricted use.",""],[1,"209","3","Legal Infrastructure and Rule of Law Strengthening","Establish the rule of law through creation of necessary legal infrastructure and compliance with the law, and bring about changes in leadership behavior and trends.",""],[1,"209","3","Good Governance and Justice-Based Legal System Reform","Strengthen the level of good governance in political, administrative, judicial and other fields by establishing a legal system based on justice, logic and foresight.",""],[1,"209","3","Artificial Intelligence and Digital Governance Law Reform","Formulate and implement laws related to artificial intelligence and digital governance to address new dimensions of development.",""],[1,"210","3","Judicial System Reform and Digitization","Reforming the judicial system: Ensure justice for all by making the judicial process simple, predictable, accountable, transparent and IT-friendly.",""],[1,"212","3","Rule of Law Assurance Program","Rule of law assurance program: Draft, formulate and amend necessary laws in accordance with the verdicts and statutory directives of the Supreme Court, the decisions and recommendations of the National Human Rights Commission as well as the Commission for the Investigation of Abuse of Authority and other constitutional commissions.",""],[1,"212","3","Legal Harmonization for International Treaty Implementation","Draft, revise and implement laws necessary for implementation of international treaties, conventions, agreements and declarations to which Nepal is a party.",""],[1,"212","3","State Organs Strengthening Against Impunity","Strengthen and consolidate all organs of the state to end state of impunity.",""],[1,"212","3","AI for Legal Governance","Extend the use of artificial intelligence to the realm of legal governance.",""],[1,"212","3","Local Judicial Committees and Legal Aid Cells","Ensure empowerment of local level judicial committees and establishment of legal aid cells.",""],[1,"213","5","Judicial Administration Strengthening Program","Program for strengthening the judicial administration system: Expand free legal aid and legal literacy to make the justice system fast, efficient and reliable.",""],[1,"214","1","Judicial Committee Strengthening and Case Management Digitization","Provide necessary resources to make the judicial committee of the local level effective, and raise efficiency of the personnel.",""],[1,"214","1","Judicial Personnel Training and Orientation Programme","Provide adequate training and orientation to judicial personnel.",""],[1,"214","1","Dispute Resolution Through Conciliation","Facilitate sustainable resolution of disputes through conciliation.",""],[1,"214","1","Court Record Management Digitization","Make optimum use of information technology for court record management.",""]],"64":[[1,"38","4","Skills Deployment and Technology Alignment for the Labour Force","Deploy and utilize skilled manpower according to modern technology and market demand.",""],[1,"38","4","Returnee Migrant and Non-Resident Nepalese Economic Integration Programme","Integrate into national mainstream skills, technology, entrepreneurship, and confidence of the returnee migrant workers as well as the investment of non-resident Nepalese.",""],[1,"85","1","Private Sector Employment and Decent Work Measures","For this, it is necessary to take a number of measures, including development of the private sector for secure employment and working environment, sufficient wages for a living, equal pay for equal work, social protection, promotion of harmonious industrial relations, respect for labor and workers, end of all forms of labor exploitation, labor rights and standardization and occupational safety and health standards.",""],[1,"86","2","Domestic Employment Promotion","For this, strategies and programs that are being implemented include promotion of domestic employment, bringing to an end compulsion for foreign employment and making it safe and dignified, expansion of contribution-based social security and raising productivity through skill development.",""],[1,"88","1","Domestic Employment Creation Campaigns","Launch employment campaigns to mainstram internal employment creation in sectoral policies.",""],[1,"88","1","Private-Sector Collaboration for Domestic Production Expansion","Expand Nepali production in collaboration with the private sector.",""],[1,"88","1","Multi-Level Employment and Self-Employment Partnerships","develop collaboration and partnerships among governments at various levels, the private sector, cooperatives and non-governmental organizations in creation of opportunities for employment and self-employment in sectors including agriculture.",""],[1,"88","1","Intergovernmental Job Creation Coordination","Develop intensive collaboration between the federal, provincial and local governments in job creation.",""],[1,"88","1","Youth Entrepreneurship Innovation and Start-Up Capital Support","Provide innovation and start-up capital to encourage youth entrepreneurship and self- employment.",""],[1,"88","1","Access to Finance and Technology Expansion","Increase access to finance and technology.",""],[1,"88","1","Agricultural Pocket Area Employment Development","Emphasize on pocket areas development to create employment in the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"90","3","Intergovernmental Coordination for Job Creation and Management","Ensure reaching out to the target group by maintaining coordination and inter-connection between the federal, provincial and local levels in job creation and management.",""],[1,"90","3","Clarification of Labor and Employment Responsibilities","Delineate areas of responsibilities of the federal, provincial and local levels in the field of labor and employment and avoid duplication of work.",""],[1,"90","3","Complementary Employment and Self-Employment Program Design","Expand opportunities for employment and self-employment by designing programs which will be complementary to progams run at various govenment levels.",""],[1,"90","4","Domestic Employment Promotion Package","Create sufficient opportunities for domestic employment: Mainstream employment issues in macroeconomic policy, monetary and fiscal policies and various sectoral policies as topic of strategic importance and set it as a priority.",""],[1,"92","4","National Employment Growth and Labor Market Support Program","Special program of employment growth within the country: Annul or restructure unproductive programs currently in operation.",""],[1,"92","4","Traditional Skills, Arts and Crafts Commercialization Initiative","Conservation and commercialization of traditional skills, arts and crafts.",""],[1,"93","1","Decade-Long Production and Employment Campaign","Launch a decade-long campaign for production and employment.",""],[1,"93","2","Integrated Entrepreneurship Development Model","In collaboration with the public, private and cooperative sectors, formulate and implement an integrated model of entrepreneurship development, product development and service delivery and marketing.",""],[1,"95","2","Special Job Creation Programmes for Poor and Unemployed Citizens","Conduct special programs related to job creation for the poor and unemployed citizens and special programs related to skills and entrepreneurship development for the unemployed to gain competence.",""],[1,"96","2","Migrant Resource Centers and Sub-centers","Establishment and management of Migrant Resource Centers/Sub-centers",""],[1,"101","4","Youth Self-Employment Promotion","Engage youths in self-employment.",""],[1,"105","5","Entrepreneurship Development Initiative","And develop entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"107","1","Youth Financial Access for Self-Employment","expand financial access to encourage their self- employment.",""],[1,"115","2","Entrepreneurial Leadership Development Initiative","Entrepreneurial leadership development;",""],[1,"187","3","Skills Development and Entrepreneurship Support","Maintain access to skills, technology and resources necessary to develop an entrepreneurial work culture.",""],[1,"187","3","Minimum Employment Guarantee and Fair Job Distribution","Ensure effective implementation of policies and plans to guarantee minimum employment to the unemployed and fair distribution of employment opportunities.",""],[1,"187","3","Agricultural Land Consolidation and Product Marketing Support","Reduce concentration of poverty in the agricultural sector, reduce fragmentation of arable land, utilize barren land properly and market agricultural products.",""],[1,"187","3","Inter-Sectoral Productive Employment Linkages","Create productive employment opportunities by maintaining inter-linkages between the primary, industry and service sectors.",""],[1,"187","6","Entrepreneurship Development for Target Households","Develop entrepreneurship among the target households through education,",""],[1,"188","2","Financial Inclusion and Income Generation Expansion","Expand income generation opportunities by enhancing financial awareness, financial access and financial inclusion.",""],[1,"188","2","Labor Participation and Fair Wage Policy Measures","Conduct programs to increase labor participation, and implement policies such as equal pay for equal work, minimum wage, etc.",""],[1,"188","4","Integrated Employment Information System","Develop an integrated employment information system and maintain citizens' access to employment information.",""],[1,"188","4","Workplace-Based Skills Development and Employment Policy","Adopt a workplace-based skills development and employment policy to support internal job creation and produce human resources required by the labor market.",""],[1,"188","4","Entrepreneurship and Start-Up Policy","Adopt entrepreneurship and start-up policies to create jobs by encouraging new and young entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"188","4","Agricultural Modernization and Commercialization Initiative","Attract youths in the agriculture sector by modernizing, commercializing, diversifying, industrializing and marketing this sector.",""],[1,"188","4","Micro, Domestic and Small Enterprise Promotion Measures","Make policy arrangements to promote micro, domestic and small enterprises.",""],[1,"188","4","Industrial Employment Expansion through Investment Attraction","Expand industrial employment opportunities by attracting domestic and foreign investment in the industrial sector.",""],[1,"188","4","Service Sector Employment Reform","Manage service-related employment in a better manner by introducing timely reforms in trade, tourism, information technology and other sectors.",""],[1,"189","3","Subsidized Seed Capital Loans for Poor Households","Through financial institutions, provide subsidized loans with seed capital to the identified poor to run business.",""],[1,"189","4","Skills and Entrepreneurship Development for Disadvantaged Areas","Develop skill and entrepreneurship development targeting the poor, disadvantaged and remote areas.",""],[1,"189","4","Agricultural Modernization and Market Linkage Program","Optimize land use, with modernization, diversification and commercialization of agriculture and establishing market linkages to improve the standard of living of citizens dependent on agriculture.",""],[1,"189","4","Community Infrastructure and Collective Production Program","Launch community-based infrastructure development, collective model production and employment programs.",""],[1,"189","4","Cooperative Support for Micro and Small Enterprises","Mobilize the cooperative sector for development of micro, domestic and small enterprises and marketing of products.",""],[1,"189","4","Local Tourism Economy Strengthening Initiative","Strengthen the local economy through tourism.",""],[1,"189","4","Financial Literacy and Inclusion Expansion","Enhance financial literacy to increase financial access of low-income and marginalized groups and communities.",""],[1,"189","4","Financial Sector Expansion and Instrument Diversification","Expand the financial sector and diversify financial instruments.",""],[1,"190","3","Employment and Self-Employment Program Review","Review the existing employment and self-employment programs to create employment at the local level by supporting production and productivity enhancement through mobilization of local skills, resources, capital, and technology.",""],[1,"190","3","Multi-Level Employment Creation Program","Conduct employment creation program with participation of the government at all levels and in partnership with the private sector.",""],[1,"190","3","Technical Assistance and Subsidized Loans for Small Enterprises","In partnership with the provincial and local levels, provide technical assistance and distribute subsidized loans for development and upgrade of small and domestic enterprises.",""],[1,"190","3","Provincial Innovation Partnership Program","Carry out innovation partnership programs in all province in partnership with provinces and local levels.",""],[1,"190","3","\"Farm to Factory\" Linkage Program","Conduct \"Farm to Factory\" programs to link local agricultural production with enterprises and thereby expand employment opportunities.",""],[1,"190","3","Subsidized Loans and Support for Women Entrepreneurs","Provide subsidized loans along with support programs from the Industrial Investment Promotion Fund to promote women, micro, domestic and small entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"190","3","Integrated Agriculture and Livestock Development Program","Conduct intensive integrated agriculture and livestock development programs targeted at the poor.",""],[1,"190","4","Infrastructure and Technology Utilization Program for Poverty Reduction and Inclusion","Infrastructure and technology utilization program for poverty reduction and inclusion: Utilize the opportunities created by development and expansion of transportation and power networks, development of information technology, etc. to promote poverty reduction and inclusion.",""],[1,"190","4","Digital Agricultural Extension and Market Linkage Platform","Establish digital platforms to provide agricultural extension services to farmers and connect them with markets.",""],[1,"190","4","Online Career and Professional Guidance Program","Conduct program to provide professional and career advice through online means.",""]],"65":[[1,"53","5","Local Infrastructure Expansion Program","Infrastructure related to transport and communication, education and health and public utility will have to be developed and expanded in all local levels.",""],[1,"70","4","Human Capital Investment Expansion","Develop human capital by increasing public and private investments in education and health sectors; increase productivity of human resources and utilize labor within the country.",""]],"66":[[1,"43","7","Cooperative Sector Reform Program","Cooperative sector reform program: Classification, integration, and structural reform of cooperatives.",""],[1,"44","1","Production-Oriented Cooperative Linkage and Oversight","Establish linkage of production-oriented cooperatives in production, branding, and marketing and ensure monitoring and supervision of cooperative organizations.",""]],"67":[[1,"154","3","Gender-Responsive Governance System","With the implementation of the National Gender Equality Policy, 2021, emphasis is being laid on gender-responsive governance system in all three levels of the state for establishment of substantive gender equality in this sector by institutionalizing the achievements made so far.",""],[1,"154","3","Gender-Responsive Budgeting System","Gender-responsive budget system has been adopted in policies and programs of federal, provincial and local governments.",""],[1,"157","2","Government Coordination and Social Mobilization Strengthening","Enhance government levelwise and sectorwise coordination and collaboration in social mobilization:",""],[1,"159","2","Fact-Based Decision-Making System","Make policy, plan and program formulation, implementation, and monitoring and evaluation related to target groups and communities including women, children, senior citizens, persons with disabilities, gender and sexual minorities, etc., based on facts.",""],[1,"159","2","Integrated Management Information System for Target Group Data","To this end, develop an integrated management information system to obtain segregated data that covers various aspects, including basis of identification of target groups, setting of standards and indicators, etc.",""],[1,"160","2","Gender-Responsive Budgeting System","Implement a gender-responsive budgeting system at all three levels of government in such a way that information on investment, expenditure and returns is publicly available.",""],[1,"160","2","Continuous Monitoring and Evaluation System","Establish a system that takes into account achievements and impacts, and continuous monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"160","2","Gender Focal Point and Desk Capacity Strengthening","Designate gender focal points and gender focal desks in all public agencies and the organized sector, and increase their capacity.",""],[1,"162","4","Integrated Data System for Gender Equality Programs","Institutionalize and develop an integrated data system to obtain basic data and information on programs related to gender equality",""],[1,"163","1","Social Data Management System Institutionalization","Institutionalize social data management system at all three levels.",""],[1,"163","1","Gender and Social Test Evaluation Methods","implement gender test and social test methods as an integral part of the evaluation in all bodies of the state.",""],[1,"163","1","Mandatory Gender Mainstreaming in Plans and Monitoring Systems","Ensure mandatory inclusion of gender issues of target groups in plans and programs and monitoring and evaluation systems.",""]],"68":[[1,"238","1","Public Health and Education Investment Increase","Increase investment in public health and education.",""],[1,"238","1","School Physical and Teaching Infrastructure Investment","Increase investment in the physical and teaching infrastructure of schools accordingly.",""]],"69":[[1,"177","4","Reform of Intergovernmental Fiscal Transfers for SDG Delivery","Reforming the use of intergovernmental fiscal transfers in order to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals: Prioritize the allocation of resources at all three levels to increase investment in sectors which are lagging behind to reach destinations set by the SDGs.",""],[1,"178","1","Fiscal Transfers to Strengthen Subnational Governments","strengthen provinces and local levels which have strong economies through financial transfers.",""],[1,"178","1","Capacity Upgrading for Economically Weak Provinces and Local Levels","Likewise, upgrade provinces and local levels that are weak from economic perspective.",""],[1,"178","3","Federalism Strengthening Program","Enact additional legislations required to strengthen federalism, bring clarity in sharing of responsibilities and establish a federalism strengthening monitoring and evaluation secretariat at the National Planning Commission.",""],[1,"179","5","Fiscal Federalism Promotion Program","Fiscal federalism promotion program: Build capacity in fiscal responsibility and planning.",""],[1,"180","1","Performance-Based Intergovernmental Fiscal Transfers","performance-based system of intergovernmental fiscal transfers.",""],[1,"180","1","Conditional Grants with Subject-Specific Conditions","Extend the conditional grants not in an operational manner but with subject-specific conditions and balanced development goals and expected achievements.",""],[1,"180","1","Fiscal Equalization Grant Expansion","Gradually increase the fiscal equalization grant.",""],[1,"197","3","Intergovernmental Fiscal Management Reform","Ensure sustainable, reliable, and predictable intergovernmental fiscal management by fulfilling vertical and horizontal fiscal gaps among different tiers of government through revenue sharing, grant transfers, proper utilization of public debt, and enhancing internal revenue capacity.",""],[1,"199","5","Intergovernmental Finance Reform Framework","Make intergovernmental financial transfers scientific, transparent, and accountable to address the financial disparities of provincial and local governments; develop and implement an appropriate framework for investing in and utilizing natural resources; enhance the expenditure capacity of governments at different levels to increase the effectiveness of intergovernmental finance.",""],[1,"200","5","Financial Transfer and Efficiency Enhancement Program","(3) Financial Transfer and Efficiency Enhancement Program: After the implementation of federalism, all three levels of government have accounts, and even when the federal government's account lacks funds, a large portion remains unused in the accounts of provinces and local governments.",""]],"70":[[1,"45","1","Completion of National Pride Projects and Large-Scale Programmes","Most of the national pride projects of and other large scale programmes and projects will be completed within the 16th plan period.",""],[1,"53","5","Completion of Large-Scale Infrastructure Programs and Projects","The large scale infrastructure programs and projects related started in the past period will be completed and brought into operation in this period.",""]],"71":[[1,"39","3","Revenue System Strengthening and Tax Base Expansion","Develop a predictable fiscal system along with expansion of the base and scope of revenue.",""],[1,"42","4","Revenue System Strengthening Program","Revenue system strengthening program: Expand the base and scope of revenue.",""]],"72":[[1,"69","1","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Production System","Establish resilient production system by adopting an agriculture system that can adapt to climate change.",""],[1,"74","1","Climate-Friendly and Inclusive Agriculture Program","Adopt climate-friendly agricultural system, launch women-friendly and youth-oriented agriculture and livestock development programs.",""],[1,"76","1","Agricultural Damage Mitigation Preparedness Program","Program to mitigate damage in agriculture through preparedness: Modernize and automate weather forecasting stations and make their information system accessible.",""],[1,"76","1","Agricultural Early Warning System Improvement","Make early warning system provided by hydrological and meteorological information reliable and timely.",""],[1,"76","1","Crop Damage Reduction Campaigns Against Wild Animals","Launch campaigns to reduce damage caused to agricultural crops by wild animals by adopting appropriate techniques and practices.",""]],"73":[[1,"125","5","Intergovernmental Infrastructure Project Management Coordination","Maintain harmony in infrastructure construction between the governments at different levels.",""],[1,"125","5","Land Acquisition and Compensation Procedure Simplification","Reduce the cost of infrastructure construction by simplifying the procedure of land acquisition and compensation distribution.",""],[1,"125","5","Infrastructure Sector Legal Compliance Enforcement","Comply with the legal provisions relating to the jurisdiction of the infrastructure sector.",""],[1,"125","5","Construction Entrepreneur Regulation and Capacity Building","Improve the regulation and capacity of construction entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"126","3","Integrated Infrastructure Laws and Structural Arrangements","Make integrated laws and structural arrangements related to infrastructure.",""],[1,"128","2","National Infrastructure Policy Formulation and Legal Reform","Formulate national infrastructure policy by interlinking the sectoral policies of infrastructure development.",""],[1,"129","2","Infrastructure Project Management Stabilization Measures","Ensure the stability of policy level and project leadership during construction period of large-scale infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"129","4","Transparent Construction Governance and Standards Compliance","Consolidate transparent working relationships between construction entrepreneurs and government agencies to ensure transparent and pragmatic construction process; comply with all construction standards in this regard.",""],[1,"131","3","Construction Materials Quarry Identification and Management","For regular supply of mineral-based construction materials, identify potential spots for quarries throughout the country and carry out extraction, development and management.",""]],"74":[[1,"40","1","Prudent Public Debt Mobilization Strategy","Mobilize domestic and external debts in productive projects of national priority.",""],[1,"43","2","Public Debt Management Program","Public debt management program: Minimize the gap between external debt commitments and disbursements and improve reimbursements.",""],[1,"53","5","Macroeconomic Stability and Investment Mobilization","macroeconomic stability will be maintained and investments of the general government, private sector and cooperatives will be mobilized.",""],[1,"59","1","Investment Resource Mobilization Strategy","To fulfil this investment needs, resources from the general government, public enterprises and the private sector will be mobilized.",""],[1,"59","1","Alternative Investment Financing Mobilization","The alternative sources to be mobilized shall be foreign direct investment, public-private partnership, mixed investment, project development bonds, income from natural resources depository, green finance, carbon tax and funds accumulated at various public enterprises.",""],[1,"59","2","Consumption Reduction and Savings Promotion Measures","In the Sixteenth plan period, unnecessary consumption will be cut down and saving will be promoted, thereby gross fixed capital formation is asumed toraisesubstantially ..",""],[1,"62","7","Monetary and Financial Sector Policy Measures","Policies related to monetary and financial sectors will be carried out as a driver of macro- economy for achieving stimulated growth and maintaining economic stability.",""]],"75":[[1,"103","3","Healthcare Technology and Artificial Intelligence Adoption","Use of latest and cutting-edge technology in overall healthcare system: To increase consumption of quality healthcare services, ensure maximum use of latest technology and artificial intelligence, and the use of alternative measures.",""],[1,"108","2","Health Services Quality Improvement Program","Program to improve the quality of health services and provider institutions: Implementation of health services for all.",""],[1,"108","4","Health Sector Digitalization Program","Health sector digitalization program: Enhance the use of modern information technology such as telemedicine, digital health, robotic technology and artificial intelligence for universal access and use of health services.",""]],"76":[[1,"102","6","Health Infrastructure and Human Resources Provision","Ensure the provision of health infrastructure and human resources based on standard criteria such as size of",""],[1,"103","1","Healthy Human Resource System Development","Develop healthy human resource system based on need, demand and consumption.",""],[1,"108","3","Intensive Health Sector Human Resources System Development and Operation Program","Develop and bring into operation an intensive health sector human resource system with provision of distribution, utilization and mobilization based on population, geography, disease burden and social justice.","Ministry of Health and Population | Medical Education Commission"]],"77":[[1,"156","4","Women's Employment and Self-Employment Promotion Measures","Adopt multidimensional measures including domestic employment and self-employment by coordinating and collaborating among agencies involved in gender empowerment, skill development and job creation.",""],[1,"156","4","Women's Contribution to National Accounts Mechanism","Develop a mechanism for calculating women's contribution to national accounts by making assessments of women's household chores and caregiving jobs.",""],[1,"156","4","Women's Work-Life Balance and Productivity Linkage Initiative","Balance women's work life and link their knowledge, skills and labor with production and productivity.",""],[1,"161","2","Women and Adolescent Girls Leadership in Production Sectors","Promote women and adolescent girls' leadership roles in the production sector (agriculture, forestry, trade, tourism) and develop a women-led socio-economic environment in economic advancement.",""],[1,"161","2","Recognition of Women's Domestic and Care Work in National Accounts","Take account of women's domestic labor and care work in national accounts; conduct awareness campaigns to develop a culture of respect for women's economic activism.",""],[1,"163","5","Self-Reliance Program for Daughters","Implement 'Self-reliance program for daughters' to prepare entrepreneurial women in economic sectors, especially in agriculture, industry, tourism and forestry, and service sectors.",""],[1,"164","1","Integrated Employment Center Support","employment center in an integrated manner.",""],[1,"164","1","Model Entrepreneur Promotion for Target Communities","Promote model entrepreneurs from among cottage, small and micro enterprises run by women, persons with disabilities, Dalits, gender and sexual minorities and other target community members on the basis of individual contributions made by each of them.",""],[1,"164","1","President Women's Empowerment Program Review and Implementation","Review and implement the President Women's Empowerment Program for economic and social transformation of women.",""],[1,"164","1","Women-Friendly Technology-Oriented Productive Sector Programs","Emphasize on conducting women-friendly technology-oriented programs in the productive sector useful for life.",""],[1,"164","1","Local Production of Sanitary Pads and Health Products","Produce items like sanitary pads and other health products using local raw materials and female labor force.",""],[1,"164","1","Local Production-Oriented Training and Self-Employment Programs","In coordination with the private sector and non-governmental organizations, conduct production-oriented training and self-employment programs at the local level, targeting adolescent girls of the technology age.",""]],"78":[[1,"209","5","Political Party Finance Transparency and Electoral Integrity Reform","Make donations and financial assistance received by political parties from different sectors and sections of the society transparent, and in full compliance with the law.",""],[1,"210","1","Electoral Process Modernization and Direct Democracy Reform","dignified and frugal by using modern technology, while discouraging door-to-door campaigns at various stages of the electoral process. Strengthen direct democracy by including issues such as the right to refuse voting in the law.",""],[1,"213","2","Election Management Reform Program","Reform program in election management process: Ensure transparency of financial transactions of political parties.",""],[1,"213","2","Electoral Education and Voter List Modernization","Conduct effective electoral education.",""],[1,"213","2","Electoral Law and Voting Rights Reform","Amend and implement electoral laws for voting and counting.",""]],"79":[[1,"159","4","Judicial System Reform for Accessible Justice","introduce reforms in the judicial system to ensure simple, affordable and speedy access to justice and cases settlement.",""],[1,"159","4","Capacity Building for Local Judicial Committees","Enhance the capacity of the local judicial committee to make the judicial system victim-friendly.",""],[1,"160","2","Local Judicial Committee Capacity Enhancement and Pro Bono Legal Assistance Expansion","Enhance capacity of local judicial committees along with expansion and upgradation of pro bono legal assistance program to make it easy, affordable and accessible.",""]],"80":[[1,"73","3","Study and Research Policy and Institutional Arrangements","Make policy and institutional arrangements for study and research in the fields of agriculture, industry, energy, irrigation, water resources, tourism, trade, etc.",""],[1,"73","3","Human Resource Capacity Building for Research","Enhance investment and build capacity of human resources.",""],[1,"73","3","Evidence-Based Sector Development Using Research Findings","Utilize the findings and suggestions from studies and research in the development of agriculture and industry as well as other sectors.",""],[1,"79","5","Public-Private Partnership for Research and Capacity Development","Adopt public-private partnership in studies, research and development related to agriculture, industry and service sectors.",""]],"81":[[1,"72","1","Weather Data Automation and Pre-Information System Upgrade","Automate weather data, make pre-information system reliable and up-to-date to mitigate potential weather-related damages.",""],[1,"79","3","Modernization of Water and Meteorological Services","Program for modernization of water and meteorological services: Upgrade water and meteorological forecasting stations by construction of additional stations.",""],[1,"135","7","Modern Weather Forecasting and Early Warning System Upgrade","To mitigate loss of lives and property by disasters, and make weather forecasting and early warning system modern, automatic and scientific, install modern technology and expand existing",""]],"82":[[1,"45","1","Irrigation Project Operation and Expansion Programme","Growth in agricultural sector will triggerd through the operation of irrigation projects under construction, further expansion of irrigation facilities from collaborative efforts of federal, provincial and local levels, regular supply of chemical fertilizers, mechanization and so on.",""],[1,"68","2","Round-the-Year Irrigation Expansion and Water Diversion Projects","As per the Irrigation Policy, 2023, emphasis is laid on expansion of round-the-year irrigation facilities and their effective management by developing storage dams and inter- watershed water diversion projects.",""],[1,"70","5","Irrigation System Construction and Upgrading","Construct, develop and upgrade different systems of irrigation as necessary such as surface, tubewell and lift irrigation to enhance agricultural production and productivity.",""],[1,"71","3","Agricultural Irrigation Infrastructure Expansion","Construct, expand and upgrade surface, tubewell, small and medium storage dams and lift irrigation system necessary to increase agricultural production and productivity by extending power transmission lines necessary for this.",""],[1,"75","4","Agricultural Production and Productivity Enhancement through Irrigation Facilities","Improve irrigation to increase agricultural production and productivity.",""]],"83":[[1,"157","2","Community and NGO Governance and Accountability Enhancement","Enhance good governance of community and non-governmental organizations and mobilize them in areas of national priority and need in a transparent and accountable manner.",""],[1,"157","2","Institutional Strengthening and One-Door Service System","Carry out institutional strengthening for good governance, internal capacity development, regulation, monitoring and evaluation, and facilitate these activities through a one-door system.",""],[1,"159","5","Institutional Strengthening of Stakeholder Agencies","Carry out institutional strengthening of the stakeholder agencies in coordination and collaboration of the federal, provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"159","5","One-Door Governance System for Non-Governmental Organizations","And adopt a one-door system to maintain institutional good governance in non-governmental organizations by enhancing their transparency, responsibility and accountability.",""],[1,"164","3","NGO and Civil Society Mobilization and Governance Strengthening Program","Program for mobilization of social and non-governmental organizations and institutional good governance and their strengthening: Classify community and non- governmental organizations on the basis of national standards and mobilize them and their resources in socio-economic transformation and developmental works in sectors of national goals and priorities.",""]],"84":[[1,"154","3","SDG Inclusion Programmes for Vulnerable Groups","Under the Sustainable Development Goals implementation program, a variety of programs have been included in diverse areas related to women, children and adolescents, persons with disabilities, senior citizens, sexual and gender minorities and indigenous and tribal peoples.",""],[1,"154","4","Senior Citizens Care and Social Protection Policy","With the increase in the number of senior citizens, a policy of strengthening the system of proper care and social protection for their dignified living and using knowledge, skills, competence and experience they hold in development efforts has been adopted.",""],[1,"156","5","Special Targeted Social Security and Protection Programs","Provide effective social security and protection to the economically backward or socially or educationally backward or infirm and destitute, destitute single women, persons with disabilities, children, persons unable to take care of themselves and citizens belonging to endangered tribes.",""],[1,"156","5","Targeted Policies for Lagging Social Development Areas","Formulate policies targeted at areas that lag behind in social development.",""],[1,"156","5","Accessibility Upgrades for Public Places and Service Sites","Make public places and service delivery sites or office infrastructure friendly to the disabled, senior citizens, children and gender.",""],[1,"157","1","Targeted Support and Inclusion Services for Vulnerable Groups","supporting materials according to the needs of disabled persons and senior citizens.",""],[1,"157","1","Economic Inclusion for Gender and Sexual Minorities and Targeted Communities","Link the citizens with gender and sexual minorities and other targeted groups and communities with production according to their abilities and skills.",""],[1,"157","1","Family-Based Protection and Engagement of Senior Citizens","Increase the role of the family in the protection of senior citizens and capitalize on the long experience and technical skills of senior citizens for the benefit of the nation.",""],[1,"157","1","Child-Friendly Protection Environment from Early Childhood","Targeting children who have fallen victims to discrimination and deprivation and those who require special care, develop a child- friendly environment right from early childhood development stage to ensure a mandatory protection of such children.",""],[1,"157","3","Disaster Resilience Promotion for Vulnerable Groups","Develop a system to ensure continued essential and basic services to target groups, communities, marginalized and people in need of special assistance and protection as well as climate- risk communities in the wake of climate change or natural or other man-made disasters or epidemics also.",""],[1,"158","4","Special Social Protection and Public Service Delivery for Excluded Groups","Give priority to the extremely poor, incapacitated, helpless and disabled as well as Dalits and citizens of excluded and deprived groups, communities and gender while conducting programs related to special social protection and public service delivery.",""],[1,"158","4","Universal and Sustainable Social Security System Reform","Make social security and service system universal and sustainable.",""],[1,"158","4","Social Security Duplication Reduction and Cost-Effective Contribution-Based Measures","Avoid duplication in social security, which has been observed lately, adopt alternative and cost- effective measures of social security based on contribution, need and ability.",""],[1,"158","5","Multi-sectoral Life-Cycle Policy and Planning Approach","While formulating and implementing policies, plans and programs, adopt a multi-sectoral and multidimensional concept based on the life cycle, ensuring a respectful living environment for every person.",""],[1,"158","5","Inclusive Technology Access and Empowerment Initiative","Increase access, affodabality and use of technology for empowerment and mobilization of communities with special needs, including women, children, senior citizens, persons",""],[1,"159","3","State Protection for Disabled and Vulnerable Children and Adolescents","Provide mandatory protection and promotion from the state to disabled and helpless children and adolescents in need of special protection.",""],[1,"160","4","Inclusive National Identity Card Linkage and Distribution System","Link all target groups and communities, including persons with disabilities, gender and sexual minorities, to the national identity card system.",""],[1,"160","4","Disability Identification Standards for Identity Card Distribution","Manage identity card distribution system to disabled persons by developing standards for easy and simple pre-test system for disability identification and classification.",""],[1,"160","4","Uniform Citizenship Acquisition Process for Gender Minorities","Facilitate and maintain uniformity in the citizenship acquisition process of the gender minority community.",""],[1,"162","2","Target Community Specific Social Development and Integration Program","Find out the basis of identification and classification of target groups, decide on standards and indicators, and on the bases of these, launch location-specific special base program at the provincial and local levels targeting the very poor, incapacitated, helpless, and disabled as well as the minority and marginalized groups.",""],[1,"162","2","Integrated Services and Mobile Outreach for Vulnerable Groups","Aiming at the incapacitated, helpless, and those who have suffered from discrimination and violence from among the target groups of women, senior citizens, people with disabilities, marginalized communities, etc., develop packages of integrated services for implementation, and launch mobile services as well.",""],[1,"162","2","Targeted Development Support for Endangered and Marginalized Communities","Conduct targeted programs to improve education, health and basic needs as well as improving overall living conditions, especially targeting endangered and marginalized communities such as Raute, Kusunda, Chepang, Lepcha, Dom, Chamar, Musahar, Halkhor and Dusadh.",""],[1,"162","2","Technology-Friendly Literacy and Service Delivery Points","Make literacy programs and service delivery points technology-friendly to increase access, affordability and use of technology by target groups, communities as well as genders.",""],[1,"162","3","Senior Citizens Security and Protection Program","Senior citizens security and protection program: Ensure a dignified living environment for senior citizens",""],[1,"164","2","Multi-purpose Senior Citizen Village Development","Establish an international level multi-purpose senior citizen village targeting domestic and foreign citizens in collaboration with the private sector.",""],[1,"164","2","Provincial Senior Citizen Care and Hospice Services","Conduct a free senior citizen care center in each province as well as hospice services at provincial level hospitals.",""],[1,"164","2","Municipal Psychosocial Counselor Provision","Make compulsory provision of psychosocial counselors in each municipality.",""],[1,"164","2","Municipal Safe Shelter Management for Women and Target Groups","Effective management of safe shelters for women, target groups and communities in each municipality.",""]],"85":[[1,"114","4","Governance 4.0 Digitalization Program","Institutionalize Governance 4.0 by making maximum use of science and information technology in all administrative work of Nepal.",""]],"86":[[1,"34","6","Public Finance Management Discipline","Maintain discipline in public finance management to create pathways for balanced and equitable development and ensuring access to all stakeholders.",""],[1,"35","1","Public Finance Efficiency and Revenue Reform Package","allocation efficiency by focusing public spending on equitable and high-return priority areas.",""],[1,"35","2","Revenue Base Expansion and Tax Structure Reform","Ensure efficient utilization of traditional sources of revenue and identify new sources for extension of revenue base.",""],[1,"35","2","Domestic Production Capacity Expansion for Revenue Support","Increase internal production capacity to fulfill resource gaps.",""],[1,"35","3","Capital Expenditure Capacity Enhancement","Increase the contribution of capital expenditure in total government expenditure.",""],[1,"35","4","Intergovernmental Fiscal Management Reform","Enhance the revenue collection and expenditure capacity of all three tires of the government.",""],[1,"35","5","Inflation Control and Price Stability Policy","Maintain inflation within targeted limits to ensure the country's economic progress and to protect the interests of the general public.",""],[1,"35","6","Financial Sector Lending Productivity and Interest Rate Stability","Make the financial sector's lending productive.",""],[1,"36","1","Financial Sector Regulation and Market Access Reform","Manage liquidity in such a way that it encourages investment and maintains financial stability too.",""],[1,"36","1","Investor Predictability and Capital Market Access Measures","Boost the morale of investors by ensuring predictability of the changes in market price.",""],[1,"36","1","Insurance Service Uniformity and Financial Sector Expansion","Facilitate uniformity in insurance services and ensure access to all citizens on it.",""],[1,"36","1","Efficient Financial Sector Regulation","Ensure efficient regulation of the financial sector.",""],[1,"36","1","Transparent and Competitive Financial Services Expansion","Expand financial services in such a way that the quality of assets of the banks and financial sector will not be adversly affected, and by maintaining transparency and healthy competition, make sure that the need for reliable resources for prosperity of the country is met.",""],[1,"36","2","Foreign Exchange Reserve Stability Measure","Maintain stability and sustainability in foreign exchange reserves; maintain favourable situation sustainably in balance of payment situation.",""],[1,"37","3","Consumption Discouragement and Savings Promotion Measures","Discourage unnecessary consumption expenditure in the households, governments, and private sectors to promote saving through regulation and provision of incentives, and conduct awareness programs.",""],[1,"37","3","Capital Market Access and Productive Investment Promotion","Increase access to the capital market, promote innovation and entrepreneurship, and create opportunities for productive investment to mobilize saving in productive sectors.",""],[1,"37","3","Domestic Investment and Capital Formation Expansion","Increase domestic investment to ensure mobilization of savings and capital formation",""],[1,"195","2","Internal Resource Mobilization","it is essential to increase the mobilization of internal resources.",""],[1,"195","2","Public Debt Mobilization and Management","Public debt should be mobilized in national needs and priority areas without restricting private sector investment, managing deficit financing, ensuring economic growth with macroeconomic stability, effective utilization of foreign capital and technology, and intergenerational equity.",""],[1,"195","2","Public Financial Management for External Debt Mobilization","Public financial management must also play a significant role in the effective mobilization of external debt.",""],[1,"195","3","Public Investment and Aid Alignment for Infrastructure and Reconstruction","For the development of modern and citizen-friendly infrastructure and reconstruction efforts, there should be alignment between the commitment, acquisition, utilization capacity, and outcomes of foreign aid.",""],[1,"195","3","Capital Expenditure Capacity and Project Governance Strengthening","Capital expenditure capacity must be enhanced by promoting transparency and accountability across all aspects of macro-fiscal discipline and project governance.",""],[1,"195","3","Public Spending Capacity Enhancement Across All Levels of Government","It is essential for federal, provincial, and local governments to enhance their public spending capacity to make public expenditure systems outcome-oriented, transparent, and accountable.",""],[1,"195","4","Public Financial Management Strengthening","the Sixteenth Plan emphasizes achieving good governance, social justice, and prosperity by increasing revenue capacity, capital expenditure capacity, acquisition and utilization of foreign aid, and using effective financial management tools.",""],[1,"197","1","Tax Base Expansion and Domestic Revenue Reform","Expand the tax base and tax scope to reduce tax disparities; increase share of domestic revenue by bringing the informal sector into the tax framework through electronic transactions; transform the current revenue structure based on imports into one based on domestic production.",""],[1,"197","2","Public Expenditure Efficiency Enhancement","Increase public expenditure efficiency through allocation efficiency and expenditure capacity, alignment between responsibilities and expenditure, and financial governance; make the medium-term expenditure framework effective; fulfill the need for capital expenditure from internal sources; enhance the capacity of public organizations and officials involved in fiscal management and capital expenditure mobilization to improve efficiency and professionalism; develop an integrated and sustainable social security system.",""],[1,"197","4","Project Bank Prioritization and Reprioritization System","Ensure prioritization, reprioritization of projects, and effective implementation project bank;",""],[1,"197","4","Public Procurement and Land Acquisition Management Reform","manage projects along with effective public procurement systems and acquisition of land and forest areas;",""],[1,"197","4","Results-Based Project Management and Contract Management System","implement results- based project management through effective contract management, performance contract with project managers, and strengthen the construction business sector.",""],[1,"197","6","Project-Based Public Debt Management System","adopt a project-based public debt system; sustainably utilize public debt by adopting short-term, medium-term, and long-term public debt mobilization strategy; ensure expenditures are made only in areas of national priority with tangible outcomes and establishing a system to spend only according to fiscal laws and regulations.",""],[1,"198","2","Contingent Liability Management and Sovereign Guarantee Framework","Ensure proper management of the government's contingent liabilities; provide sovereign guarantees by assessing the capacity to bear risks solely for strategic infrastructure development; and utilize investments in financial assets and potential cash savings in government funds in a profitable and equitable manner.",""],[1,"198","3","Result-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System","(9) Result-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System: Emphasize a result-based monitoring and evaluation system through effective accounting, reporting, and auditing of public expenditures; develop a strong internal control system; monitoring the financial discipline of non-budgetary entities in public financial management and obtaining financial reports.",""],[1,"198","4","Revenue Base Expansion and Tax Administration Reform","Expand the scope of revenue: Make the tax determination system a subject of parliamentary discussion through tax proposal bills; assure the parliament the authority to set tax rates and provide tax exemptions; restructure the sources and rates of revenue; conduct tax audits and research focused on sectors and activities with tax discrepancies; revie and adopt tax laws aimed at protecting the tax base, reducing cost of economy, and increasing efficiency; control revenue leakage, enhancing tax compliance, and identifying and expanding new revenue bases; promoting the formal economy through digital transactions and increase tax awareness, thereby expand the scope of revenue.",""],[1,"198","5","Revenue Administration Reform and Modernization","Strengthen Revenue Administration: Streamline procedures ensuring inter- organizational coordination, and maximizing the use of modern technology to make the revenue system sustainable and dynamic through policy and institutional reform of revenue administration; develop an integrated system to include all types of income in the revenue basket; control tax evasion through all means by increasing the use of artificial intelligence; strengthen revenue administration through taxpayer-friendly tax administration; establish mechanisms to provide recommendations for improvements in tax policy, changes in tax rate, and hearing of tax disputes based on regular research and development.",""],[1,"198","6","Evidence-Based Resource Allocation Mechanisms","Develop mechanisms to ensure research, evidence, and accountability in resource estimation;",""],[1,"198","6","Contribution-Based Participatory Expenditure System","adopt a contribution-based, partnership, and participatory expenditure system to make mandatory and contingent public expenditures sustainable and bearable;",""],[1,"198","6","Priority-Based Public Resource Allocation","allocate resources to priority areas based on preparedness, need for expenditure and capacity, fiscal discipline, investing capital by integrating scattered funds;",""],[1,"198","6","Periodic Public Expenditure Review","enhance allocation efficiency and expenditure effectiveness by conducting periodic reviews of public expenditure;",""],[1,"198","6","Professional Management of Completed Projects","operate completed projects professionally;",""],[1,"198","6","Parliamentary Approval for Long-Term Liabilities","establish provision of the parliamentary approval for long-term liabilities creating programs, and budget re- appropriation.",""],[1,"199","1","Project Governance and Capital Expenditure Reform","(4) Improve Capital Expenditure Capacity by Ensuring Project Governance: Establish an institutional arrangement of project banks at all three tiers; prioritize and reprioritize projects focused on physical infrastructure with comparative advantage and competitive capacity for economic growth; focus capital expenditure on strategically important and multi-year projects and programs; adopting a quarterly target and payment policy for projects; implement a system where loans can be obtained from banks with project guarantees after signing an invoice or contract; simplify environmental impact assessments and land acquisition processes to improve project governance; create a separate development policy for the implementation of large projects; ensure only the labor-intensive and locally-sourced materials-based construction work is carried out through consumer committees, and discourage the practice of splitting large works to assign them to consumer committees to avoid competition.",""],[1,"199","3","Public Debt Mobilization for High-Return Capital Projects","Focus public debt mobilization on feasible and high- return projects based on cost-benefit analysis for long-term capital formation; issue project-specific development bonds instead of budget support to mobilize domestic debt; balance short-term and long-term debt in domestic borrowing.",""],[1,"199","4","Public Financial Management Reform Plan","Implement continuous reform plans to strengthen and make public financial management effective by enhancing financial investment, efficiency, and managing contingent liabilities; monitor the financial discipline of non-budgetary bodies and produce financial reports; assess risk-bearing capacity to provide sovereign guarantees; invest in financial assets and ensure the beneficial use of potential cash savings in government funds while ensuring intergenerational justice.",""],[1,"200","2","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System","Develop a Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System: Strengthen internal control systems, effective accounting, reporting, and auditing of public funds, liabilities, assets, income, and expenditure; adopt an integrated monitoring and evaluation system with coordination and cooperation at different levels and bodies; develop a financial information system so that an integrated financial report of all three levels of government, including the entire government, can be audited.",""],[1,"200","3","Revenue System Strengthening Program","Revenue System Strengthening Program: Restructure revenue administration to manage risks; review tax rates and structures, conduct tax audits and investigations focusing on large establishments and individuals with significant assets to reduce tax compliance costs and time; review the effectiveness of tax incentives; develop and implement a paperless, faceless, contactless system based on electronic and artificial intelligence technologies; integrate all tax and business administration into a one-door system.",""],[1,"200","4","Financial Resource Mobilization Improvement Program","(2) Financial Resource Mobilization Improvement Program: Conduct comprehensive reforms in resource mobilization, as a large amount of resources is needed to meet development needs; establish a scientific customs duty system to control revenue evasion and leakage; improve surveillance systems by using technologies such as CCTV, scanners, and vehicle scanners; increase compliance with value-added tax (VAT); make monitoring and inspection more effective; implement punitive measures for both sellers who do not issue invoices and customers who do not take them; reward and incentivize good employees and businesses while imposing fines and penalties for wrongdoers; provide logistics and special facilities to security personnel and staff deployed to control smuggling, tax evasion, and illegal trade in border areas.",""],[1,"200","6","Financial Resource Mobilization Through Natural Resources Program","Financial Resource Mobilization Through Natural Resources Program: Make appropriate use of available land, forest resources, water, stones, soil, river materials, etc .; develop a system to increase revenue through the judicious use of natural",""],[1,"201","2","Formalization of Informal Economic Activities Program","(5) Formalization of Informal Economic Activities Program: Promote the registration, labeling, renewal, and inclusion of rental housing in the tax system; make it mandatory to conduct real estate transactions and land deals through registered agents; bring real estate brokers and businesspeople into the tax net; actively engage local governments in the formalization of the informal economy and distribute revenues accordingly; take effective steps to control illegal trade and transactions from both the demand and supply sides; revise the methodology for calculating gross domestic product (GDP) and change the base year.",""],[1,"201","3","Accountable Public Financial Management Program","(6) Accountable Public Financial Management Program: Strengthen information technology for accountable public financial management; publish accurate financial statements for the entire government; develop a system for assessing and managing public financial risks; introduce legal provisions to punish heads of agencies and financial officers if their audited financial accounts show an audit objection ratio of more than 1.5% of the total government financial transactions (expenditure and revenue).",""],[1,"201","4","Project Management Strengthening and Capital Expenditure Capacity Building Program","(7) Project Management Strengthening and Capital Expenditure Capacity Building Program: Enhance the interconnectedness of project banks, medium-term expenditure structures, and ministry-level budget information systems; prioritize the open, competitive selection of project heads through external contracts and performance contracts; develop an integrated development law to enhance the capacity for capital expenditure; implement the public investment management action plan to increase cost-effectiveness in capital expenditure; coordinate and facilitate land acquisition, forest area utilization, availability of construction materials, and adequate budget provisions; improve the project management system through the use of advanced technologies; end the frequent changes in project heads and ensure the availability of appropriate skilled personnel.",""],[1,"201","5","Construction Entrepreneurs' Capacity and Efficiency Enhancement Program","(8) Construction Entrepreneurs' Capacity and Efficiency Enhancement Program: Amend the Public Procurement Act related to construction to make it acceptable to both the government and the private sector; manage standards and codes of conduct for construction; enhance the capacity and efficiency of construction entrepreneurs; introduce a provision for the collateralization of contracts and interim payment certificates and allow direct reimbursement by government bodies; adopt a system where construction entrepreneurs are required to submit a completion certificate for their previous responsibilities when selecting them for new contracts.",""],[1,"201","6","Public Funds Integration and Resource Expansion Program","Formulate policies for the integration of public funds, implement them, and allow borrowing from the integrated funds; identify and expand additional revenue sources for local and provincial governments.",""],[1,"202","2","Artificial Intelligence Promotion Program","(12) Artificial Intelligence Promotion Program: Reduce current government expenses by increasing the use of information technology, including artificial intelligence, which requires less manpower; streamline and economize the use of vehicles, fuel, drivers, and office assistants; adopt measures for frugality in the use of stationery, electricity, water, etc .; increase the use of artificial intelligence wherever possible.",""],[1,"202","4","Results-Based Monitoring, Evaluation, and Sustainability Program","Continuously revise and adopt on-site and off-site methods for results-based monitoring and evaluation based on information technology; integrate information systems and establish automated information exchange between systems.",""]],"87":[[1,"41","4","Public Enterprise Efficiency and Reform Programme","Classify public enterprises, and limit government involvement in those enterprises only where it is mandatory or in those areas where the private sector does not get attracted.",""],[1,"44","5","Public Enterprises Strengthening Program","Public enterprises strengthening program: Classify and prioritize public enterprises.",""]],"88":[[1,"200","1","Public-Private Partnership Project Prioritization and Enabling Measures","Identify viable projects to be implemented under public-private partnership and timely amend legal provisions; assess the capacity of contractors and enhance their capacity; mobilize direct foreign investment and domestic investment in public-private partnerships; ensure the smooth supply of construction materials based on natural resources and enhance worker skills while promoting public-private partnerships; develop the capacity to manage and operate assets after transferring such projects to the government.",""],[1,"202","1","Investment Climate Improvement and Promotion Program","Improve business operation indicators through legal reforms, implementation of automated systems, and facilitation measures to promote the country as an attractive investment destination; encourage domestic investors to make additional investments and attract substantial foreign investment; promote public-private partnerships (PPPs) for various infrastructure projects by implementing Viability Gap Funding; enhance the effectiveness of economic diplomacy.",""]],"89":[[1,"105","1","Curriculum Modernization and Practical Education Reform","Make contemporary changes and develop curricula and educational programs of all levels.",""],[1,"105","1","Higher Education Emerging Technology Curriculum Strengthening","Increase the effectiveness of subjects related to emerging technology in higher education.",""],[1,"105","1","National Yoga, Meditation, and Spirituality Promotion Initiative","Make Nepal a center of yoga, meditation and spirituality to increase spiritual sentiments and provide education right from elementary level based on good governance, ethics, patriotism and values.",""],[1,"111","3","School Education Quality Improvement Program","Improve the quality of education at the school level by revising textbooks every 5 years.",""],[1,"111","3","Practical Skills Curriculum Reform","Include activities such as internship, 'study and earn', etc. in the curriculum for promotion of practical knowledge and skill development.",""],[1,"112","1","Curriculum Revision for Local Knowledge and Self-Reliance","Revise the basic level curriculum to include lessons on local knowledge, culture, lifestyle, and promotion of self-reliance.",""],[1,"112","1","School Curriculum Update for Moral Education and Good Governance","Update school curriculum so as to support the campaign for moral education and good governance in keeping with child psychology.",""],[1,"112","2","Two-Month Compulsory Orientation Program After Class 10","Provide a two- month (eight weeks) long compulsory orientation program for students who have just finished secondary school examination and are waiting for results.",""]],"90":[[1,"85","1","Labour Force Skills and Productivity Upgrading","Taking optimum advantage of demographic dividend prevailing in the country and building a self-reliant economy call for production and mobilization of labour force that conforms to the demand of the labour market on one hand, while making it technology friendly, competent, skilled, active, competitive and dedicated to serve the nation, on the other.",""],[1,"86","2","Skills Development for Productivity Improvement","For this, strategies and programs that are being implemented include promotion of domestic employment, bringing to an end compulsion for foreign employment and making it safe and dignified, expansion of contribution-based social security and raising productivity through skill development.",""],[1,"88","1","Curriculum Alignment for Labor Market Balance","collaborate and coordinate to bring comtemporary changes in educational curriculum and program.",""],[1,"88","1","Local Employment Bank for Youth Skills","In collaboration with the local levels, provide employment and skill development opportunities to unemployed youths locally through employment bank.",""],[1,"88","2","Youth Workforce Utilization and Skills Training Initiative","Optimum utilization of youth force in productive sectors.",""],[1,"89","2","Vocational and Skill-Based Training System Integration","Integrate vocational training and technical education that is operated in a fragmented manner under the three levels of government, private sector and non-governmental organizations to make them effective and quality-oriented.",""],[1,"89","2","Public-Private-Cooperative Training Partnership","Conduct training programs in a public-private-cooperative partnership framework.",""],[1,"89","2","Labor Market Responsive Skills Upgrading","In the context of changes taking place in global production and labor practices, provide new training to human resources and upgrade the existing training programs.",""],[1,"89","2","Training Centre Coordination and Quality Improvement","Maintain coordination among training centres and raise quality of all training programs.",""],[1,"89","2","Vocational Training Access and Institutional Efficiency Expansion","Increase efficiency of training institutions; expand the opportunities for vocational and skill trainings and people's access to them.",""],[1,"89","2","Foreign Employment Training Standards Alignment","Align foreign employment-oriented trainings with quality standards of the labour destination country.",""],[1,"89","2","Skills Certification Arrangements","Make arrangements for certification of skills acquired at home and abroad.",""],[1,"89","2","Labor Market and Technology Responsive Skills Development","Make skills relevant to changes that have come in labor market, entrepreneurship and technology and develop skill-oriented training provider institutions on a par with international standard.",""],[1,"89","4","Technical and Vocational Education Effectiveness Improvement","Increasing effectiveness of technical and vocational education: Make technical education practical, useful for life and relevant to national and international market demand and capable of creating job opportunities for domestic and foreign employment.",""],[1,"90","1","Standardized Skills Training for Quality Improvement","Standardize skill trainings for quality.",""],[1,"90","5","National Human Resource Development and Mobilization Plan","Formulate national human resource development and mobilization plan and implement it.",""],[1,"90","5","Human Resource Development Investment Increase","Increase investment in human resource development for raising labor productivity.",""],[1,"91","1","Technical and Vocational Training Effectiveness Program","Conduct technical and vocational trainings targeted to youths who have entered the labor market for transformation of their skills towards employment orientation.",""],[1,"92","4","Employment Service Center Upgrading","Equip employment service centers with resources and technology.",""],[1,"93","1","Employment-Oriented Curriculum Reform","practical contents to make the educational curriculum at all levels employment-oriented.",""],[1,"93","2","Short-Term Job-Oriented Skills Training Programme","Launch short-term job-oriented skill development trainings.",""],[1,"93","2","Government Training Center Center of Excellence Upgrade","Develop the government training center as a center of excellence through sectoral integration and consolidation of the the subject content.",""],[1,"93","2","School Curriculum Skills Content Integration","To ensure supply of skilled workers in the country, include necessary skill content in the curriculum of the school level.",""],[1,"93","2","Integrated Vocational and Skills Training Strengthening","Integrate and strengthen vocational and skill development training.",""],[1,"93","2","Work-Based Learning and Earn-While-Learning Training","Conduct work-based training for learning while earning.",""],[1,"93","2","Native Worker Skills Development in Migrant Occupations","Develop the skills and capacity of native workers in areas where migrant workers are involved.",""],[1,"93","3","Alternative Employment Enhancement Program","Alternative employment enhancement program: Launch earn while you are studying program, employment for apprentices, part-time employment program, digital employment program.",""],[1,"93","3","Social Mobilization Skills Development and Job Creation Program","Conduct skill development and job creation programs through social mobilization.",""],[1,"93","3","Information Technology-Based Employment Program","Information technology-based employment program; special employment program targeted at 15-30 age group.",""],[1,"93","3","Youth Returnee Employment Support Program","Conduct special program focused on youths who have either returned from foreign employment or who want to return.",""],[1,"101","4","Human Resource Projection and Skills Supply Programme","Make projection of human resources needed in all sectors for overall development of the country.",""],[1,"101","4","Human Capital Quality and Ethics Development","Produce and supply human resources of quality, ethical standard, and pragmatic skills useful for life.",""],[1,"101","4","Human Resource Upgrading and Labor Market Linkage","Upgrade the existing human resources to raise capacity; link higher education to the labor market.",""],[1,"101","4","Inclusive TVET Access Expansion","Extend access of technical and vocational education and training to all social classes and groups.",""],[1,"101","4","Talent Retention Strategy","Sustain talented human resources within the country.",""],[1,"101","4","Research- and Innovation-Based Human Capital Development","Create, develop and utilize human capital that is based on research, technology and innovation.",""],[1,"105","3","National Human Resource Development Plan","Formulate a long-term and periodic national human resource development plan to build necessary human capital for the country and develop a mechanism and methodology for creating educational programs based on it.",""],[1,"105","4","Secondary Education Career Development Linkage Program","To make secondary education focused on career development, link it with literacy and skill development, and higher education entrepreneurship and employment focused, lay emphasis on programs like \"Earn while you learn, and learn while you earn\".",""],[1,"105","4","National Skills Development and Employment Creation Campaign","Launch national skill development and employment creation grand campaign in collaboration with government, non- governmental, cooperative and private sectors.",""],[1,"105","4","Recognition of Prior Learning Procedure","Make effective procedure of recognition of prior learning of workers involved in informal jobs.",""],[1,"111","3","Technical and Professional Human Resource Development","Emphasize more on production of technical and professional human resources with skills and abilities according to market demand.",""],[1,"111","4","Human Resource Needs Projection and Skilled Workforce Production Program","Taking into account the number of human resources required within the country and the quantity of labour force who may go abroad for employment, make projection of human resource needs for the next ten years.",""],[1,"111","4","Education and Skills Development for Skilled Human Resources","Emphasize on education and skill development in order to produce skilled human resources accordingly.",""],[1,"111","4","Curriculum and Skills Training Alignment with Labor Market Demand","Balance market demand for human resources in general subjects and specialization by fine-tuning teaching learning and skill development activities.",""],[1,"113","4","National Skill Development Program","National skill development program: Conduct short and long-term job-oriented and workplace-based skill development training to develop human resources according to labor market demand.",""],[1,"234","3","Labor Force Skills and Capacity-Building Investment","Increase investment in professional skills and capacity-building of labor force that enters the labor market every year on the basis of demand of the labor market.",""],[1,"234","3","National Human Resource Development Plan","Formulate and implement a national human resource development plan that deems necessary for Nepal.",""],[1,"235","4","Short-Term and Medium-Term Skills Development and Technical Training","Transform unskilled and semi-skilled human resources into skilled and competitive human resource by providing short-term and medium-term skill development and technical training.",""],[1,"238","1","Skilled Labor Production Program","Skilled labor production program: Development of labor skills according to market demand, development of skills for internal and foreign employment, and development of a labor demand and supply information system.",""],[1,"238","1","Technical and Vocational Education Expansion","Strengthen and expand technical and vocational education to produce skilled labor force with necessary skills for Nepal.",""],[1,"238","1","School-Based Technical Education Policy","Emphasize technical education right from school, and adopt a policy of inculcating skills in students from school education onwards based on their individual abilities, interests and skills.",""],[1,"238","1","National Human Resources Development Sectoral Plan","Prepare a sectoral plan for national human resources development to address the needs of Nepal's long-term development.",""],[1,"238","1","Labor Force Skill Testing and Enhancement Program","Conduct skill testing and skill enhancement program of the labor force in the labor market in order to address the demand of national labor needs.",""],[1,"240","1","Trade Negotiation Skills and Capacity Building Programme","Enhance trade negotiation skills and build capacity accordingly in the public and private sectors.",""]],"91":[[1,"105","5","Inclusive Education Access for Children with Disabilities","Ensure access to education for children with all types of disabilities, including autism.",""],[1,"112","1","Mobile Education Camps in High Mountain Areas","Conduct mobile education camps in high mountain areas.",""],[1,"112","1","Mobile Education Programme in the Himalayan Region","Conduct mobile education programs in the Himalayan region.",""],[1,"113","7","Disabled Students Support Program","Disabled students support program: Make available basic level education in local schools for students who have become disabled due to various reasons.",""],[1,"161","1","Universal Learning Methods for Children with Learning Disabilities","Teaching and learning through universal learning methods for children with learning disabilities.",""],[1,"161","1","Parent Education Adaptation for Inclusive Teaching","Adapt parent education to the teaching process.",""],[1,"162","1","Expanded Early Childhood Development Access Programme","Enhance access of all groups and communities to early childhood development programs for the mental and physical development of children, and their capacity to use such services.",""],[1,"162","1","Targeted Education Quality Improvement for Dalit Children","Conduct targeted programs to improve the quality of education and learning of Dalit children.",""]],"92":[[1,"85","2","Safe and Managed Foreign Employment Reform","it is necessary to make foreign employment additionally safe, managed and dignified, while identifying labour destinations that offer attractive service and facilities to conclude bilateral labour agreements.",""],[1,"86","2","Safe and Dignified Foreign Employment Reform","For this, strategies and programs that are being implemented include promotion of domestic employment, bringing to an end compulsion for foreign employment and making it safe and dignified, expansion of contribution-based social security and raising productivity through skill development.",""],[1,"89","1","Foreign Employment Management and Protection Measures","Make foreign employment safe, dignified, orderly and highly profitable.",""],[1,"91","2","Foreign Employment Management and Migrant Worker Protection Measures","Identify new and attractive destinations offering high income and safe working environment for foreign employment and ensure signing labor agreements.",""],[1,"92","3","National Migration Policy Formulation","Formulate a national migration policy.",""],[1,"92","3","Migrant Worker Record-Keeping System","Systematically keep records of migrant workers.",""],[1,"92","3","Migrant Worker Skills Development and Capacity Building","Skill development and capacity building of migrant workers and employment of domestic workers in related fields.",""],[1,"92","3","Labor Monitoring Strengthening","Make labor monitoring effective.",""],[1,"93","4","Safe Migration and Foreign Employment Management Program","Conduct a safe migration program for safe, orderly, dignified and productive foreign employment.",""],[1,"94","1","Program to Strengthen Nepali Missions in Labor Destination Countries","Program to strengthen Nepali missions in labor destination countries: Monitor the workplaces in the destination countries.","Labour and Foreign Employment Ministries | Foreign Affairs Ministries"]],"93":[[1,"125","6","Vehicle Fleet Modernization for Cleaner Transport","Upgrade old fossil fuel-based vehicles into sustainable environment friendly vehicles based on latest technology.",""],[1,"126","3","Resilient Road Construction Standards","Maintain sustainability and resilience in road construction.",""],[1,"126","3","Road Safety Measures","Minimize road accidents by adopting necessary measures for road safety.",""],[1,"126","3","Accessible Transport and Urban Infrastructure Design","Design and construct road transport and urban infrastructure to render them accessible to all types of disabled persons.",""],[1,"129","5","National Road Safety Master Plan Review and Enforcement","To make roads safe and accessible, review national road safety master plan and enforce it.",""],[1,"227","1","Clean Public Transport Transition","Make public transport reliable, technology-friendly, and clean energy based.",""],[1,"227","1","Pedestrian and Bicycle Infrastructure Improvement","Ensure easy and safe passage for bicycles and pedestrians, and construct mandatory footpaths on the right and left sides of highways in market areas.",""],[1,"227","1","Vehicle Emissions Reduction Measures","Displace old smoke-emitting vehicles.",""]],"94":[[1,"132","3","Transport Authority Establishment and Agency Management Reform","Establish a transport authority and manage transport-related offices and agencies.",""],[1,"133","1","Legal Harmonization for Construction Delivery Models","Amend the provisions of existing laws and bring harmony in sectoral laws to enable using of these methods and models.",""]],"95":[[1,"135","2","Security Printing Sector Institutional Restructuring and Professional Development Program","Professional development program of security printing: Make security printing self-reliant, professional and competitive by institutional restructuring of the printing sector.",""]],"96":[[1,"124","2","Department of Printing Modernization","Work has started to strengthen and modernize the Department of Printing, the printing press of the Government of Nepal.",""],[1,"124","2","Ultra-Modern Film Studio and Film City Construction","Construction of a ultra-modern film studio and film city has been started with the objective of developing Nepal into a destination for film shooting, capitalizing on Nepal's unique natural resources and beauty.",""],[1,"126","5","Mass Media Sector Reform","Increase citizens' access to information by making the mass media sector dignified, organized, responsible and effective.",""],[1,"126","5","Human Resource Capacity Building for Mass Communication","Increase the efficiency of human resources involved in mass communication.",""],[1,"126","5","Postal Service Modernization","Make the postal service modern, competitive and professional.",""],[1,"126","5","Film Shooting and Photography Promotion","Make Nepal an attractive destination for film shooting and photography.",""],[1,"126","5","Printing Sector Regulation and Security Printing Commercialization","Regulate the printing sector and make security printing commercial and competitive to meet national needs.",""],[1,"130","6","Mass Communication Sector Legal and Structural Reform","Carry out legal and structural reforms in the mass communication sector to keep it impartial, neutral, responsible and professionally driven.",""],[1,"130","6","Social Network Misuse Control Measures","Curb misuse of social network.",""],[1,"131","2","Postal Service Diversification and Modernization","Manage infrastructure related to postal service and diversify its jurisdiction of work, modernize and commercialize service delivery.",""],[1,"131","2","Printing Sector Human Resource Development and Regulation","By producing necessary human resources in the printing sector, increase contribution to the economy through promotion and regulation of this sector.",""],[1,"131","2","Printing Sector Institutional Restructuring","Through institutional restructuring of the printing sector, make security printing safe, reliable, self-reliant, professional and competitive.",""],[1,"131","2","Nepal Film and Cultural Promotion Initiative","To have distinct identity of Nepal's natural and cultural diversity on the global map through use of information technology, promote Nepal as an attractive destination for feature films, photography and intenational film shooting.",""]],"97":[[1,"206","2","Anti-Corruption Strategy and Action Plan Implementation","the National Strategy and Action Plan for the Implementation of the United Nations Convention against Corruption, 2012 has been formulated and implemented to effectively implement the provisions of the convention",""],[1,"206","2","Legal and Institutional Frameworks for Convention Implementation","necessary laws and structures for the implementation of these conventions are being developed and programs are being conducted",""],[1,"206","4","Civil Service Policy and Ethics Reform","it is necessary to revise the policies, regulations, work and ethical behavior related to the civil service",""],[1,"206","4","Civil Servant Capacity-Building Initiative","In order to increase contribution and role of civil servants in achieving the constitutional goals by enhancing the capacity of the civil servants",""],[1,"207","4","Cashless Public Transactions Reform","Design and develop policy, legal, institutional and programmatic measures for fully cashless transactions to end all forms of corrupt practices.",""],[1,"207","4","Public Budget Formulation and Fiscal Discipline Measures","All public bodies should formulate budgets within the prescribed procedures, methods and timeframe and effectively implement them.",""],[1,"207","4","Public Resource Allocation and Revenue Leakage Control","Ensure allocation and mobilization of public resources and means in a frugal, productive and fair manner.",""],[1,"207","4","Revenue Leakage and Evasion Control","Control revenue leakage and evasion and maintain financial balance at each level.",""],[1,"207","5","Political Party Financial Transparency and Frugal Election Management","Make financial transactions of political parties transparent.",""],[1,"210","2","Open Government and Accountable Public Service Reform","Adopt the concept of open government to maintain good governance in public services, and prepare an environment that complies with accountable, transparent and participatory laws.",""],[1,"210","2","Integrity Evaluation Mechanism for High Officials","Develop a mechanism to evaluate the integrity of high officials compulsorily based on indicators.",""],[1,"210","4","Ethics, Integrity, and Conduct Policy Reform","Improve the policies and laws related to ethics, morals, integrity and spiritual understanding necessary for employees working in the government and private sectors, officials and members affiliated to political parties, etc.",""],[1,"210","4","Diplomatic Code of Conduct Compliance Enforcement","Ensure full compliance of the diplomatic code of conduct and its effective use.",""],[1,"213","3","Fiscal and Administrative Good Governance Promotion Program","Fiscal and administrative good governance promotion program: Promote transparency and accountability through digital governance.",""],[1,"213","4","Automated Civil Service Performance Appraisal System","Develop an automated performance appraisal system.",""],[1,"214","2","National Ethics Policy and Morality Promotion Program","Formulate a national ethics policy.",""],[1,"214","2","Ethics Training for Politicians and Administrators","Provide politicians and administrators regular training on ethics and morality.",""],[1,"214","2","Inter-Agency Ethics Exchange Mechanism","Conduct inter- agency exchange of successful and exemplary efforts to maintain ethics and morality in public bodies.",""],[1,"214","2","Community Ethics and Law-Abiding Culture Campaign","Conduct an intensive campaign at the community level on necessary education and culture needed to make citizens aware of their responsibilities and duties towards the state, society and family.",""],[1,"214","2","Legal Education Integration into the Education System","Make citizens aware of their responsibilities and duties to be performed through promotion of law-abiding culture and linking legal education to the education system.",""]],"98":[[1,"231","2","Sustainable Development Goals Implementation Arrangements","Policy and institutional arrangements have been made for the implementation of Sustainable Development Goals, which are the main basis for embodying Nepal's long-term vision.",""],[1,"231","2","Institutionalization of Sustainable Development Achievements","the achievements made from the implementation of policies and programs related to sustainable development should be institutionalized",""],[1,"231","2","Implementation of Plans for Further SDG Progress","emphasis should be placed on the implementation of plans to achieve further progress.",""],[1,"233","1","SDG Coding and Localization in Planning and Budgeting","While formulating annual budget and program, programs and projects are being coded in line with the Sustainable Development Goals.",""],[1,"233","1","Whole-of-Government and Whole-of-Society SDG Collaboration","There is collaboration between the government, private, cooperative and community sectors and development partners to achieve SDGs in consonance with the concept of whole-of-government and whole-of-society.",""],[1,"233","1","SDG Resource Mobilization and Implementation Strategy Update","The assessment of financial resources required to meet the goals and targets set for the year 2030 and the resource mobilization and implementation strategy have been updated.",""],[1,"233","1","Institutional Capacity Reform for SDG Acceleration","In order to achieve satisfactory outcomes in all the indicators of Sustainable Development Goals and to accelerate implementation, there should be further reforms in institutional capacity.",""],[1,"234","5","SDG Localization and Mainstreaming Programme","Taking into consideration the fundamentals of SDGs, implement programs to achieve Sustainable Development Goals by federal, provincial and local governments, private sector, civil society, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, and social organizations.",""],[1,"234","5","Integration of SDGs into Periodic Plans and Budgets","By internalizing Sustainable Development Goals and indicators in the periodic plans and budgets of the three levels of government, accelerate implementation with balance across goals to achieve SDGs.",""],[1,"237","3","SDG Localization and Mainstreaming","Internalize SDGs in policies, plans, budgets and programs of the federal, provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"240","3","SDG Localization and Mainstreaming Support","Empower the federation, provinces and local levels to implement SDGs.",""],[1,"241","2","Targeted SDG Acceleration Programs","Conduct additional programs targeted at sectors and communities with low progress in achieving Sustainable Development Goals.",""]],"99":[[1,"135","5","Water Resource Protection and Recharge Initiative","Identify and protect surface and underground water resources, encourage and promote water recharge and multi-use, integrated use and reuse of water resources.",""],[1,"135","5","Chure Area Protection for Water Security","Protect the Chure area for sustainable management of irrigation and drinking water needs.",""],[1,"148","5","Surface Water Conservation and Groundwater Recharge Program","Implement a program to conserve surface water sources and recharge underground water sources in every settlement.",""],[1,"148","5","Rural Pond and Water Storage Construction Campaign","Carry out campaigns to construct ponds and water storage facilities in rural settlements.",""],[1,"148","5","Rainwater Harvesting System Development","Develop a system that can collect rainwater and use it for drinking and irrigation purposes.",""]],"100":[[1,"79","2","Multi-Dimensional Water Resources Utilization Program","Program for multi-dimensional utilization of water resources: Water resource utilization based on River Basin Master Plan.",""],[1,"130","2","Multiple Use Water Resources Management Measures","Take measures for multiple use of water resources, which comprise : integrated management and use of water resources based on river basin planning, identification and protection of underground water resources, establishment of river basin structures under the jurisdiction of the Water and Energy Commission at the provincial level, distribution of water resources, keeping records, testing of use.",""]],"101":[[1,"148","6","River Source Cleaning and Conservation Program","To purify the Bagmati and all other tributaries in the Kathmandu valley, and rivers flowing through major cities of the country as well as water sources that are close to settlements, make a mandatory arrangements for alternative sewerage and treatment system.",""],[1,"148","7","Integrated Urban Waste Management Program","Integrated urban waste management program: For scientific management of wastes through cyclical use with classification at sources, extend technical support and",""],[1,"149","1","Urban Waste Treatment System Development","Develop waste treatment system, including management of waste treatment centers and landfill sites, in all cities.",""],[1,"149","1","Separate Municipal Waste Collection Standards","Make arrangements for collecting biodegradable, non-biodegradable and recyclable wastes separately through local levels by developing separate standards for management of these wastes.",""],[1,"149","1","Plastic Use Reduction and Burning Ban","Discourage the use of plastic materials and prohibit burning plastics.",""]],"102":[[1,"41","3","Private Sector Investment Promotion and Regulatory Reform","Attract private sector investment by implementing policy, legal, and structural reforms, ensuring that the government plays a supportive and catalytic role.",""],[1,"41","3","Low-Cost Technology, Infrastructure, and Finance Support","Facilitate the provision of low-cost technology, infrastructure, and financial resources to increase competitiveness.",""],[1,"41","3","Fair Competition Code of Conduct","Formulate and enforce a code of conduct to promote fair competition and professional conduct in the marketplace.",""],[1,"41","3","Public-Private Partnership and Foreign Investment Promotion","Encourage public-private partnership and collaboration with foreign investors to attract private-sector investment.",""],[1,"41","3","Private Sector Social Responsibility Promotion","Strengthen the culture of social responsibility by the private sector.",""],[1,"41","3","Private Sector and NGO Monitoring Mechanism","Establish a mechanism for the regular monitoring of activities of the private sector and non-governmental organizations.",""],[1,"41","3","NGO Coordination with Local Governments","Ensure that Non- governmental organizations operate in coordination with the local governments, and mobilize resources in the areas of national needs and priorities only.",""],[1,"41","3","NGO Facilitation Agency Strengthening","Strengthen and empower the agencies responsible for facilitating the operations of national and international non-governmental organizations, and making them efficient, robust, and accountable.",""],[1,"44","4","Private Sector Strengthening Program","Private and non-governmental sector strengthening program: Promote private sector investment and enhance its competitive capacity.",""]],"103":[[1,"72","3","Special Economic Zones and Dry Ports Development","promote international trade by emphasizing infrastructure development measures like special economic zones and dry ports.",""],[1,"78","1","Trade-Enhancing Infrastructure Development Programme","To promote international trade, lay emphasis on programs that help in building trade-enhancing infrastructure such as special economic zones, dry ports, etc.",""]],"104":[[1,"33","2","Economic Policy and Productivity Enhancement Measures","Increasing production and productivity by applying domestic and foreign capital and technology.",""],[1,"33","2","Capital, Labor, and Technology Coordination for Comparative Advantage","Coordinating the flow of capital, labor and technology in areas of comparative advantage by ensuring, among others, participation and cooperation of the private and cooperative sectors.",""],[1,"33","2","Labor-Intensive Employment Promotion Measures","Solving the persistent unemployment problem in the country by optimum utilization of the demographic dividend and achieving high economic growth by promoting labor-intensive economic activities.",""],[1,"33","2","Natural Resource Efficiency and Digital Growth Strategy","Making prudent use of available natural resources and ensure sustainable economic growth by tapping the opportunities created by information technology and networking.",""],[1,"33","3","Agricultural Productivity Enhancement through Investment and Good Governance","Increase productivity in the agriculture sector by enhanced investment and application of the principles of good governance.",""],[1,"33","3","Manufacturing Sector Expansion for Youth Employment","Expanding manufacturing industries to create employment opportunities for the youths within the country.",""],[1,"33","3","Structural Transformation of the Service Sector","Under the service sector, which contributes 63 percent to the country's economy, prioritizing areas with high comparative advantage and adopting appropriate policy for structural transformation of the economy.",""],[1,"37","2","Production and Productivity Enhancement Measures","Increase availability and use of resources, tools, skills, and technology used in the production cycle to increase sectoral production and productivity in the economy.",""]],"105":[[1,"34","4","Cooperative Sector Regulatory and Governance Reform","Operating cooperatives according to the principles, policies, regulations and standards set for co-operatives.",""],[1,"34","4","Cooperative Self-Regulation and Good Governance Strengthening","Enhancing self-regulation and good governance in cooperatives.",""],[1,"34","4","Cooperative Investment and Lending for Productive Sectors","Focusing on investment and lending of cooperatives in productive sectors and employment generation.",""],[1,"34","4","Cooperative Savings Protection Measures","Minimizing and mitigating risk to the saving of ordinary citizens in cooperatives.",""],[1,"34","4","Second-Tier Cooperative Regulatory Mechanism","Establishing a second-tier regulatory mechanism for the cooperative sector.",""],[1,"34","4","Special Regulation and Monitoring Arrangements for Savings and Credit Cooperatives","Taking into account the significant turnover, establishing special arrangements for regulation and monitoring saving and credit oriented cooperatives ..",""],[1,"38","2","Cooperative Sector Strengthening Measures","Ensure the flow of resources and capital of the cooperative sectors to the productive sector rather than in activities related to financial mediation; Enforce self-regulation and ensure good governance in cooperatives that deal with saving and loan; Establish and operate credit information centers, saving and credit guarantee funds, and stabilization funds, and make it mandatory to return citizens' savings immediately upon demand to reduce the risk in financial transactions of cooperatives.",""],[1,"38","2","Second-Tier Cooperative Regulatory Body","Establish a second-tier regulatory body for regulation and monitoring.",""]],"106":[[1,"36","3","Informal Economy Formalization and Compliance Programme","Increase registration and book-keeping behaviour of informal economic establishments.",""],[1,"36","3","Incentive-Based Formalization of Legitimate Informal Businesses","Formalize legitimate but informal businesses through incentive programmes.",""],[1,"36","3","Counterfeit and Illegal Production Enforcement","Control and punish counterfeit and illegal productions and transactions.",""],[1,"36","3","Household Production Accounting System Development","Develop an accounting system for unobserved household productions and services.",""],[1,"36","3","Informal Financial Transaction Control and Anti-Money Laundering Measures","Control informal financial transactions; strengthen legal and institutional arrangements to control activities such as illegal transactions, smuggling across border areas, commercial fraud and deflection and money laundering and other financial crimes.",""]],"107":[[1,"40","3","Foreign Exchange Earnings Expansion Strategy","Identify, develop, and expand potential areas for foreign exchange earnings.",""],[1,"40","3","Service Sector Export Development Initiative","Develop service sectors such as information technology, hydropower, and tourism as a means of earning foreign exchange.",""],[1,"40","3","Formal Remittance Channel Incentive and Informal Transfer Control","Incentivize the flow of remittances through formal channels, and control informal transactions.",""],[1,"40","3","Current Account Pressure Mitigation Measures","Take policy initiatives to mitigate the negative impact on the current account and balance of payment due to the outflow of foreign currency for education, tourism, etc.",""],[1,"42","5","Foreign Exchange System Strengthening Program","Foreign exchange system strengthening program: Review the exchange rate system of Nepali currency based on need and suitability.",""],[1,"43","4","Remittance Flow Management Program","Remittance flow management program: Encourage remittance inflow through the banking system.",""]],"108":[[1,"40","3","Foreign Investment Approval Automation","Automate the foreign investment approval process.",""],[1,"40","3","Illegal Transaction Control Measures","Reduce pressure on the balance of payments by controlling illegal transactions such as online gambling, cryptocurrency, and hundi that may occur through misuse of information technology.",""]],"109":[[1,"40","4","Formalization of the Informal Economy","Identify the size and nature of informal economy sectors.",""],[1,"44","2","Formalization Program for Informal Economic Activities","Formalization program of informal and unaccounted economic activities: Ensure promotion of electronic transactions, integrate the institutional registration system, and facilitate registration and accounting system.",""],[1,"44","2","Border Area Regulation Against Illegal Activities","Regulate border areas by controlling illegal activities within the facade of an informal economy.",""],[1,"44","2","Household Services Accounting and Evaluation System","Establish an accounting and evaluation system for the time and efforts spent by family members on household services.",""],[1,"45","2","Formalization of the Informal Economy","It is expected that formalization of the informal economy will contribute to growth.",""],[1,"63","7","Informal Economy Formalization and Compliance Reform","Reform measures to be taken in this regard will formalization of informal sector and controling illegal activities, smuggling, commercial fraud and money laundering.",""]],"110":[[1,"41","2","Intergovernmental Finance Management Reform","Increase the revenue capacity of the provincial and local levels, and review tax and non-tax revenue rates by studying revenue potential.",""],[1,"44","3","Intergovernmental Fiscal Management Reform Program","15)Inter-governmental fiscal management program: Reform of provincial and local revenue administration and enhance their capacity.",""]],"111":[[1,"53","5","Resilient Physical and Social Infrastructure Investment","To reduce the incremental cost of capital, substantial investments have to be made in modern, resilient, sustainable and strategic physical infrastructure, information and communication technology and health and education-related infrastructural programmes and projects.",""]],"112":[[1,"70","5","Agricultural Land Classification and Production Zone Development","Ensure pragmatic classification of land with coordination of all three levels of government.",""],[1,"70","5","Agricultural Land Conservation and Consolidation Measures","Increase agricultural productions by taking such measures as conservation of arable land, utilization of land that has fallen barren, minimizing land fragmentation and establishing larger production zones.",""]],"113":[[1,"45","2","Sectoral Program Implementation for Economic Growth","During the plan period, major sectoral programs will be implemented effectively, which will increase the production and productivity of the overall economy and will ultimately support economic growth.",""],[1,"45","2","Public and Private Construction Expansion","Construction activities by the general government and private sectors will take momentum, Construction of residential buildings, public infrastructure development and reconstruction after the Jajarkot earthquake will have a positive impact.",""],[1,"45","2","Human Resource Utilization for Productive Sectors","human resources will have been utilized in productive sector to optimize the benefits of demographic dividends; innovation and entrepreneurship will have been promoted; and sustainable use of water resources, forest resources, minerals and other natural resources will have been ascertained.",""],[1,"45","2","Federal Governance System Implementation","Through effective implementation of the federal governance system, the provincial and local economies will pick up economic dynamism.",""],[1,"45","2","Intergovernmental and Multi-Sector Collaboration for Capital Formation","Similarly, capital formation will be enhanced through the strong, consolidated and collaboration with complementarity among the tiers of the governments, private sector, cooperatives and community sectors.",""],[1,"73","4","Stakeholder Transparency, Accountability, and Responsibility Framework","Ensure transparency, responsibility and accountability of stakeholders - persons and agencies, linked in various stages of production to consumption.",""],[1,"73","4","Regulatory System Strengthening for Relevant Agencies","Make regulatory system of relevant agencies effective.",""],[1,"73","4","Intergovernmental Coordination for Institutional Strengthening in the Productive Sector","Establish linkages between inter-governmental agencies and various levels of government for institutional strengthening in the productive sector.",""]],"114":[[1,"74","2","High Mountain Collective Farming and Agroforestry Program","Introduce collective farming system in the high mountain areas in the form of agricultural farm.",""],[1,"74","2","Wild Animal Farming Initiative","In collaboration with the government and local households, run wild animal farms such as those of deer, musk deer, wild boar, and local species of pheasants.",""],[1,"74","2","Barren Land and Riverbank Production Linkage Program","Link barren land, river banks, sloppy land, forest areas and riverine sections with production and employment.",""]],"115":[[1,"75","3","Provincial Organic Fertilizer Production Program","Organic fertilizer production program at the provincial level.",""],[1,"75","3","Chemical Fertilizer Factory Establishment","Establishment of a chemical fertilizer factory based on new technology.",""]],"116":[[1,"78","3","Market System Development and Assurance Program","Program for market system development and assurance: Assurance of market for sale of every product of the producer.",""],[1,"78","3","Agricultural Produce Collection and Direct Purchase App System","Develop an app that helps in collection and purchase of agricultural produce from the farm gate and build a system of direct purchase and marketing.",""],[1,"93","1","Market Access Support for Produced Goods","Ensure market for produced goods.",""]],"117":[[1,"85","2","Formalization of Informal Work and Care Economy","It is also necessary to formalize informal jobs and caregiving work as well as informal economy to make work dignified.",""],[1,"87","1","National Master Plan on Elimination of Child Labor","To address the root cause of child labor, National Master Plan on Elimination of Child Labor 2018-2028 is being implemented, under which the campaign of declaring child labor free local levels is ongoing.",""],[1,"88","3","Labor Governance and Inspection Reform","Reform in labor management: Create an environment for youths to work in Nepal.",""],[1,"91","3","Labor Management Reform Package","(5) Reforms in labor management: Maintain good industrial relations through promotion of decent work.",""],[1,"94","2","Decent Jobs Promotion Program","6) Decent jobs promotion program: Develop clear standard for decent employment.",""]],"118":[[1,"85","2","Collaborative Local Employment Creation Initiative","All three levels of government are required to make collaborative efforts to create local employment opportunities in order to properly mobilize money received as remittances, knowledge, skill, experience, competence, work culture, technology, entrepreneurship and self-confidence of persons gained through foreign employment.",""],[1,"90","1","Foreign Migrant Worker Record-Keeping System","Keep record of foreign migrant workers.",""],[1,"90","1","Domestic Labour Market Pressure Reduction Measures","Reduce pressure created by foreign migant workers on the domestic labour market and, in order to create opprtunities for local labor, promote good industrial relations.",""],[1,"90","2","Returnee Worker Reintegration Program","Make reintegration program effective; emphasize on building social capital by attracting investment from non-resident Nepalis.",""],[1,"90","3","Decentralized Foreign Employment Service Delivery","Decentralize service delivery in the foreign employmnet sector down to the local level.",""],[1,"92","2","Returnee Worker Skills Certification and Productive Sector Mobilization","Certify the skills of returnee workers and keep records systematically.",""],[1,"92","2","Remittance and Foreign Employment Investment Mobilization","Mobilize the remittance income, knowledge, skills, work culture, technology, entrepreneurship and confidence gained through foreign employment in the productive sector.",""],[1,"92","2","Foreign Employment Bond Management and Investment Incentive","Properly manage foreign employment bond and encourage citizens who are in foreign employment to invest in shares and other productive sectors.",""],[1,"93","2","Foreign Migrant Worker Skills Study","Study the work done by foreign migrant workers.",""]],"119":[[1,"101","1","Nuclear Technology Safety and Regulatory Framework","For safe and peaceful use of nuclear technology and other technological regulation and technical analysis services, related laws and regulations are being formulated and implemented by various agencies of the Government of Nepal.",""]],"120":[[1,"101","3","Infrastructure, Technology and Resource Provision for Social Sectors","Make provision for physical infrastructure, latest technology, machines, tools and resources necessary for health, education and skill development, science and technology and youth and sports sectors.",""],[1,"101","3","Efficient Use of Existing Public Infrastructure and Equipment","Make efficient use of available physical infrastructures and equipments.",""],[1,"101","3","Public and Private Investment Mobilization for Social Sectors","Ensure adequate investment from the government and private sector for these sectors.",""]],"121":[[1,"102","3","Institutional Capacity Enhancement for Health and Education Service Providers","Enhance institutional capacity of all government and private sector service providers in the fields of health and education to provide quality and reliable services.",""],[1,"102","3","Resilient Human Resource Development System","Make the human resource development system resilient to all kinds of risks and disasters.",""]],"122":[[1,"102","4","Health Policy Integration on Environmental Determinants","Properly address issues related to larger determinants of health and environmental health in health policies and programs.",""],[1,"110","3","Pesticide Use Regulation for Public Health Risk Reduction","Regulation of pesticide use in collaboration with relevant stakeholders to minimize public health risks.",""]],"123":[[1,"102","4","Healthy Lifestyle and Preventive Care Campaigns","Launch enough campaigns for improvement of people's attitude and behaviour for healthy lifestyle and promotion of preventive healthcare.",""],[1,"107","4","Public Health Promotion Campaign","Run public health promotion campaign through healthy lifestyle and practice of yoga.",""],[1,"110","1","Occupational Health System Institutionalization","Evaluate impact of development projects, industries, factories and commerce and trade on public health and institutionalize occupational health systems.",""],[1,"110","3","Mental Health and Alternative Health Program","15) Mental health and alternative health program: Prevention and control of drug abuse; suicide prevention and other mental health promotion activities.",""],[1,"110","3","Ward and Community-Level Citizens' Good Health Program Expansion","Expand the citizens' good health program down to the ward and community levels in coordination with organized institutions, cooperatives and communities.",""],[1,"110","3","Community-Level My Health, My Responsibility Campaign","Extend \"My Health, My Responsibility\" campaign down to the community level.",""],[1,"110","3","Senior Citizens' Physical, Mental and Spiritual Health Promotion","Promote physical, mental and spiritual health of senior citizens through recreation centres, libraries, yoga centers, community learning and skill exchange centres.",""]],"124":[[1,"103","4","Provincial Referral Hospital Construction","Build referral hospitals in all provinces.",""],[1,"103","4","District Hospital Upgrading for Specialist Services","Upgrade district level hospitals to make available minimum specialist services.",""],[1,"108","5","Specialized Service Hospital Operation Program","To provide specialized services in all seven provincces, either establish or manage a hospital with at least 300 to 500 beds in each province.",""],[1,"108","5","Provincial Specialized Hospital Development","Develop these hospitals as international level service provider hospitals for treatment of cancer, kidney, mental and nerve related diseases, orthopedic diseases, as well as for handling disasters and accidents.",""],[1,"108","5","Kanti Children's Hospital Upgrade and Provincial Children's Hospitals","Kanti Children's Hospital will be upgraded for development in the concept of Children's Health Science Institute and under it specialized children's hospitals will be run in each province.",""]],"125":[[1,"103","5","Health Tourism Promotion Initiative","Promote health tourism service of international standard through collaboration of the government, private and community sectors.",""],[1,"111","2","International Health Tourism Promotion Program","International health tourism promotion program: With active participation of government, private and community secors, promote high quality health services, integrated health system with modern, Ayurvedic, natural and alternative healthcare system.",""]],"126":[[1,"103","6","Multi-sectoral Non-Communicable Disease Control Initiative","Reduce and control non- communicable diseases with coordination, collaboration, co-funding and shared responsibility of all levels, agencies and parties.",""],[1,"103","6","Emerging and Re-emerging Disease and Malnutrition Control Programme","Control emerging and re-emerging health problems and malnutrition.",""],[1,"103","6","Resilient Public Health System Development","Develop a resilient public health system that can address climate-related health issues impacting on human health.",""],[1,"103","6","Single Health Policy Institutionalization","Institutionalize the concept of a 'single health policy' to address health issues such as antimicrobial resistance, vector- borne diseases, diseases related to old age, etc.",""],[1,"109","3","Multisectoral Nutrition Programme III Implementation","While giving priority to implementation of Multisectoral Nutrition Programme III, carry out programs targeted to groups and communities based on their special needs and priorities.",""],[1,"109","3","Micronutrient Deficiency Reduction Programs","To address deficiency of micronutrients, conduct short-term, medium-term and long-term programs, giving priority to local and indigenous produce in supplementation, fortification and food diversification.",""],[1,"109","4","Vector-Borne and Communicable Disease Control Program","Program for control and prevention of vector-borne, communicable and non- communicable diseases and diseases on the verge of elimination: Control of vector- borne diseases like malaria, kala-azar and dengue, and other vector-borne diseases; infectious diseases like tuberculosis, HIV/AIDS, leprosy;",""],[1,"109","4","Non-Communicable Disease Mitigation Program","and program for mitigation of non-communicable diseases like high blood pressure, heart diseases, nerve diseases, diabetes, cancer, kidney diseases, drug addiction, diabetes, cancer, kidney diseases.",""],[1,"109","4","Tuberculosis Diagnosis, Treatment and Prevention Campaign","Diagnosis, treatment and prevention program for multi-drug resistant and all other types of TB and launching campaign to attain \"Tuberculosis-free Nepal\".",""],[1,"110","2","Public Health Laboratory Strengthening Program","Public health laboratory strengthening program: Specialized services related to cancer testing in view of biological safety.",""]],"127":[[1,"104","2","Health Sector Governance and Quality Control Strengthening","institutionally strengthen regulatory, monitoring and quality control mechanism and enhance ledership capacity.",""],[1,"104","2","Community Participation in Health Planning and Oversight","Maintain accountability by increasing community involvement in planning, monitoring and evaluation activities carried out by various agencies.",""],[1,"104","3","Health Sector Investment Expansion and Governance Reform","Increase investment in the health sector according to international standards and national commitment.",""],[1,"107","3","Health Sector Investment Enhancement Program","Investment enhancement program in the health sector: On the basis of population, geography and disease burden, the state will invest in basic health services at a per unit rate, and for this, the federal and state governments will provide financial and technical support to the local level.",""],[1,"107","3","Health Budget Allocation Increase","Gradually increase the share of allocation in the total national budget for the health sector.",""],[1,"107","3","Health Sector Budget and Programme Milestone System","Enforce a milestone system for federal, provincial and local level budget and program implementation.",""],[1,"107","3","Health Harmful Consumption Tax Measures","Raise taxes to discourage the consumption of tobacco products, alcohol as well as drinks and food products that have been prepared with materials harmful for public health.",""],[1,"107","3","Additional Health Investment Mobilization","Identify additional sources for investment to increase investment in the health sector.",""]],"128":[[1,"104","6","Educational Infrastructure and Digital Learning Enhancement","Enhance educational quality through the best use of communication and information technology.",""],[1,"113","2","Physical Infrastructure Improvement Program for Educational Institutions","Physical infrastructure improvement program of educational institutions: Equip educational institutions with adequate teachers and basic minimum infrastructure such as earthquake-resistant smart classrooms, library, laboratory, toilet with clean drinking water, etc.",""],[1,"113","2","Educational Institution Database Development","Furthermore, prepare detailed database of educational institutions.",""],[1,"113","3","Inter-Agency Coordination for Social Infrastructure Accessibility","Establish inter-agency coordination for raising quality and accessibility of social sector infrastructure - education, health, drinking water, sanitation, to women, children, senior citizens, disabled people, gender and sexual minority and operationalize them in a friendly way.",""],[1,"128","1","Social Infrastructure Maintenance and Accessibility Measures","Maintain quality and accessibility of infrastructure related to education, health and social sectors.",""]],"129":[[1,"105","2","Climate-Resilient Education System","Strengthen climate-resilient education system.",""]],"130":[[1,"115","1","Indigenous Products and Technology Development Program","Carry out research on intraditional technology of Nepal, and attach importance to their development, promotion and application in production methodology.",""],[1,"115","1","Indigenous Products and Technology Development Academy","Establish \"Indigenous products and technology development academy\" under the Ministry of Education, Science and Technology for development of such products and technology.","Ministry of Education, Science and Technology"],[1,"115","1","Internationalization and Intellectual Property Protection for Indigenous Products","Internationalize indigenous products and technology and protect intellectual property right.",""]],"131":[[1,"121","2","Integrated Transport Management and ICT Connectivity Enhancement","Communication and information technology, in conjunction with with integrated transport management system, play an important role in connecting rural settlements with markets and bolstering support to activities in the economic sector such as industry, tourism, agriculture, energy.",""],[1,"121","2","Policy Coherence for Infrastructure and Climate-Sensitive Development","For development and prosperity of all three levels of government, policy coherence and functional inter-linkages in sectors and dimensions including physical infrastructure, energy, irrigation, drinking water, forest, environment and climate change, communication and information technology are indispensable.",""],[1,"121","2","Information Technology Expansion for National Development","Likewise, the priority of this plan is making maximum use of information technology for overall development of the country by strengthening the linkages with national and international communities.",""],[1,"125","3","Integrated Transport Infrastructure Planning and Coordination","Establish coordination and inter-linkages between the sectoral policies of infrastructure development.",""],[1,"126","2","Strategic Infrastructure Mobilization through Multi-Sector Coordination","In coordination and collaboration of governments at different levels and coupled with partnsership of public, private and cooperative sectors, ensure strategic mobilization in construction of proper infrastructure.",""],[1,"131","5","Integrated Infrastructure-Productivity Linkage Framework","Forge an integrated concept for interlinkages between infrastructure development and production and productivity at all three levels of government.",""],[1,"131","5","Social Infrastructure Modernization for Productivity","For conservation and modernization of social infrastructure like traditional knowledge, skills and practices, ensure their interlinkages with productivity.",""]],"132":[[1,"122","5","Driving License Issuance Process Reform","It is necessary to make driving license distribution process fast, efficient and qualitative.",""],[1,"122","5","Embossed Vehicle Number Plate System","In order to link transport management to modern system, it is necessary to fix up embossed number plate on vehicles, and make the system work effectively.",""],[1,"122","5","Transport Management Procedures Guide Amendment","The Transport Management Procedures Guide, 2003 has been amended to",""],[1,"123","1","Domestic Vehicle Registration Facilitation","facilitate the registration process of vehicles manufactured or assembled in Nepal.",""],[1,"123","1","Electronic Vehicle Driving License System","The service of the electronic vehicle driving license system with electronic payment has been put into operation as a test case.",""],[1,"125","6","Digital Public Transport Service Management","Provide services such as driving license distribution and management and regulation of vehicles through fully digitalized system.",""]],"133":[[1,"124","3","Agricultural Infrastructure Programmes","Launching programmes in these areas fall in priority of all three levels of government, even though expected result is not visible yet.",""]],"134":[[1,"126","3","Public-Private Partnership for Multipurpose Projects","Implement the concept of public-private partnership to build and operate multi-purpose projects.",""],[1,"126","3","Multipurpose Projects for Electricity, Irrigation, and Tourism","Focusing on sustainable development, expansion and management of electricity, irrigation and tourism, put emphasis on implementation of multipurpose projects.",""],[1,"128","2","Transmission Line Land Classification and Plot Allocation","Make arrangements for classification of land and allocation of plots for construction of transmission lines.",""],[1,"128","2","Integrated Road Network Transport System Development","Develop a sustainable and faster transport system by interconnecting road networks.",""],[1,"128","3","Public-Private Partnership System for Transport Infrastructure","Implement public-private partnership system based on feasibility in the field of transport infrastructure.",""],[1,"128","3","Road Maintenance Expenditure System","Bring into effect road maintenance expenditure system in different levels of government; make arrangements for autonomus source tapping for the Road Board to moblize resources for repair and maintenance of roads.",""],[1,"128","3","Foreign Investment and Public-Private Partnership for Electricity and Reservoir Dam Projects","Make electricity and reservoir dam projects development-friendly for foreign investments and implement the concept of public-private partnership to this end.",""],[1,"128","3","Long-Term Reservoir Dam Development Strategy","Adopt reservoir dam projects as a long-term strategy for power development.",""],[1,"128","4","Road Construction Cost and Time Reduction Reform","To link infrastructure development with economic benefits in an objective manner, initiate policy, legal and structural reforms to reduce cost, time and distance in road construction.",""]],"135":[[1,"129","3","Private-Academic-Government Technology Collaboration for Infrastructure Innovation","Strengthen collaboration between private, academic and government agencies in utilization of new technologies and practices developed in the infrastructure sector, and in this regard, consolidate evidence-based policy and planning process.",""],[1,"129","3","Local Resource and Traditional Skills Utilization Policy","Adopt a policy of utilizing resources and traditional skills and knowledge available at the local level, and establish intellectual property rights that helps in transfer of knowledge from generations to generations and upgrade it.",""]],"136":[[1,"131","5","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Financing","Address environmental and climate-related challenges by using climate finance in infrastructure development.",""],[1,"136","1","Infrastructure Development Program Based on Real-Time Data and Disaster Risk Accounting","Conduct infrastructure development program based on real-time data and disaster risk accounting.",""]],"137":[[1,"132","2","Road Infrastructure Maintenance Program","Road infrastructure maintenance program: Implement immediately heavy vehicle management policy for the regulation of heavy load capacity vehicles for sustainable management of constructed roads.",""],[1,"132","4","Physical Infrastructure Assets Management System Development Program","Physical infrastructure assets management system development program: Strengthen assets management system of roads, including other physical infrastructure, roads maintenance expenditure system and road bridge management information system to enhance their effectiveness.",""],[1,"133","1","Road Toll System Implementation for Bridge Reconstruction","Ensure effective implementation of road tolls system to provide long-term resources required to rebuild dilapidated bridges.",""]],"138":[[1,"132","5","Financial Resource Mobilization for Infrastructure Development","Financial resource management program: Mobilize financial resources in infrastructure development, keeping in mind dimensions of public-private partnership, adopt various methods including innovative finance model, hybrid annuity model,",""],[1,"133","2","Mineral-Based Construction Materials Management Program","Mineral-based construction materials management program: Establish a comprehensive construction materials industry by the government itself or in partnership with the private sector.",""]],"139":[[1,"135","3","International Film Shooting Destination Development Program","International film shooting destination development program: In order to promote Nepal as an attractive destination for international film shooting, develop necessary infrastructure in the Himalayan region in consultation with the Film Development Corporation.",""]],"140":[[1,"135","5","Archaeological Resource Identification and Conservation Program","Carry out programs for identification and conservation of wells, stone spouts, wetlands, lakes and ponds, rivers and other watershed areas which carry traditional archaeological significance.",""]],"141":[[1,"145","3","Urban Stakeholder Capacity and Coordination Mechanism","Enhance the capacity of stakeholders working in urban infrastructure development and service sector with better coordination.",""],[1,"145","3","Urban Information and Service Delivery Improvement","Improve access to urban information and make urban service delivery effective.",""],[1,"145","3","Urban Jurisdiction Delineation and Intergovernmental Coordination Framework","Delineate clear areas of jurisdiction for the three levels of government and develop the mechanism of coordination, collaboration and co-invesment effective.",""],[1,"145","3","Technology-Based Urban Government System","Make urban government structure and system based on technology.",""],[1,"145","3","Urban Security and Inequality Coordination Support","Provide necessary resources to coordinate efforts to address growing security challenges and economic inequality in the city.",""],[1,"145","5","Urban Spatial Planning and Settlement Legislation Reform","Establish spatial planning system by enacting urban and settlement legislation and reforming policy.",""],[1,"145","5","Integrated Urban Information System","Establish integrated urban information system.",""],[1,"147","2","Spatial Planning System Reform and Urban and Residential Planning Law","Establish spatial planning system by reforming policy and enacting urban and residential planning law.",""],[1,"147","2","Integrated Urban Information Management System","Establish an integrated urban information management system.",""],[1,"147","2","Multi-Level Urban Governance and Service Delivery Coordination","For good governance, service delivery and guarantee of security in the rural and urban sectors, mobilize civil society, security agencies, community organizations and non-governmental organizations through collaboration and coordination of federal, provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"147","2","Strengthening Federal Ministries for Urban Governance","Make relevant federal ministries additionally effective to achieve this goal.",""],[1,"149","2","Urban Good Governance and Institutional Reform Program","Make reforms in the existing policy and institutional arrangements for spatial planning, regulation of land use and physical development and integrated infrastructure development.",""],[1,"149","2","Urban Planning and Human Resource Mobilization","Manage and mobilize physical and human resources (urban planners, architects, technicians, including engineers) required for the formulation and implementation of urban plans at the local level.",""],[1,"149","2","Integrated Urban Economic Corridor Development Mechanism","Develop mechanisms for integrated development of urban economic corridors.",""],[1,"149","2","Urban Stakeholder Communication System","Establish a direct communication system between urban information and stakeholders.",""],[1,"149","3","Kathmandu Valley Development Authority Restructuring and Integrated Urban Development Planning","Prepare an integrated urban development plan to keep the Kathmandu valley as a single development unit where local levels can also feel ownership.",""]],"142":[[1,"156","2","Economic and Social Empowerment of Marginalized Communities","Remove barriers to empowerment and socio-economic mobilization of marginalized groups and communities.",""],[1,"158","2","Inclusive Infrastructure Investment for Marginalized Groups","For economic and social empowerment and mobilization of the indigent, incapacitated, helpless and disabled persons and minorities and marginalized communities, increase investments in social, economic and physical infrastructures in collaboration and partnerhip with the private, cooperative and non-governmental sectors.",""],[1,"158","4","Employment and Income Generation Support for Target Groups","Enhance self-reliance of target groups and communities through opportunities for employment and income generation.",""],[1,"159","2","Capacity Support for Constitutional Commissions","Empower the constitutional commissions established for the upliftment and development of the target groups with resources for relevant research and awareness creation.",""],[1,"163","2","Dalit Empowerment Program","10) Dalit empowerment program: Carry out campaigns related to elimination of untouchability and caste discrimination at the local level.",""],[1,"163","5","Target Group and Community Self-Reliance Program","12) Program of target group and community self-reliance: Promote economic empowerment, entrepreneurship and employment opportunities for self-reliance of rural and indigent target groups.",""],[1,"163","5","Local Indigenous Crop Production and Marketing Support","Produce and sell local indigenous crops and other products.",""],[1,"163","5","Domestic Liquor Production, Branding and Export Promotion","Make arrangements for controlled production, branding, sales and distribution as well as export promotion of domestic liquor.",""],[1,"163","5","Skills Development and Entrepreneurship Training for Target Groups","To enhance competitive capacity of target groups, communities and genders, conduct skill development training and entrepreneurship development programs.",""],[1,"163","5","Reservation in Education, Health and Public Sector Jobs","Make provision of reservation in education, health and public sector jobs.",""],[1,"165","1","Indigenous Knowledge-Based Livelihood and Entrepreneurship Support","In places with intense settlements of certain specific groups, tribes and communities, carry out indigenous farming, animal husbandry, agriculture or other business operations, entrepreneurship development and marketing by utilizing indigenous knowledge, skills and technology.",""]],"143":[[1,"170","3","Institutional and Systemic Reforms for Fiscal Federalism","To enhance allocative efficiency of public resources, improve implementation capacity and maintain fiscal discipline, institutional and systemic reforms have been made in areas such as revenue mobilization, budget, accounting, internal control, etc ..",""],[1,"170","3","Provincial and Subnational Budget Management Information Systems","For budgeting, management information system such as Provincial Line Ministries Budgetory Information System and Subnational Treasury Account are being implmented.",""],[1,"172","3","Equitable Revenue Sharing and Fiscal Transfer Reform","Make revenue sharing and fiscal tranfer just by analyzing the expenditure needs and capacity of provincial and local governments based on indicators and their ability of revenue mobilization.",""],[1,"172","5","Public Spending Efficiency and Fiscal Responsibility Reform","Improving quality and efficiency of public spending: Optimally utilize the revenue rights and potentials of the provincial and local levels according to their responsibilities, link fiscal transfer with revenue capacity and expenditure needs, ensure financial responsibility in the use of resources.",""],[1,"174","3","Provincial and Local Fiscal Planning and Service Delivery Reform","Determine spending needs of provincial and local levels based on development and service standards, and take steps to make fiscal balance, development management and service delivery effective.",""],[1,"174","3","Project Prioritization and Budget Formulation for Resource Mobilization","Ensure optimum mobilization of resources through selection of projects, their prioritization, classification, budget formulation and its effective implementation.",""],[1,"174","4","Fiscal Federalism Strengthening Reform","Strengthen fiscal federalism by mobilizing internal resources, developing linkages in resource mobilization, efficient resource allocation and effective expenditure management.",""],[1,"175","3","Provincial and Local Public Resource Allocation Efficiency Reform","Identify spending needs at the provincial and local levels, map the available resources and means, and increase mobilization of internal resources.",""],[1,"175","3","Provincial and Local Revenue Source Expansion","Identify and expand the scope of new sources of provincial and local revenue and mobilize provincial",""],[1,"176","1","Prioritized Fiscal Equalization Grant Transfer","Transfer fiscal equalization grants in a prioritized and balanced manner in order to meet the gap between the expenditure needs and revenue capacity of the provinces and local levels.",""],[1,"176","1","Equitable Revenue Sharing and Natural Resource Benefit Distribution","In the areas of revenue sharing, and while increasing investment in natural resources, ensure equitable and just distribution of benefits.",""],[1,"176","1","Revenue Reform Program","Formulate and execute revenue reform program.",""],[1,"176","1","Provincial and Local Public Financial Management Improvement","Improve public financial management of provincial and local levels by ensuring effective planning, budgeting, accounting, internal and external auditing, settlement of irregularities, make arrangements for selection of projects which have completed initial preparation in project bank.",""],[1,"176","1","Implementation Capacity Strengthening","Also raise implementation capacity to this end.",""],[1,"176","1","Public Expenditure Transparency and Fiscal Discipline Reform","Maintain fiscal discipline by making the public expenditure system smart, transparent and capable of documenting the realistic picture of public assets.",""],[1,"176","1","Performance-Based Grant System","Link all types of grants transferred from the federal and provincial governments to performance, and implement an incentive-based grant system.",""],[1,"176","1","Equitable Royalty and Revenue Sharing Reform","Make royalty and revenue sharing equitable.",""],[1,"176","1","Local and Ward Project Prioritization Reform","Make project preparation and prioritization objective at the local and ward levels thereby improving project governance and financial discipline.",""],[1,"177","1","Performance-Based Fiscal Transfer System","financial discipline by adopting a performance-based fiscal transfer system and minimizing fudiciary risks.",""]],"144":[[1,"172","3","Three-Pillar Economic Policy Adoption","Adopt a three-pillar economic policy including the government, private and cooperative sectors and the community.",""],[1,"172","3","Provincial and Local Productive Sector Investment Promotion","Identify productive sectors with comparative advantage at provincial and local levels and create conducive environment for investment, and enhance their utility.",""],[1,"172","3","Provincial and Local Economic Policy Development","Analyze the priorities, facts, data and technical bases to adopt provincial and local economic policies.",""],[1,"173","3","Provincial and Local Investment Exploration and Research Promotion","Promote investment for exploration and research of the specificities and potentials of the province and local level.",""],[1,"173","3","Local Production and Entrepreneurship Promotion","Enhance local production, indigenous knowledge, skills, entrepreneurship and confidence.",""],[1,"173","3","Local Economic Development and Service Delivery Reform","Promote local economic development, simplify service delivery and promote good governance by strengthening governance capacity.",""],[1,"173","3","Economic Institutions Strengthening and Plan Implementation","Make sure of good presence of economic institutions and effective implementation of economic development plan.",""],[1,"173","3","Provincial and Local Value Chain Development","Develop the value chains of production at the provincial and local levels; identify natural and man-made resources and manage, conserve, invest, utilize, and distribe the returns.",""],[1,"173","3","Intergovernmental Financial Management Coordination","Coordinate and facilitate to improve financial management efficiency of all three levels of government.",""],[1,"173","4","Inter-Level Economic Network Development and Fiscal Federalism Strengthening","Establish inter-provincial and inter-local and provincial-local production and means of production, market, access, information system and interconnection of good practices.",""],[1,"174","3","Provincial and Local Economic Policy Framework","After reviewing the existing legal underpinnings and maintaining coordination with the governments at all levels, formulate a guiding policy on provincial and local economies and implement it effectively.",""],[1,"175","1","Provincial and Local Economic Development Programs","Review economic potentials and capacity of the provincial and local levels, and conduct economic programs based on the specificities of the respective level.",""],[1,"175","1","Provincial and Local Resource Mapping Initiative","Identify potentials of the provincial and local levels for economic development (resource mapping), and utilize them and balance the provincial and regional levels, thereby.",""],[1,"175","1","Local Government Co-Investment Model","Delineate responsibility to local governments by designating sample sectors for co-investment.",""],[1,"175","1","Public-Private-Cooperative and Community Participation Projects","Launch projects and programs through models based on public-private-cooperative and community participation.",""],[1,"175","1","Productive Sector Investment Promotion","Enhance production and productivity by promoting investment in the productive sectors.",""],[1,"176","4","Provincial and Local Governance Capacity Building","Increase local participation and inclusiveness in every sector of governance by strengthening administrative federalism, administrative organization and institutional strengthening, human capital formation and mobilization and development of local leadership as well as use of modern technology.",""],[1,"176","4","Local and Provincial Economic Promotion and Regulation","Strengthen the local and provincial economy by promoting and regulating the government and private sectors.",""],[1,"177","1","Strengthening Provincial and Local Economic Bodies","Enhance financial efficiency by strengthening provincial and local level economic bodies.",""]],"145":[[1,"175","1","Climate-Resilient Productivity Enhancement","Increase production and productivity through the use of appropriate and modern technology by controlling the growing fragmentation of arable land and mitigating the impacts of and adapting to the effects of climate change.",""],[1,"175","1","Special Economic Zones and Industrial Infrastructure Development","Raise production and productivity and create employment opportunities by increasing investment in the productive sector, establishing special economic zones at different levels, development of industrial estates, industrial centers, industrial villages and economic centers.",""],[1,"175","1","Local Product Branding Campaigns","Initiate branding campaigns for local vending markets, exhibition venues and locally produced goods, services and products.",""],[1,"175","2","Small and Medium Enterprise Development Partnership","Develop small and medium enterprizes in partnership with the private and non-governmental sectors to build the base of the provincial and local economy.",""],[1,"175","2","Local Worker Skills Mapping and Identification Card System","In order to create an environment for internal and external investment in areas of comparative advantage, each local level is required to do skill mapping of the workers and issue identification cards.",""],[1,"175","2","Inter-Provincial and Local Employment Coordination","Coordinate with other provinces and local levels for employment opportunities if such opportunities cannot be created locally.",""],[1,"175","2","Local Tax Reform Linked to Service Delivery","Apply local taxes according to the principle of ability to pay and connect them to service delivery system.",""],[1,"175","2","Tourism Diversification and Service Quality Improvement","Promote tourism in education, health, sports, adventure, natural, religious, spiritual and cultural fields, and provide quality tourism services which have forward and backward linkages.",""],[1,"175","2","Tourism Destination and Product Diversification","Diversify tourism destinations and products.",""],[1,"175","2","Local Goods Production and Consumption Campaign","Transform the consumption-oriented economy into a production-oriented economy by conducting a special campaign to increase the production and use of local goods.",""],[1,"175","2","Agricultural Modernization, Mechanization, and Commercialization","Promote food and nutrition security by increasing productivity through modernization, mechanization and commercialization of the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"175","2","High-Value Export Product Promotion","Increase production of high value and low volume products to promote exports.",""],[1,"177","3","Branding and Certification Support for High-Value Export Goods and Services","Make arrangements for branding and certification of high-value export goods and services in all seven provinces by protecting and promoting natural resources.",""]],"146":[[1,"158","2","Targeted Grants for Inclusive and Balanced Development","In conditional and non- conditional as well as other grants provided by the federal level to the provinces and local levels, put Madheshis, indigenous tribal communities, Dalits, women and marginalized communities in priority, and utilize these grants in social sectors.",""],[1,"176","2","Regional Balance and Equitable Development Grants","These provinces and local levels will be especially considered while sharing resources and transferring grants from the standpoint of provincial balance and equitable development.",""],[1,"176","2","Equitable Natural Resource Benefit-Sharing Provisions","On the basis of economic and social indicators and other specificities, make provisions for distribution and use of benefits accruing from natural resources in an equitable and fair manner.",""],[1,"176","2","Special and Complementary Grants for Infrastructure and Basic Services","Develop infrastructure and basic services through special and complementary grants.",""],[1,"176","2","Local Employment Generation Participation Initiative","Encourage participation of local levels in employment generation.",""]],"147":[[1,"159","3","Gender Mainstreaming in Climate Change Policies and Investments","Ensure gender mainstreaming in policies, programs and investments related to climate change to reduce the impact of climate change on the overall human life as well as the negative impact on women's workload, productivity, health and livelihood.",""],[1,"161","1","Disability Service Continuity Disaster Action Plan","Develop and implement an action plan for service continuity in the event of disaster, targeting persons with high risks, such as persons with disabilities, children, the disabled, the helpless, the poor, etc.",""],[1,"173","5","Multi-Stakeholder Collaboration for Climate Adaptation and Social Inclusion","Collaborate with intergovernmental and non-governmental sectors for climate change adaptation, protection of human rights, end of absolute poverty and for ensuring social inclusion.",""],[1,"177","3","Climate-Resilient Community Feasibility Study","Make feasibility study of high mountainous and Himalayan regions to build climate resilient communities who can contribute to adoption of climate resilient production system.",""]],"148":[[1,"178","4","Provincial Potential Mapping and Promotion Initiative","Explore and conduct research on the best potential of the seven provinces.",""],[1,"178","4","Provincial Productivity and Comparative Advantage Mapping","Identify and map areas of high productivity and comparative advantage.",""],[1,"178","4","Provincial Skills and Resource Promotion Initiative","Emphasize the use and promotion of provincial specificities, capabilities, skills, tools and resources.",""],[1,"178","4","Provincial Knowledge Exchange and Linkage Development","Ensure exchange of exemplary, successful and illustrative works of the province and local level, transfer resources and develop forward and backward linkages.",""],[1,"178","4","Local Specialty Production and Traditional Skills Promotion","Facilitate the production of local specialties, preserve and promote traditional skills.",""],[1,"178","4","Labor-Intensive Project Development","Design and implement labor intensive projects.",""],[1,"178","4","Cooperative Investment Promotion in Productive Sectors","Promote investment of cooperatives in productive sectors.",""],[1,"178","4","Provincial and Local Revenue Reform Plan","Identify the revenue potential of the provincial and local levels, create an action plan for revenue reforms and prioritize the mobilization of internal resources.",""],[1,"178","4","Revenue Efficiency Reform Plan","Design and implement a revenue reform plan to increase utilization and collection efficiency of revenue potential in all three levels.",""],[1,"178","5","Special Investment Mobilization for Lagging Provinces and Local Levels","Balanced development program through special investment mobilization: Determine the listed base and standards of provinces and local levels that are falling behind from economic, social, administrative, geographic, environmental and humanitarian perspectives.",""],[1,"179","1","Provincial and Local Level Incentive Program","Conduct incentive programs for the upliftment and empowerment of the provinces and local levels.",""],[1,"179","1","Large Infrastructure and Service Delivery Partnership","Build large infrastructure and ensure service delivery in collaboration with the private sector.",""],[1,"179","2","Innovation and Entrepreneurship Economic Development Partnership Program","Economic development and partnership program based on innovation and entrepreneurship: Mobilize financial institutions for enerprise development based on local innovative technology and skills through measures such as partnership in start-up capital investment, arrangement for innovative finance and managing shortfall of finance.",""],[1,"179","2","Local Produce Marketing, Storage, and Value Chain Improvement","Improve and enhance marketing system, storage, processing and value chains for local produce.",""],[1,"179","2","Local Production and Tourism Infrastructure Integration","Promote local production by integrating local production system with tourism infrastructure.",""],[1,"179","2","Multi-Level Partnership for Regional and Local Projects","Develop partnership of federation, provincial and local levels in regional and local projects.",""],[1,"179","2","Public-Private Partnership and Co-Investment Promotion","Promote public-private partnership and co-investment.",""],[1,"179","2","Local Economic Development Service Delivery Simplification","Simplify service delivery, facilitate local economic development, promote good governance and build human and social capital.",""],[1,"179","2","Youth-Targeted Economic Development and Product Certification Programme","Promote youth targeted programs in economic development and certification and marketing of local products.",""],[1,"179","3","Economic-Social Transformation and Rural-Urban Integration Program","5) Economic-social transformation and rural-urban integration program: For balanced and equitable development of provinces and local levels, launch targeted small and medium enterprises development program on the basis of potential and specificity of the concerned province and local level.",""],[1,"179","3","Rural-Urban Connectivity and Service Linkage Development","Develop interlinkages in areas and activities like rural cooperative, development of modern vendor market, roads and communication infrastructure, financial access, partnership in resources use, and education, health and employment promotion.",""],[1,"179","3","Community Forestry and Climate-Resilient Organic Production Promotion","For improvement of living standard, take measures such as conservation and use of community forestry, climate resilient production system and organic farming and herbal products promotion.",""],[1,"179","3","Community-Based Economy Promotion","Develop and promote community-based economy and follow good practices.",""],[1,"179","4","Inter-Provincial and Inter-Local Network Development Program","6) Inter-provincial and inter-local level network development program: Emphasize on development and expansion of inter-provincial and local and inter-local networks that connect provincial economic centers for integrated development of provincial and local economies.",""],[1,"180","2","Integrated Local Economic Development Program","Integrated local economic development program: Identify potential for economic development at the provincial and local levels.",""]],"149":[[1,"188","3","Special Concessions for Access to Technical and Vocational Education","Establish easy access to technical and vocational education by arranging special concessions for poor and underprivileged citizens.",""],[1,"188","3","Coordinated Human Capital Development Programme","Conduct coordinated programs with the government, private sector, cooperatives and development partners in building healthy, educated and skilled citizens by increasing the quality and accessibility of education and health.",""],[1,"188","3","Education-to-Employment Linkage Programme","Develop and implement programs that links education to skills, skills to employment, employment to production and production to markets.",""]],"150":[[1,"208","6","Comprehensive Human Security Policy and Programmatic Arrangements","Make policy and programmatic arrangements to ensure comprehensive human security by managing new security challenges.",""],[1,"208","6","Organized Crime Control Measures","Control all forms of organized crimes.",""],[1,"209","1","Social Harmony and National Unity Promotion Measures","Given high priority in matters related to national concerns, maintain solidarity among various ethnic groups, religions, languages, cultures and sects based on harmony and tolerance.",""],[1,"209","1","Cultural Respect and Unity in Diversity Initiative","Keeping in mind the concept of unity in diversity, develop an environment of respecting each others' culture.",""],[1,"209","1","National Security and Unity Protection Measures","Control activities that adversely effect the national security and national unity.",""],[1,"209","1","Conflict Analysis and Resolution Measures","Analyze various aspects of conflicts and adopt measures for their resolutions.",""],[1,"211","5","National Security and National Unity Strengthening Program","National security and national unity strengthening program: Make contemporary reforms in policy and organizational aspects related to national security and defence.",""],[1,"212","1","Curriculum Revision for National Unity","make timely modifications in the curriculum from school to university education.",""],[1,"215","4","Border Movement Documentation and Regulation System","Apply the same type of system for movement across Nepal-India and Nepal-China border areas.",""]],"151":[[1,"214","6","Human Rights Promotion Program","Human rights promotion program: Ensure institutional strengthening of the National Human Rights Commission.",""],[1,"214","6","Victim Relief, Reparation, and Compensation Mechanism","Provide relief, reparation and compensation to the victims on the recommendation of the Commission, enact and implement laws related to the implementation of all kinds of fundamental rights.",""]],"152":[[1,"225","2","Climate Change Awareness and Responsibility Campaign","Make individuals, communities and organizations aware of and responsible for the impacts created by climate change.",""],[1,"225","2","Local Natural Resources and Heritage Record-Keeping System","Each local level shall keep and update records of natural resources and heritages available within its area.",""],[1,"225","3","Climate Change Data and Evidence Collection System","Establish a climate change data and evidence collection, updating and verification system.",""],[1,"225","3","Evidence-Based Policy and Program Development","Make policies and programs evidence-based and empirical.",""],[1,"225","3","Research Investment and University Partnership Expansion","Increase investment and partnerships with universities and other institutions involved in research for conduting relevant study and research.",""],[1,"225","4","Environment and Climate Policy and Legal Reform","Review and revise the relevant laws from the point of view of environment and climate change.",""],[1,"225","4","Climate-Responsive Policy, Program, and Budget Integration","Integrate economic, social and infrastructure development policies, programs and budgets with national adaptation plans and nationally determined contributions in an environment- and climate-friendly manner.",""],[1,"225","4","Climate Adaptation Capacity Development","Develop the capacity of governments, private sector and communities to reduce the impact of climate change and increase adaptation.",""],[1,"225","4","Government-Development Partner Coordination Platform Activation","Activate the agreements and various platforms set up between the Government of Nepal and development partners.",""],[1,"228","2","Study, Research, and Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening Program","Program to strengthen study, research and monitoring and evaluation system: Increase investment in research on biodiversity, environment and climatic conditions trends and risks.",""],[1,"228","3","Climate Change Policy Mainstreaming and Institutional Capacity Development Program","Mainstream the Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation National Implementation Plans in all sectoral and governments level policies, plans and programs.",""]],"153":[[1,"231","1","LDC Graduation Transition Management Strategy","A strategy needs to be formulated and implemented for smooth management of the impact to be brought about by this situation.",""],[1,"232","5","LDC Graduation Smooth Transition Strategy","To address the impacts of Nepal's graduation into a developing country, 'LDC Graduation Smooth Transition Strategy, 2024' is being implemented, along with International Development Cooperation Policy, 2019 and Nepal Trade Integration Strategy, 2023.",""],[1,"235","3","Smooth Transition Strategy Implementation","Implement Smooth Transition Strategy, 2024, which carries necessary policy and institutional arrangements to address the impacts on trade, development assistance and technical assistance following graduation.",""],[1,"239","1","Advocacy for Special Arrangements for LDC-Graduated Countries","Take initiative and activism for special arrangements in favor of countries which have graduated from LDC status and for participation in other regional trade agreements.",""],[1,"239","5","Preparations for GSP+ Concessions","make necessary preparations for obtaining concessions under the Generalized System of Preferences plus (GSP+).",""]],"154":[[1,"233","3","Formulation and Implementation of Macro and Sectoral Policies","it is necessary to formulate and implement appropriate sectoral policies and adjust fiscal allocation and tax policies.",""],[1,"234","2","Domestic Resource Mobilization and Alternative Financing Reform","Nepal should increase mobilization of internal financial resources or identify alternative sources of financial assistance.",""],[1,"235","5","Federal Economic Policy Coordination and Fiscal-Monetary Harmonization","Maintain policy coordination and harmony among the three tiers of government through federal economic policy.",""],[1,"235","5","Fiscal and Monetary Policy Harmonization","Harmonize fiscal policy with monetary policy.",""],[1,"235","5","Public Debt and Productive Sector Finance Management","Improve the investment base by managing public debt and internal and external finance in the productive sector.",""],[1,"241","1","Revenue Base Expansion and Alternative Resource Mobilization","For economic development through sustainable, high and broad-based economic growth supported by growth in revenue, expand the sectors and bases of revenue.",""]],"155":[[1,"234","3","Export-Oriented Employment Creation Initiative","Create more employment opportunities through study, research and development of goods and services with export potential.",""],[1,"235","4","Entrepreneurship Development and Internal Employment Creation","Expand income-earning opportunities through entrepreneurship development and internal employment creation.",""],[1,"235","4","High-Income Foreign Employment and Remittance Strategy","Increase per capita national income by concentrating foreign employment in high-income countries and sectors, thereby increasing inflows of remittances.",""],[1,"235","4","Agricultural, Industrial, and Service Sector Productivity Improvement","Improve production and productivity of the agricultural, industrial and service sectors.",""],[1,"239","2","Production and Productivity Enhancement Program","Give priority to the program to increase production and productive capacity of the government and private sectors in the budgets of all the three levels of government.",""],[1,"239","2","Agricultural Modernization, Commercialization, and Diversification Program","Modernize, commercialize and diversify the agricultural sector.",""],[1,"239","2","Local Product Export Promotion Program","Conduct programs for identification, development and promotion of local products (goods) for export.",""],[1,"239","2","Supply-Side Constraint Reduction Measures","Address supply side constraints.",""],[1,"239","2","Farm Produce Quality, Storage, and Price Guarantee System","Develop a system of guaranteeing the quality, storage and price of farmers' produce through state intervention.",""],[1,"239","3","Market Access and Industrialization Promotion Program","6) Market Access and industrialization promotion program: Join the supply chain of auxiliary raw materials or auxiliary materials used in the manufacturing industry of the two huge neighboring economies.",""],[1,"239","4","Private Sector Promotion Program","7) Private sector promotion program: Mobilize mixed finance and co-financing by mobilizing the private sector in development projects in a bid to reducing initial investment risk.",""]],"156":[[1,"236","4","Information Technology Infrastructure and Human Resource Development Plans","Formulate information technology infrastructure and human resource development plans and implement them.",""],[1,"236","4","Concessional Support for IT Sector Investment","Address basic utility needs and investments in the IT sector through concessional rates or fiscal incentives.",""],[1,"236","4","Diaspora Engagement for the IT Sector","Attract the Nepali diaspora to this sector.",""],[1,"236","4","E-commerce Expansion Initiative","Expand electronic commerce.",""],[1,"236","5","Intellectual Property Rights Protection and Capacity Development","make legal arrangements for the protection of other intellectual property rights (geographical indications, genetic resources and traditional knowledge, traditional cutural expressions, trade secrets, integrated circuits) and develop capacity of related organizations for implementation.",""]],"157":[[1,"237","2","Social Inclusion and Integration Program Consolidation","Consolidate social inclusion and integration programs in line with National Integrated Framework, involving coordination and collaboration of the three levels of government.",""],[1,"239","2","Provincial and Local Government Collaboration Mechanism","Promote healthy, competitive collaboration between the provincial and local governments.",""]]}});